gin":"voidmatcha","providerType":"User"},"email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T21:59:25.489Z","repositoryId":1167628626,"sha":"f70a76e54ba7be7fcbd57e651bccd8f57755ad45"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"voidmatcha","providerType":"User"},"email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-08T08:19:08Z","committedDate":"2026-08-08T08:19:08Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"voidmatcha","providerType":"User"},"email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T21:59:25.489Z","repositoryId":1167628626,"sha":"a942beacc20788bc114029261050c04159861488"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"voidmatcha","providerType":"User"},"email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"authoredDate":"2026-08-08T08:19:08Z","committedDate":"2026-08-08T08:19:08Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"voidmatcha","providerType":"User"},"email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"observedAt":"2026-10-08T21:59:25.489Z","repositoryId":1167628626,"sha":"4207c27e3d48630c8647292969c27531031e0e43"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-08T21:59:25.489Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/16463a426fa98e64ae62bfb1d9e24052dc20bb71/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:42:05Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T09:42:05Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Count the holdout v7 run made on the shipped skills\n\nThe counted v7 run now measures what this release ships. It executed\nall three arms from a host shell against the release revision with a\nclean tree, 180 calls and zero infrastructure errors, with the trimmed\nbodies, the #3 swallowed-assertion fix, the conditional-rethrow triage\nrule and the lexer fix all in place.\n\nThe full arm passes every preregistered absolute threshold: stable\nprecision 1.000, stable recall 0.958, stable F1 0.979, P0 stable-label\nrecall 1.000, clean-case specificity 1.000, and no unstable P0 label.\nThe earlier counted run measured the pre-trim reviewer and failed P0\nrecall at 0.875; its miss is what exposed the #3 defect this release\nfixes.\n\nThe comparator still returns FAIL with no skill-lift claim, now for a\nsingle reason. Against no-skill all six lift checks pass. Against a\ncatalog-only control that lists the 24 patterns and nothing else, the\nstable F1 delta is +0.059 and clears its +0.05 bar for the first time,\nbut the paired-bootstrap 95% CI lower bound is -0.003 against a\nrequired +0.01, so the protocol refuses the claim. That is a failure,\nnot a partial success.\n\nThe #3 fix was designed after the earlier run missed pw-a06 in this\nsame public corpus, so pw-a06 is contaminated here and its recovery is\nnot evidence of generalization. The README says so where the P0 recall\nof 1.000 appears, not only in a footnote.\n\nFive runs are now one table: two that hung inside a Codex sandbox, one\nwhose in-checkout reports gave each arm a different dirty-tree digest,\nthe earlier counted run, and this one. Their artifacts stay under\nattempts/. Because the release history was squashed before this run,\nthe revisions the earlier reports record are no longer reachable on\nthis branch, which the table states plainly.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow; benchmark evidence and docs\nNot-tested: an uncontaminated rerun on a corpus the #3 fix never saw\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"466d46d1b2048e58b7c041ddcc6252f55f9d00e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/466d46d1b2048e58b7c041ddcc6252f55f9d00e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/16463a426fa98e64ae62bfb1d9e24052dc20bb71","verification":{"payload":"tree 466d46d1b2048e58b7c041ddcc6252f55f9d00e1\nparent 2ba34237cb0b67e9918cd28c177774c8e5ed0fc9\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789897325 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789897325 +0900\n\nCount the holdout v7 run made on the shipped skills\n\nThe counted v7 run now measures what this release ships. It executed\nall three arms from a host shell against the release revision with a\nclean tree, 180 calls and zero infrastructure errors, with the trimmed\nbodies, the #3 swallowed-assertion fix, the conditional-rethrow triage\nrule and the lexer fix all in place.\n\nThe full arm passes every preregistered absolute threshold: stable\nprecision 1.000, stable recall 0.958, stable F1 0.979, P0 stable-label\nrecall 1.000, clean-case specificity 1.000, and no unstable P0 label.\nThe earlier counted run measured the pre-trim reviewer and failed P0\nrecall at 0.875; its miss is what exposed the #3 defect this release\nfixes.\n\nThe comparator still returns FAIL with no skill-lift claim, now for a\nsingle reason. Against no-skill all six lift checks pass. Against a\ncatalog-only control that lists the 24 patterns and nothing else, the\nstable F1 delta is +0.059 and clears its +0.05 bar for the first time,\nbut the paired-bootstrap 95% CI lower bound is -0.003 against a\nrequired +0.01, so the protocol refuses the claim. That is a failure,\nnot a partial success.\n\nThe #3 fix was designed after the earlier run missed pw-a06 in this\nsame public corpus, so pw-a06 is contaminated here and its recovery is\nnot evidence of generalization. The README says so where the P0 recall\nof 1.000 appears, not only in a footnote.\n\nFive runs are now one table: two that hung inside a Codex sandbox, one\nwhose in-checkout reports gave each arm a different dirty-tree digest,\nthe earlier counted run, and this one. Their artifacts stay under\nattempts/. Because the release history was squashed before this run,\nthe revisions the earlier reports record are no longer reachable on\nthis branch, which the table states plainly.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow; benchmark evidence and docs\nNot-tested: an uncontaminated rerun on a corpus the #3 fix never saw\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEGEfMMDmSyDFRd5n6d6fzZx6Hg0UqqNrNC9ckEeJauhhSXqPXXYsdIOdUE0QVXr0i\nNa1SZz0znOWTDLUa85JAg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T11:37:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/16463a426fa98e64ae62bfb1d9e24052dc20bb71","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDE2NDYzYTQyNmZhOThlNjRhZTYyYmZiMWQ5ZTI0MDUyZGMyMGJiNzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/2ba34237cb0b67e9918cd28c177774c8e5ed0fc9","sha":"2ba34237cb0b67e9918cd28c177774c8e5ed0fc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/2ba34237cb0b67e9918cd28c177774c8e5ed0fc9"}],"sha":"16463a426fa98e64ae62bfb1d9e24052dc20bb71","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/16463a426fa98e64ae62bfb1d9e24052dc20bb71"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/2ba34237cb0b67e9918cd28c177774c8e5ed0fc9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T07:31:27Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T07:31:27Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Fold the follow-up work into 1.19.0 and settle the release reviews\n\n1.19.0 was never pushed and its tag was never public, so the trims, the\nholdout v7 result, the #3 fix, the lexer fix and the generator wording\nship as part of it rather than as a second release. The three manifests\nalready carried 1.19.0, so only the changelog and a few provenance\nsentences changed: the Unreleased section is merged in, and sentences\nthat named the old tag or branch now name revisions instead.\n\nTwo adversarial reviews of the release candidate, one on code and\nevidence and one on the user-facing documentation, returned twenty\nfindings. All are settled here.\n\nThe two that changed behavior were both in #3. A synchronous assertion\ninside a surrounding try/catch was excluded as if it were an attached\n.catch(), where the matcher throws before the catch can attach; only\nthe attached form is exempt now. And a catch was exempted whenever it\nheld any throw, so `if (!(e instanceof TimeoutError)) throw e`\nswallowed the assertion''s ordinary timeout and stayed invisible. The\nscanner now decides in three steps: propagation on every path is\nexempt, a negated identity test allowlisting a named application error\nis exempt, and anything else is a triage candidate, including a guard\nwhose named error is the framework''s own timeout or assertion failure.\nFour real repositories raise 0, 0, 1 and 1 candidates under the new\nrule, so it costs no noise.\n\nThe lexer''s JSX rule now requires matching tag names, so\n`parse<Result>(''throw error</p>'')` is not read as JSX text, and rethrow\ndetection matches a throw statement rather than the word anywhere, so\nJSX prose containing \"throw\" no longer fakes propagation.\n\nThree checks were proving less than they claimed: a generator contract\nsearched a concatenation instead of the approval table, the debugger\nV2-V6 parity searched whole files instead of each rule''s own bullet,\nand the reviewer evidence digest had gone stale.\n\nThe documentation findings were mostly the trim''s shadow: pointers that\nnamed a reference without its directory, an AGENTS layout and a\ngenerator sibling list from before the move, a CONTRIBUTING tier table\nthat would have let a behavioral change to a moved procedure pass as\ndocs-only, and a benchmark page still describing v5 as current. The\nREADME and its three translations now state the v7 outcome, including\nthe failed lift bar against catalog-only.\n\nConfidence: medium\nScope-risk: moderate; #3 scanner classification changed\nNot-tested: a live review on a repository with heavy conditional\n-rethrow usage\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"eeae1e4ac81af435e362c00c35571b7195ac4935","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/eeae1e4ac81af435e362c00c35571b7195ac4935"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/2ba34237cb0b67e9918cd28c177774c8e5ed0fc9","verification":{"payload":"tree eeae1e4ac81af435e362c00c35571b7195ac4935\nparent 7e07433e8f70270920b4e918c32f4fa5142eec9f\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789889487 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789889487 +0900\n\nFold the follow-up work into 1.19.0 and settle the release reviews\n\n1.19.0 was never pushed and its tag was never public, so the trims, the\nholdout v7 result, the #3 fix, the lexer fix and the generator wording\nship as part of it rather than as a second release. The three manifests\nalready carried 1.19.0, so only the changelog and a few provenance\nsentences changed: the Unreleased section is merged in, and sentences\nthat named the old tag or branch now name revisions instead.\n\nTwo adversarial reviews of the release candidate, one on code and\nevidence and one on the user-facing documentation, returned twenty\nfindings. All are settled here.\n\nThe two that changed behavior were both in #3. A synchronous assertion\ninside a surrounding try/catch was excluded as if it were an attached\n.catch(), where the matcher throws before the catch can attach; only\nthe attached form is exempt now. And a catch was exempted whenever it\nheld any throw, so `if (!(e instanceof TimeoutError)) throw e`\nswallowed the assertion''s ordinary timeout and stayed invisible. The\nscanner now decides in three steps: propagation on every path is\nexempt, a negated identity test allowlisting a named application error\nis exempt, and anything else is a triage candidate, including a guard\nwhose named error is the framework''s own timeout or assertion failure.\nFour real repositories raise 0, 0, 1 and 1 candidates under the new\nrule, so it costs no noise.\n\nThe lexer''s JSX rule now requires matching tag names, so\n`parse<Result>(''throw error</p>'')` is not read as JSX text, and rethrow\ndetection matches a throw statement rather than the word anywhere, so\nJSX prose containing \"throw\" no longer fakes propagation.\n\nThree checks were proving less than they claimed: a generator contract\nsearched a concatenation instead of the approval table, the debugger\nV2-V6 parity searched whole files instead of each rule''s own bullet,\nand the reviewer evidence digest had gone stale.\n\nThe documentation findings were mostly the trim''s shadow: pointers that\nnamed a reference without its directory, an AGENTS layout and a\ngenerator sibling list from before the move, a CONTRIBUTING tier table\nthat would have let a behavioral change to a moved procedure pass as\ndocs-only, and a benchmark page still describing v5 as current. The\nREADME and its three translations now state the v7 outcome, including\nthe failed lift bar against catalog-only.\n\nConfidence: medium\nScope-risk: moderate; #3 scanner classification changed\nNot-tested: a live review on a repository with heavy conditional\n-rethrow usage\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKmtzT5UnB/FePO+BerKpn5Z0uK5KgSBIr9J41KXavUkywri1dlUErNUw53Ay8+w3a\nPT80v+EvAuVzNkgaj4hQw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T11:37:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/2ba34237cb0b67e9918cd28c177774c8e5ed0fc9","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDJiYTM0MjM3Y2IwYjY3ZTk5MThjZDI4YzE3Nzc3NGM4ZTVlZDBmYzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/7e07433e8f70270920b4e918c32f4fa5142eec9f","sha":"7e07433e8f70270920b4e918c32f4fa5142eec9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/7e07433e8f70270920b4e918c32f4fa5142eec9f"}],"sha":"2ba34237cb0b67e9918cd28c177774c8e5ed0fc9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/2ba34237cb0b67e9918cd28c177774c8e5ed0fc9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/7e07433e8f70270920b4e918c32f4fa5142eec9f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T06:04:38Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T06:04:38Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Trim the debuggers and the generator, and fix the JSX lexer\n\nBoth debugger bodies and the generator body load on every run, so\neverything in them cost context whether or not the run needed it.\nFollowing the reviewer, their step procedure moves word for word behind\npointers that say when to read it. Each debugger gains four parallel\nreferences: report acquisition, bounded artifact extraction, the\nclassification procedure, and fix verification. The generator already\nhad sibling files, so its material joins them, with scenario-design.md\nadded for scenario and locator planning.\n\nEach body keeps what every run needs or could miss. The debuggers keep\ntheir triggers, safety gates, stop conditions, the complete F1-F15\ntables that back the classifier''s inline fallback and SP5 parity, the\nCANNOT_VERIFY boundary and the output contract. The generator keeps\nboth approval tables and the approval gate, the exploration safety\ngate, write ownership, the tracer and expansion gate, the reviewer\ndelegation with its inline fallback and the completion contract.\n\nSizes after: playwright-debugger 169 lines and about 4.6k tokens,\ncypress-debugger 178 and 5.2k, generator 247 and 5.4k, from 8.9k, 9.9k\nand 11.6k. Every line and sentence of each old body appears verbatim in\nthe file that now owns it, checked mechanically per skill. Contract\ntests, parity mutations, security pins, the scanner listing and the\neval and holdout prompt builders read each moved sentence from its new\nfile. Host ci-local found four consumers a sandbox run could not.\n\nThe shared lexer read the apostrophe in `<p>Don''t panic</p>` as the\nstart of a string and swallowed the rest of the line, leaving a real\ntry/catch unpaired, which 1.19.0 had recorded as a known limitation. A\nquote is now inert only between an opening tag and its matching closing\ntag on the same line, which keeps TypeScript generics and comparisons\nout of the rule, and the same handling reaches the relative-import\nlexers, which had kept their own copy. Quotes in multiline JSX text,\nfragments, or after a nested child still bound the lexer, so\npattern-reference keeps that narrower limitation.\n\nThree generator questions the wording still left open are settled: when\nan exploration observation is sufficient without another probe, that\nStep 5b runs once whether or not Step 4 required a tracer, and that\nreal writes are allowed only against a server the approved run starts\nand stops, since loopback is a location and not a lifecycle.\n\nConfidence: medium\nScope-risk: moderate; changes what three skills load up front\nNot-tested: live debugger and generator runs reading the references on\ndemand\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"5620c7413f2296a588d7d823958f798f1073c5ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/5620c7413f2296a588d7d823958f798f1073c5ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/7e07433e8f70270920b4e918c32f4fa5142eec9f","verification":{"payload":"tree 5620c7413f2296a588d7d823958f798f1073c5ed\nparent 12d4b0ef3ed7200b19979a8da8e1cae21c85fec6\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789884278 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789884278 +0900\n\nTrim the debuggers and the generator, and fix the JSX lexer\n\nBoth debugger bodies and the generator body load on every run, so\neverything in them cost context whether or not the run needed it.\nFollowing the reviewer, their step procedure moves word for word behind\npointers that say when to read it. Each debugger gains four parallel\nreferences: report acquisition, bounded artifact extraction, the\nclassification procedure, and fix verification. The generator already\nhad sibling files, so its material joins them, with scenario-design.md\nadded for scenario and locator planning.\n\nEach body keeps what every run needs or could miss. The debuggers keep\ntheir triggers, safety gates, stop conditions, the complete F1-F15\ntables that back the classifier''s inline fallback and SP5 parity, the\nCANNOT_VERIFY boundary and the output contract. The generator keeps\nboth approval tables and the approval gate, the exploration safety\ngate, write ownership, the tracer and expansion gate, the reviewer\ndelegation with its inline fallback and the completion contract.\n\nSizes after: playwright-debugger 169 lines and about 4.6k tokens,\ncypress-debugger 178 and 5.2k, generator 247 and 5.4k, from 8.9k, 9.9k\nand 11.6k. Every line and sentence of each old body appears verbatim in\nthe file that now owns it, checked mechanically per skill. Contract\ntests, parity mutations, security pins, the scanner listing and the\neval and holdout prompt builders read each moved sentence from its new\nfile. Host ci-local found four consumers a sandbox run could not.\n\nThe shared lexer read the apostrophe in `<p>Don''t panic</p>` as the\nstart of a string and swallowed the rest of the line, leaving a real\ntry/catch unpaired, which 1.19.0 had recorded as a known limitation. A\nquote is now inert only between an opening tag and its matching closing\ntag on the same line, which keeps TypeScript generics and comparisons\nout of the rule, and the same handling reaches the relative-import\nlexers, which had kept their own copy. Quotes in multiline JSX text,\nfragments, or after a nested child still bound the lexer, so\npattern-reference keeps that narrower limitation.\n\nThree generator questions the wording still left open are settled: when\nan exploration observation is sufficient without another probe, that\nStep 5b runs once whether or not Step 4 required a tracer, and that\nreal writes are allowed only against a server the approved run starts\nand stops, since loopback is a location and not a lifecycle.\n\nConfidence: medium\nScope-risk: moderate; changes what three skills load up front\nNot-tested: live debugger and generator runs reading the references on\ndemand\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOMlra6GgbbqvaxlItxK88LmzKrtp6aWu2wL+0KAmSGGAhtg8BqWCpPl10sMGOQY8z\nok0oHLGxS5DvO6KYYn1QM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T11:37:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/7e07433e8f70270920b4e918c32f4fa5142eec9f","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDdlMDc0MzNlOGY3MDI3MDkyMGI0ZTkxOGMzMmY0ZmE1MTQyZWVjOWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/12d4b0ef3ed7200b19979a8da8e1cae21c85fec6","sha":"12d4b0ef3ed7200b19979a8da8e1cae21c85fec6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/12d4b0ef3ed7200b19979a8da8e1cae21c85fec6"}],"sha":"7e07433e8f70270920b4e918c32f4fa5142eec9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/7e07433e8f70270920b4e918c32f4fa5142eec9f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/12d4b0ef3ed7200b19979a8da8e1cae21c85fec6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:26:52Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T04:26:52Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Trim the reviewer, run holdout v7, and fix what the run exposed\n\nThe reviewer SKILL.md was 434 lines and about 16.7k tokens, over three\ntimes the Agent Skills guidance of a body under 500 lines and about 5k\ntokens, and it loads on every review. Phase-specific procedure moves\nword for word into four references, each with a pointer that says when\nto read it: review-scope, scanner-workflow, semantic-review and\nreporting. The body keeps the exact scanner command and its trust gate,\nthe INCOMPLETE outcome, the zero-P0 floor, the every-review #20-#23\nobligation, the bounded sweep, Real P0 counting, the delegation\nfallback and all 24 Quick Reference rows. It is now 134 lines and about\n3.8k tokens, and every one of the old file''s 555 sentences appears\nverbatim in the body or a reference.\n\nThe counted v7 run then made 180 Codex gpt-5.6-sol calls across three\narms from a clean tree with zero infrastructure errors. The comparator\nreturned FAIL and no skill-lift claim: the skill passes all six lift\nchecks against no-skill, but against a catalog-only control that lists\nthe 24 patterns and nothing else the stable F1 delta falls far short of\nthe preregistered bar and recall is slightly lower. What the full body\nadds over the bare catalog is precision and clean-case specificity.\nThree earlier attempts are archived and disclosed, not dropped: two\nhung inside a Codex sandbox, where nested calls time out, and one wrote\nreports inside the checkout, so each arm recorded a different\ndirty-tree digest and the comparator refused to compare them.\n\nThe run also found a real defect. The #3 rule said never wrap\nassertions in try/catch, but its confirmation step asked whether an\n\"independent meaningful verification\" survived, so a later assertion on\na different element excused a swallowed one, and the reviewer missed\nthat case in every repetition. A real assertion swallowed by a\nnon-rethrowing catch is now P0 unless the identical check is\nre-asserted unswallowed, control flow fails the test regardless, or\ndocumented JUSTIFIED intent applies. Evals use a new fixture rather\nthan the holdout case, so the public corpus stays a measurement.\n\nAn uncounted addendum reruns the protocol after the trim and that fix.\nIts full arm clears every absolute threshold, one stable true positive\nis lost, and the run cannot isolate the trim''s effect; the case the fix\nwas written against is contaminated and disclosed as such.\n\nConfidence: medium\nScope-risk: moderate; changes what the reviewer loads and reports\nNot-tested: an uncontaminated rerun on a corpus the fix never saw\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"a7e881bebceebe483728e7769b169a48e8c530e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/a7e881bebceebe483728e7769b169a48e8c530e8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/12d4b0ef3ed7200b19979a8da8e1cae21c85fec6","verification":{"payload":"tree a7e881bebceebe483728e7769b169a48e8c530e8\nparent 39a71d336792cae14f11452b784979999be7c32e\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789878412 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789878412 +0900\n\nTrim the reviewer, run holdout v7, and fix what the run exposed\n\nThe reviewer SKILL.md was 434 lines and about 16.7k tokens, over three\ntimes the Agent Skills guidance of a body under 500 lines and about 5k\ntokens, and it loads on every review. Phase-specific procedure moves\nword for word into four references, each with a pointer that says when\nto read it: review-scope, scanner-workflow, semantic-review and\nreporting. The body keeps the exact scanner command and its trust gate,\nthe INCOMPLETE outcome, the zero-P0 floor, the every-review #20-#23\nobligation, the bounded sweep, Real P0 counting, the delegation\nfallback and all 24 Quick Reference rows. It is now 134 lines and about\n3.8k tokens, and every one of the old file''s 555 sentences appears\nverbatim in the body or a reference.\n\nThe counted v7 run then made 180 Codex gpt-5.6-sol calls across three\narms from a clean tree with zero infrastructure errors. The comparator\nreturned FAIL and no skill-lift claim: the skill passes all six lift\nchecks against no-skill, but against a catalog-only control that lists\nthe 24 patterns and nothing else the stable F1 delta falls far short of\nthe preregistered bar and recall is slightly lower. What the full body\nadds over the bare catalog is precision and clean-case specificity.\nThree earlier attempts are archived and disclosed, not dropped: two\nhung inside a Codex sandbox, where nested calls time out, and one wrote\nreports inside the checkout, so each arm recorded a different\ndirty-tree digest and the comparator refused to compare them.\n\nThe run also found a real defect. The #3 rule said never wrap\nassertions in try/catch, but its confirmation step asked whether an\n\"independent meaningful verification\" survived, so a later assertion on\na different element excused a swallowed one, and the reviewer missed\nthat case in every repetition. A real assertion swallowed by a\nnon-rethrowing catch is now P0 unless the identical check is\nre-asserted unswallowed, control flow fails the test regardless, or\ndocumented JUSTIFIED intent applies. Evals use a new fixture rather\nthan the holdout case, so the public corpus stays a measurement.\n\nAn uncounted addendum reruns the protocol after the trim and that fix.\nIts full arm clears every absolute threshold, one stable true positive\nis lost, and the run cannot isolate the trim''s effect; the case the fix\nwas written against is contaminated and disclosed as such.\n\nConfidence: medium\nScope-risk: moderate; changes what the reviewer loads and reports\nNot-tested: an uncontaminated rerun on a corpus the fix never saw\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQC1BdIWn7TYKhVah+dgrS2AgaNhIJbfkokK+5GYkTYkrZVH3a4NB8l8HGw1qLXP70J\nNSBLzgHDHEMuFMh3vdngw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T11:37:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/12d4b0ef3ed7200b19979a8da8e1cae21c85fec6","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDEyZDRiMGVmM2VkNzIwMGIxOTk3OWE4ZGE4ZTFjYWUyMWM4NWZlYzY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/39a71d336792cae14f11452b784979999be7c32e","sha":"39a71d336792cae14f11452b784979999be7c32e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/39a71d336792cae14f11452b784979999be7c32e"}],"sha":"12d4b0ef3ed7200b19979a8da8e1cae21c85fec6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/12d4b0ef3ed7200b19979a8da8e1cae21c85fec6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/39a71d336792cae14f11452b784979999be7c32e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T02:47:19Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T02:47:19Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Freeze reviewer holdout v7 and bump the bundle to 1.19.0\n\nReviewer holdout v7 is a Codex-only rerun protocol for the unchanged v5\npublic-development corpus. The 2026-09-19 v5 run could not reach a\nverdict: the runner starts Claude with --permission-mode plan, and\nFable followed the plan-file instruction in 8-10% of calls, breaking\nthe single-JSON output contract. V7 narrows the matrix to the v5 Codex\ncell and changes execution tooling and host scope, not cases, labels,\nscoring, stability, schedule seed, repetitions or thresholds. It\ndeclares a minimum CLI floor rather than an exact pin, because v5 and\nv6 both stopped being runnable from an ordinary checkout once the\ninstaller rotated their pinned build away.\n\nA follow-up post-implementation review and a sixth live generator run\nare settled in the same batch. The #14 filter had lost a credential\nwhose evidence was a string selector at the head of a multi-line chain,\na recall regression against 1.18.0, so those lines are re-read with\ninert string tokens kept; the credential tokens no longer match author\nor tokenizer. Step 5b runs only when the final set''s verdicts allow\nComplete, a V2 gate that also proves a secondary outcome counts as that\noutcome, \"persistent write\" means an effect that outlives the run, and\ntracer carry-over names what always reruns on the final set.\npattern-reference records that an odd quote in JSX text can still\nunbalance the shared lexer, with the lexer change left to a later\ncommit.\n\nAll four skills and the three plugin manifests move to 1.19.0.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow; a frozen protocol, wording, and the version bump\nNot-tested: the v7 run itself, which follows in this release\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"e38bad027f28ae06f7f9a25ae1c701dca5c19a8e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/e38bad027f28ae06f7f9a25ae1c701dca5c19a8e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/39a71d336792cae14f11452b784979999be7c32e","verification":{"payload":"tree e38bad027f28ae06f7f9a25ae1c701dca5c19a8e\nparent 495be5aab8323e8b265f8c5a125cf27ec4bec519\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789872439 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789872439 +0900\n\nFreeze reviewer holdout v7 and bump the bundle to 1.19.0\n\nReviewer holdout v7 is a Codex-only rerun protocol for the unchanged v5\npublic-development corpus. The 2026-09-19 v5 run could not reach a\nverdict: the runner starts Claude with --permission-mode plan, and\nFable followed the plan-file instruction in 8-10% of calls, breaking\nthe single-JSON output contract. V7 narrows the matrix to the v5 Codex\ncell and changes execution tooling and host scope, not cases, labels,\nscoring, stability, schedule seed, repetitions or thresholds. It\ndeclares a minimum CLI floor rather than an exact pin, because v5 and\nv6 both stopped being runnable from an ordinary checkout once the\ninstaller rotated their pinned build away.\n\nA follow-up post-implementation review and a sixth live generator run\nare settled in the same batch. The #14 filter had lost a credential\nwhose evidence was a string selector at the head of a multi-line chain,\na recall regression against 1.18.0, so those lines are re-read with\ninert string tokens kept; the credential tokens no longer match author\nor tokenizer. Step 5b runs only when the final set''s verdicts allow\nComplete, a V2 gate that also proves a secondary outcome counts as that\noutcome, \"persistent write\" means an effect that outlives the run, and\ntracer carry-over names what always reruns on the final set.\npattern-reference records that an odd quote in JSX text can still\nunbalance the shared lexer, with the lexer change left to a later\ncommit.\n\nAll four skills and the three plugin manifests move to 1.19.0.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow; a frozen protocol, wording, and the version bump\nNot-tested: the v7 run itself, which follows in this release\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLN931FSA5EcdbNdrDLVIITdbdeIBLzPON46b4g7GjM13ipkVX9wv7cIySO9PjyVYe\nqwiFecPyJpT3TNUN2NXgw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T11:37:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/39a71d336792cae14f11452b784979999be7c32e","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDM5YTcxZDMzNjc5MmNhZTE0ZjExNDUyYjc4NDk3OTk5OWJlN2MzMmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/495be5aab8323e8b265f8c5a125cf27ec4bec519","sha":"495be5aab8323e8b265f8c5a125cf27ec4bec519","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/495be5aab8323e8b265f8c5a125cf27ec4bec519"}],"sha":"39a71d336792cae14f11452b784979999be7c32e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/39a71d336792cae14f11452b784979999be7c32e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/495be5aab8323e8b265f8c5a125cf27ec4bec519/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T01:38:05Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T01:38:05Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Pair try/catch on lexed source and require credential shape for #14\n\nThe #3 try/catch rule paired each catch with its try by counting braces\nin the raw file. A `}` inside a string or regex literal in a nested try\npaired the outer catch with the inner try, whose catch rethrows, and\nhid a swallowed readiness gate. The word `throw` in a comment also\ncounted: in a catch block it exempted the catch, and in a try body it\nqualified a sleep-only try as a gate. Pairing now reads\nsource_executable_code, the shared lexer in scope-source.sh, which\ndrops comments, string and template contents and regex literals while\nkeeping one output line per input line, so hit line numbers are\nunchanged.\n\nThe #14 scanner filter returned a candidate for any .fill() or .type()\nwith a string literal, so fill(''''), a todo title, and even\n`message.type() === \"error\"` reached Phase 2 as hardcoded credentials.\nA form literal is now a candidate only when the lexed target line\npasses a non-empty literal as its first argument and the target line,\nits selector or variable, or its value carries a credential token. On\nthe seven-repository field scan this takes 94 candidates to 25, all in\none repository.\n\nThe generator''s gate, tracer and Step 5b questions are settled in the\nsame batch: when a weaker passing assertion on the primary element is a\nsettled-state gate, that V3 is CANNOT_VERIFY when the gate and the\nprimary render the same faulted data and the gate is never weakened to\nreach the primary, what a tracer''s Complete means and what carries over\nto the final set, and that Step 5b runs after Step 7 records the final\nset''s verdicts.\n\nConfidence: medium\nScope-risk: moderate; changes what two scanner rules raise\nNot-tested: a live review against the narrowed #14 filter\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"24bccfda0f05eb6d9beb20c5a6591453b6ea4713","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/24bccfda0f05eb6d9beb20c5a6591453b6ea4713"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/495be5aab8323e8b265f8c5a125cf27ec4bec519","verification":{"payload":"tree 24bccfda0f05eb6d9beb20c5a6591453b6ea4713\nparent 5f68b809d952feeb57679c4a5437f520308cd3d7\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789868285 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789868285 +0900\n\nPair try/catch on lexed source and require credential shape for #14\n\nThe #3 try/catch rule paired each catch with its try by counting braces\nin the raw file. A `}` inside a string or regex literal in a nested try\npaired the outer catch with the inner try, whose catch rethrows, and\nhid a swallowed readiness gate. The word `throw` in a comment also\ncounted: in a catch block it exempted the catch, and in a try body it\nqualified a sleep-only try as a gate. Pairing now reads\nsource_executable_code, the shared lexer in scope-source.sh, which\ndrops comments, string and template contents and regex literals while\nkeeping one output line per input line, so hit line numbers are\nunchanged.\n\nThe #14 scanner filter returned a candidate for any .fill() or .type()\nwith a string literal, so fill(''''), a todo title, and even\n`message.type() === \"error\"` reached Phase 2 as hardcoded credentials.\nA form literal is now a candidate only when the lexed target line\npasses a non-empty literal as its first argument and the target line,\nits selector or variable, or its value carries a credential token. On\nthe seven-repository field scan this takes 94 candidates to 25, all in\none repository.\n\nThe generator''s gate, tracer and Step 5b questions are settled in the\nsame batch: when a weaker passing assertion on the primary element is a\nsettled-state gate, that V3 is CANNOT_VERIFY when the gate and the\nprimary render the same faulted data and the gate is never weakened to\nreach the primary, what a tracer''s Complete means and what carries over\nto the final set, and that Step 5b runs after Step 7 records the final\nset''s verdicts.\n\nConfidence: medium\nScope-risk: moderate; changes what two scanner rules raise\nNot-tested: a live review against the narrowed #14 filter\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKS1GHGyDx2931nUQelnIP1SCTrRLdGqnV2Lh705X+YbCq9Tp8VCqONQ4hFy9ZXREu\nbljshgQos6wOgsuBNCBwo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T11:37:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/495be5aab8323e8b265f8c5a125cf27ec4bec519","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDQ5NWJlNWFhYjgzMjNlOGIyNjVmOGM1YTEyNWNmMjdlYzRiZWM1MTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/5f68b809d952feeb57679c4a5437f520308cd3d7","sha":"5f68b809d952feeb57679c4a5437f520308cd3d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/5f68b809d952feeb57679c4a5437f520308cd3d7"}],"sha":"495be5aab8323e8b265f8c5a125cf27ec4bec519","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/495be5aab8323e8b265f8c5a125cf27ec4bec519"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/5f68b809d952feeb57679c4a5437f520308cd3d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:12:41Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T00:12:41Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Raise a swallowed gate as a #3 candidate; say what the generator runs\n\nA 2026-09-05 ablation found the reviewer caught the .catch(() => {})\nswallow 6 times in 6 but the try/catch form at most once in 6, although\nthe contract already forbade it: the difference was whether Phase 1\nraised a hit to adjudicate. A scanner rule was drafted then and shelved\nbecause its raw hits exceeded the per-rule cap on large repositories;\n1.16.0 moved the cap after the file-scope filter, removing the blocker.\nThe rule pairs each catch with its own try by brace balance and raises\nit as [P0?][LLM-TRIAGE] when the try body holds a web-first matcher, a\nreadiness or network wait, a poll, an expect, a Cypress\nwait/get/contains, a Page Object helper named for a check, or a throw,\nand the catch does not propagate. It never reaches the P0 exit gate.\n\nThe generator''s Step 4 table gains an Effect column. Every\ntarget-controlled command already needed exact approval, but the table\ngave the user nothing to judge a row by: a test:e2e whose config resets\na database looked the same as one that only runs tests. Rows are\nlabelled runs tests, starts server, persistent write, non-loopback\negress, installs, or unknown, and unknown is the default.\n\nStep 3''s mechanics move word for word out of SKILL.md into a new\nexploration-preflight.md: the preflight launcher''s internals, the frame\nwriter, the Playwright CLI guard recipe, the raw-ARIA fallback and the\nCLI-first rationale. Pasted TestRail/Zephyr/Xray/Qase handling moves to\nimported-test-cases.md, and the write-set definition and path ownership\nmove to verification-rules.md.\n\nA post-implementation review of those changes is settled here too: the\nEffect label''s evidence requirement, the write-set disclosure, and the\nplaces where a correct run could not tell what the contract required.\n\nConfidence: medium\nScope-risk: moderate; a new scanner candidate class\nNot-tested: a live generator run against the new table (RUNBOOK)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"b2134e0896daf043921e2b0c9a818462c4c8ff60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/b2134e0896daf043921e2b0c9a818462c4c8ff60"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/5f68b809d952feeb57679c4a5437f520308cd3d7","verification":{"payload":"tree b2134e0896daf043921e2b0c9a818462c4c8ff60\nparent 3b29fc987dee8cccd922aa1e3e29085a3a762f0d\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789863161 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789863161 +0900\n\nRaise a swallowed gate as a #3 candidate; say what the generator runs\n\nA 2026-09-05 ablation found the reviewer caught the .catch(() => {})\nswallow 6 times in 6 but the try/catch form at most once in 6, although\nthe contract already forbade it: the difference was whether Phase 1\nraised a hit to adjudicate. A scanner rule was drafted then and shelved\nbecause its raw hits exceeded the per-rule cap on large repositories;\n1.16.0 moved the cap after the file-scope filter, removing the blocker.\nThe rule pairs each catch with its own try by brace balance and raises\nit as [P0?][LLM-TRIAGE] when the try body holds a web-first matcher, a\nreadiness or network wait, a poll, an expect, a Cypress\nwait/get/contains, a Page Object helper named for a check, or a throw,\nand the catch does not propagate. It never reaches the P0 exit gate.\n\nThe generator''s Step 4 table gains an Effect column. Every\ntarget-controlled command already needed exact approval, but the table\ngave the user nothing to judge a row by: a test:e2e whose config resets\na database looked the same as one that only runs tests. Rows are\nlabelled runs tests, starts server, persistent write, non-loopback\negress, installs, or unknown, and unknown is the default.\n\nStep 3''s mechanics move word for word out of SKILL.md into a new\nexploration-preflight.md: the preflight launcher''s internals, the frame\nwriter, the Playwright CLI guard recipe, the raw-ARIA fallback and the\nCLI-first rationale. Pasted TestRail/Zephyr/Xray/Qase handling moves to\nimported-test-cases.md, and the write-set definition and path ownership\nmove to verification-rules.md.\n\nA post-implementation review of those changes is settled here too: the\nEffect label''s evidence requirement, the write-set disclosure, and the\nplaces where a correct run could not tell what the contract required.\n\nConfidence: medium\nScope-risk: moderate; a new scanner candidate class\nNot-tested: a live generator run against the new table (RUNBOOK)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQE8fPW+Hx428XV9dBq1iJy1UBhvEJbRjV0t9GCJIbbyzKzAQAswBhV5OAhzhoJMzf7\n+XhXOhRpS7EZBlt1yhWw0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-20T11:37:27Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/5f68b809d952feeb57679c4a5437f520308cd3d7","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDVmNjhiODA5ZDk1MmZlZWI1NzY3OWM0YTU0MzdmNTIwMzA4Y2QzZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/3b29fc987dee8cccd922aa1e3e29085a3a762f0d","sha":"3b29fc987dee8cccd922aa1e3e29085a3a762f0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/3b29fc987dee8cccd922aa1e3e29085a3a762f0d"}],"sha":"5f68b809d952feeb57679c4a5437f520308cd3d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/5f68b809d952feeb57679c4a5437f520308cd3d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/3b29fc987dee8cccd922aa1e3e29085a3a762f0d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T03:18:53Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T03:18:53Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Let the v11 carried-report mutation run on hosts other than macOS\n\nHosted CI failed on 5d6ae38 at test-independent-review-v11.py with\n\"pre-normalization report substituted\". The mutation rebuilds the report\nas it was before portable-path normalization by replacing this host''s\nportable home prefix with the real home. The carried report was\nrecorded on macOS, so it holds /Users/user/; on the Linux runner the\nprefix is /home/user/, which never occurs in it, the replacement did\nnothing, and the \"mutated\" payload kept the pinned digest.\n\nWhen this host''s prefix is absent, the mutation now substitutes the\nportable prefix the report actually records, and fails if it records\nnone. The check still proves that a pre-normalization report is\nrejected.\n\nThe suite was added in 1.17.0 and never reached this step on Linux\nbefore: hosted CI stopped earlier on the /usr/bin/sg scanner defect\nthat 1.18.0 fixed. No skill file changes, so this is not a release.\n\nReproduced on macOS with a non-/Users HOME, then run as a non-root\nuser with HOME=/home/runner in the pinned amd64 Ubuntu image: 25\nchecks pass, 1 skipped (needs the pinned live CLI binary).\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; one CI test''s mutation input\nNot-tested: later hosted-CI stages that have never run on Linux\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"240c698db2992c06ceb5bb82e851bae7e7955a38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/240c698db2992c06ceb5bb82e851bae7e7955a38"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/3b29fc987dee8cccd922aa1e3e29085a3a762f0d","verification":{"payload":"tree 240c698db2992c06ceb5bb82e851bae7e7955a38\nparent 5d6ae3804fdab72b4dec6909ca15fed04f8716b5\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789787933 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789787933 +0900\n\nLet the v11 carried-report mutation run on hosts other than macOS\n\nHosted CI failed on 5d6ae38 at test-independent-review-v11.py with\n\"pre-normalization report substituted\". The mutation rebuilds the report\nas it was before portable-path normalization by replacing this host''s\nportable home prefix with the real home. The carried report was\nrecorded on macOS, so it holds /Users/user/; on the Linux runner the\nprefix is /home/user/, which never occurs in it, the replacement did\nnothing, and the \"mutated\" payload kept the pinned digest.\n\nWhen this host''s prefix is absent, the mutation now substitutes the\nportable prefix the report actually records, and fails if it records\nnone. The check still proves that a pre-normalization report is\nrejected.\n\nThe suite was added in 1.17.0 and never reached this step on Linux\nbefore: hosted CI stopped earlier on the /usr/bin/sg scanner defect\nthat 1.18.0 fixed. No skill file changes, so this is not a release.\n\nReproduced on macOS with a non-/Users HOME, then run as a non-root\nuser with HOME=/home/runner in the pinned amd64 Ubuntu image: 25\nchecks pass, 1 skipped (needs the pinned live CLI binary).\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; one CI test''s mutation input\nNot-tested: later hosted-CI stages that have never run on Linux\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMvw5nIVbUjgKxQ7ncfAmo20vQz4De/+TT4DhZ/UkeAzI4sxv9qHhG8DJCRElpIQ76\nFQBSZIWHtxXq2sZYSlNAw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T03:20:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/3b29fc987dee8cccd922aa1e3e29085a3a762f0d","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDNiMjlmYzk4N2RlZThjY2NkOTIyYWExZTNlMjkwODVhM2E3NjJmMGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/5d6ae3804fdab72b4dec6909ca15fed04f8716b5","sha":"5d6ae3804fdab72b4dec6909ca15fed04f8716b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/5d6ae3804fdab72b4dec6909ca15fed04f8716b5"}],"sha":"3b29fc987dee8cccd922aa1e3e29085a3a762f0d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/3b29fc987dee8cccd922aa1e3e29085a3a762f0d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/5d6ae3804fdab72b4dec6909ca15fed04f8716b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T00:05:14Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T00:05:14Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Release v1.18.0\n\nBumps all four SKILL.md files and all three plugin manifests to 1.18.0\nand cuts the changelog section for the nine commits since 1.17.0 plus\nthe HOL scanner suppression already on main.\n\nThe release note leads with the scanner fix because it changes results\nfor existing users: every release from 1.11.0 through 1.17.0 ran Linux\n/usr/bin/sg as ast-grep on Debian and Ubuntu hosts without ast-grep, and\neach scan there ended INCOMPLETE with exit 2.\n\nThe last two commits were first planned as 1.19.0. With 1.18.0 not yet\npublished, they ship here instead, so existing installs take one update\nrather than two a day apart.\n\nEach batch went through a pre-implementation plan review and a\npost-implementation review, and the generator changes through three live\nruns against a local todo app.\nThe reviewer evidence status records the new skill digest, written by\nscripts/dev/refresh-reviewer-evidence-digest.py.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; version metadata, changelog, and one recorded digest\nNot-tested: hosted CI, pending push\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"75f804cce0dde3ccb6cf2c5e6bc2d64089ab8589","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/75f804cce0dde3ccb6cf2c5e6bc2d64089ab8589"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/5d6ae3804fdab72b4dec6909ca15fed04f8716b5","verification":{"payload":"tree 75f804cce0dde3ccb6cf2c5e6bc2d64089ab8589\nparent 20cffa0cab47ea834bcce1bbb252e5039bb8769c\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789776314 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789776314 +0900\n\nRelease v1.18.0\n\nBumps all four SKILL.md files and all three plugin manifests to 1.18.0\nand cuts the changelog section for the nine commits since 1.17.0 plus\nthe HOL scanner suppression already on main.\n\nThe release note leads with the scanner fix because it changes results\nfor existing users: every release from 1.11.0 through 1.17.0 ran Linux\n/usr/bin/sg as ast-grep on Debian and Ubuntu hosts without ast-grep, and\neach scan there ended INCOMPLETE with exit 2.\n\nThe last two commits were first planned as 1.19.0. With 1.18.0 not yet\npublished, they ship here instead, so existing installs take one update\nrather than two a day apart.\n\nEach batch went through a pre-implementation plan review and a\npost-implementation review, and the generator changes through three live\nruns against a local todo app.\nThe reviewer evidence status records the new skill digest, written by\nscripts/dev/refresh-reviewer-evidence-digest.py.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; version metadata, changelog, and one recorded digest\nNot-tested: hosted CI, pending push\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n\n\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQGDt6zSv7XfVIPDMloKrbXNiJQV9ZArg5qT8czjYD7QuH7WBah+fBsxAtX0MMxKvEF\nyFVi6ecEL9RBKtGUXS4Q4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T02:40:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/5d6ae3804fdab72b4dec6909ca15fed04f8716b5","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDVkNmFlMzgwNGZkYWI3MmI0ZGVjNjkwOWNhMTVmZWQwNGY4NzE2YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/20cffa0cab47ea834bcce1bbb252e5039bb8769c","sha":"20cffa0cab47ea834bcce1bbb252e5039bb8769c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/20cffa0cab47ea834bcce1bbb252e5039bb8769c"}],"sha":"5d6ae3804fdab72b4dec6909ca15fed04f8716b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/5d6ae3804fdab72b4dec6909ca15fed04f8716b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/20cffa0cab47ea834bcce1bbb252e5039bb8769c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-19T00:02:37Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-19T00:02:37Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Tell readers what the generator and scanner now guarantee\n\nThe 1.18.0 changes a user would choose the bundle for were only in the\nchangelog. Three sentences, in all four README editions, put them where\nreaders look:\n\n- The generator lists every file it will write for approval, snapshots\n  git status and content hashes before exploring, checks what it wrote\n  against that snapshot, never reverts uncommitted work, and does not\n  report Complete after an unapproved write.\n- Playwright CLI exploration runs behind an origin allowlist, checked to\n  block an unapproved origin before the first navigation.\n- A full-root ever-gauzy scan, one of field scan v1''s two timeouts, went\n  from 5,932 to 1,226 seconds with byte-identical output. The sentence\n  says it was measured outside that ledger''s protocol, so it does not\n  read as a re-run of the frozen ledger.\n\nThe translations were written against the new README.md bytes and their\ncanonical-revision digests updated.\n\nTwo other pages had the same gap. benchmarks/STATUS.md now cites the\nreal-repository timings from the hot-path addenda (cal.com 212 s to\n192 s; ever-gauzy 5,932 s to 1,226 s, byte-identical output), and the\nAI-generated test review guide gains a pre-merge question for an absence\nasserted after a rejected write on a view the failure never refreshed.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; README prose in four editions and two docs pages\nNot-tested: native-speaker review of the ja and zh-cn sentences\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"34ebb44936b431cc9d35b8fb6d693e83c3d77fd7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/34ebb44936b431cc9d35b8fb6d693e83c3d77fd7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/20cffa0cab47ea834bcce1bbb252e5039bb8769c","verification":{"payload":"tree 34ebb44936b431cc9d35b8fb6d693e83c3d77fd7\nparent 2bfe9d59cc42b4de8b78ec789797988b1988f5c9\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789776157 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789776157 +0900\n\nTell readers what the generator and scanner now guarantee\n\nThe 1.18.0 changes a user would choose the bundle for were only in the\nchangelog. Three sentences, in all four README editions, put them where\nreaders look:\n\n- The generator lists every file it will write for approval, snapshots\n  git status and content hashes before exploring, checks what it wrote\n  against that snapshot, never reverts uncommitted work, and does not\n  report Complete after an unapproved write.\n- Playwright CLI exploration runs behind an origin allowlist, checked to\n  block an unapproved origin before the first navigation.\n- A full-root ever-gauzy scan, one of field scan v1''s two timeouts, went\n  from 5,932 to 1,226 seconds with byte-identical output. The sentence\n  says it was measured outside that ledger''s protocol, so it does not\n  read as a re-run of the frozen ledger.\n\nThe translations were written against the new README.md bytes and their\ncanonical-revision digests updated.\n\nTwo other pages had the same gap. benchmarks/STATUS.md now cites the\nreal-repository timings from the hot-path addenda (cal.com 212 s to\n192 s; ever-gauzy 5,932 s to 1,226 s, byte-identical output), and the\nAI-generated test review guide gains a pre-merge question for an absence\nasserted after a rejected write on a view the failure never refreshed.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; README prose in four editions and two docs pages\nNot-tested: native-speaker review of the ja and zh-cn sentences\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQG3e/OhmKMXvh2uhIFAEx8cOuEC90I1tYyMVUt4hHbRsmaAF5rMiqvDxF/GaU/CORQ\nSOjHnwGbwlJ3GzwXlqvgE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T02:40:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/20cffa0cab47ea834bcce1bbb252e5039bb8769c","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDIwY2ZmYTBjYWI0N2VhODM0YmNjZTFiYmIyNTJlNTAzOWJiODc2OWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/2bfe9d59cc42b4de8b78ec789797988b1988f5c9","sha":"2bfe9d59cc42b4de8b78ec789797988b1988f5c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/2bfe9d59cc42b4de8b78ec789797988b1988f5c9"}],"sha":"20cffa0cab47ea834bcce1bbb252e5039bb8769c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/20cffa0cab47ea834bcce1bbb252e5039bb8769c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/2bfe9d59cc42b4de8b78ec789797988b1988f5c9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:34:43Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T20:34:43Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Let correct generator runs reach Complete; settle live-run ambiguities\n\nThree live generator runs against the runbook fixture kept stopping at\nthe same places. A pre-implementation review sorted the reported\nambiguities into do-now, defer, and reject; this commit does the do-now\nset and the gaps the third run found in it.\n\nThree rules made a correct run unable to reach Complete:\n- V2-V4 probes needed temporary spec copies whose names an exact-command\n  approval could not cover. A targeted runner row may now carry one\n  <spec> slot covering only the candidate and its temporary verifier\n  copies, in the test directory or the project-accepted scratch\n  directory, and that targeted command may run again within the task.\n- A serial project (workers: 1, a serial describe, or a serial setting\n  the approved plan added) could never pass V5''s parallel mode, and\n  CANNOT_VERIFY there forced PARTIAL/BLOCKED. That mode is now N/A;\n  V5 is CANNOT_VERIFY only when solo, repeat, or suite-context cannot run.\n- A V6 verdict that reached the writer only through another agent had no\n  recording rule. It counts when its verdict line is quoted verbatim with\n  the reviewer''s identifier; a paraphrase is CANNOT_VERIFY.\n\nSmaller clarifications, one clause each: a request that names its target\nskips Step 2; driving a local disposable stack through its own UI during\nexploration is allowed; Right layer may record NO_LOWER_LAYER; an exact\nuser scenario list gets no additions, with gaps named at the gate;\nsecondary outcomes follow the primary, except an assertion that doubles\nas the V2 gate, which stays before it; a sibling element from the same\nrender counts as a V2 gate; V3 faults must leave the declared gate\npassing; a transient-by-design outcome skips the reload check; the\nCLAUDE.md row, and the conventions template''s pointer, follow whether a\nroot CLAUDE.md or .claude/ exists; the init-agents probe is listed only\nwith an agent directory or a request; Step 5b runs once after the final\nset in a tracer flow; afterEach may revert the test''s own writes; a\ntemporary copy may keep only the scenario under test; an earlier\nwebServer.command approval counts, but the server still starts only after\nthe failed probe; the baseline runs before any approved config edit; and\nthe report reads \"N P0 found, N fixed\".\n\nRejected as already covered: a stale installed reviewer copy (SKILL.md''s\ninline fallback) and V6 advisories (the material-delta rule). Deferred:\nthe playwright-cli update check, pending its opt-out variable.\n\nA post-implementation review found the V5 paragraph still told the\nagent to report a mode the repository cannot express as CANNOT_VERIFY,\ncontradicting the new N/A clause; a parallel mode the repository cannot\nexpress is now N/A too. It also found the conventions template clause\nunpinned, the rerun permission unscoped, and eval 33 relying on repeat\nand full-suite runs its approved table did not list; all are fixed.\n\nEvery clause has a contract assertion that failed before the edit, with\nmutation guards for the three blockers, the secondary order, the probe\nlisting, and the V3 gate rule. Generator eval 33 covers the blockers\ntogether. SKILL.md grows by about 250 words, to 7,659.\n\nThe third live run, with no command pre-approved, reached Complete: ten\nprobe runs under the <spec> slot with no new approval, V5 parallel N/A,\nboth V6 verdicts quoted with reviewer identifiers, the user''s files\nuntouched, and the write set exactly the approved rows.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate; changes generator approval, verification, and completion text\nNot-tested: hosts other than Claude Code for the live runs\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"ce52aebcbc4c53761c48d50e27e40466d7063ea2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/ce52aebcbc4c53761c48d50e27e40466d7063ea2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/2bfe9d59cc42b4de8b78ec789797988b1988f5c9","verification":{"payload":"tree ce52aebcbc4c53761c48d50e27e40466d7063ea2\nparent 8dbd5c2912419fddcff819c1a8467a3dc5750ed0\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789763683 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789763683 +0900\n\nLet correct generator runs reach Complete; settle live-run ambiguities\n\nThree live generator runs against the runbook fixture kept stopping at\nthe same places. A pre-implementation review sorted the reported\nambiguities into do-now, defer, and reject; this commit does the do-now\nset and the gaps the third run found in it.\n\nThree rules made a correct run unable to reach Complete:\n- V2-V4 probes needed temporary spec copies whose names an exact-command\n  approval could not cover. A targeted runner row may now carry one\n  <spec> slot covering only the candidate and its temporary verifier\n  copies, in the test directory or the project-accepted scratch\n  directory, and that targeted command may run again within the task.\n- A serial project (workers: 1, a serial describe, or a serial setting\n  the approved plan added) could never pass V5''s parallel mode, and\n  CANNOT_VERIFY there forced PARTIAL/BLOCKED. That mode is now N/A;\n  V5 is CANNOT_VERIFY only when solo, repeat, or suite-context cannot run.\n- A V6 verdict that reached the writer only through another agent had no\n  recording rule. It counts when its verdict line is quoted verbatim with\n  the reviewer''s identifier; a paraphrase is CANNOT_VERIFY.\n\nSmaller clarifications, one clause each: a request that names its target\nskips Step 2; driving a local disposable stack through its own UI during\nexploration is allowed; Right layer may record NO_LOWER_LAYER; an exact\nuser scenario list gets no additions, with gaps named at the gate;\nsecondary outcomes follow the primary, except an assertion that doubles\nas the V2 gate, which stays before it; a sibling element from the same\nrender counts as a V2 gate; V3 faults must leave the declared gate\npassing; a transient-by-design outcome skips the reload check; the\nCLAUDE.md row, and the conventions template''s pointer, follow whether a\nroot CLAUDE.md or .claude/ exists; the init-agents probe is listed only\nwith an agent directory or a request; Step 5b runs once after the final\nset in a tracer flow; afterEach may revert the test''s own writes; a\ntemporary copy may keep only the scenario under test; an earlier\nwebServer.command approval counts, but the server still starts only after\nthe failed probe; the baseline runs before any approved config edit; and\nthe report reads \"N P0 found, N fixed\".\n\nRejected as already covered: a stale installed reviewer copy (SKILL.md''s\ninline fallback) and V6 advisories (the material-delta rule). Deferred:\nthe playwright-cli update check, pending its opt-out variable.\n\nA post-implementation review found the V5 paragraph still told the\nagent to report a mode the repository cannot express as CANNOT_VERIFY,\ncontradicting the new N/A clause; a parallel mode the repository cannot\nexpress is now N/A too. It also found the conventions template clause\nunpinned, the rerun permission unscoped, and eval 33 relying on repeat\nand full-suite runs its approved table did not list; all are fixed.\n\nEvery clause has a contract assertion that failed before the edit, with\nmutation guards for the three blockers, the secondary order, the probe\nlisting, and the V3 gate rule. Generator eval 33 covers the blockers\ntogether. SKILL.md grows by about 250 words, to 7,659.\n\nThe third live run, with no command pre-approved, reached Complete: ten\nprobe runs under the <spec> slot with no new approval, V5 parallel N/A,\nboth V6 verdicts quoted with reviewer identifiers, the user''s files\nuntouched, and the write set exactly the approved rows.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate; changes generator approval, verification, and completion text\nNot-tested: hosts other than Claude Code for the live runs\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n\n\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQEPnHktl5Rvi3cUalvgtQxTgxXaruU1Nu6Ft76axCd2tv652RIhv2g7ToD3oc4VwvH\nuufzKHHHyr/aNjZ0F6igg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T02:40:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/2bfe9d59cc42b4de8b78ec789797988b1988f5c9","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDJiZmU5ZDU5Y2M0MmI0ZGU4Yjc4ZWM3ODk3OTc5ODhiMTk4OGY1Yzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/8dbd5c2912419fddcff819c1a8467a3dc5750ed0","sha":"8dbd5c2912419fddcff819c1a8467a3dc5750ed0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/8dbd5c2912419fddcff819c1a8467a3dc5750ed0"}],"sha":"2bfe9d59cc42b4de8b78ec789797988b1988f5c9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/2bfe9d59cc42b4de8b78ec789797988b1988f5c9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/8dbd5c2912419fddcff819c1a8467a3dc5750ed0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T19:47:58Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T19:47:58Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Re-stamp what a scope query read instead of every recorded path\n\nA full scan of ever-gauzy took 5,932 seconds, and 4,683 of them were\nscope-worker.py re-validating every recorded dependency, about 240,000\npaths by the end, before and after each of its 5,568 operations. The\nqueries themselves took 123 seconds.\n\nThat per-operation global check came from the v1 per-process engine, which\nhad to re-trust a cache file written by another process on every call.\nThe persistent worker kept it for parity; no threat write-up or review\nasked for it, and a pre-implementation review found none.\n\nEach query now re-stamps the sources and resolution candidates it\ntraversed, so its answer matches the files it read, including a missing\ncandidate that has since appeared. A new non-terminal checkpoint\noperation validates the whole witness set, ancestor directories and\nmissing paths included, at the four tier checkpoints where the scanner\nalready re-checks its candidate manifest, and the terminal validate still\nruns before any Summary. ping only confirms the worker is alive.\n\nStamps carry ctime, which an unprivileged process cannot restore, so a\nfile modified and put back mid-scan still fails the next checkpoint.\nChanges that appear and vanish between operations were never caught\ndeterministically by the old check either; strict watch mode remains the\nguarantee for those, and its transient-change test still passes.\n\nTests written first: an in-process test counts full validations (ten\nacross three queries and two pings before, none after, one per\ncheckpoint) and another counts stats for one query against 3,000 extra\nwitnesses (6,072 before, under 300 after). Integration tests inject a\nchange before the second query for a cached barrel and for a missing\ncandidate, and the scan still exits 2 without a Summary. The ping test\nnow asserts that ping does not validate and checkpoint does, and the\nconditional-exclusion integration test requires a dependency created mid-\nscan to fail the scan at the next checkpoint, by the candidate manifest or\nthe witness check, naming the path, instead of at an excluded file''s ping.\n\never-gauzy now takes 1,226 seconds with byte-identical output; cal.com''s\napps/web/playwright is unchanged at 171 seconds.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate; changes when the scope worker validates its dependencies\nNot-tested: filesystems without real ctime (FAT/exFAT, some FUSE or network mounts), where a modify-and-restore evades the checkpoint as it also could before\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"686a954e7c58f603f58d1d7eee1c8901001b0128","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/686a954e7c58f603f58d1d7eee1c8901001b0128"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/8dbd5c2912419fddcff819c1a8467a3dc5750ed0","verification":{"payload":"tree 686a954e7c58f603f58d1d7eee1c8901001b0128\nparent c6f0496b827223d9f041172a9a94ed36d742a2e3\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789760878 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789760878 +0900\n\nRe-stamp what a scope query read instead of every recorded path\n\nA full scan of ever-gauzy took 5,932 seconds, and 4,683 of them were\nscope-worker.py re-validating every recorded dependency, about 240,000\npaths by the end, before and after each of its 5,568 operations. The\nqueries themselves took 123 seconds.\n\nThat per-operation global check came from the v1 per-process engine, which\nhad to re-trust a cache file written by another process on every call.\nThe persistent worker kept it for parity; no threat write-up or review\nasked for it, and a pre-implementation review found none.\n\nEach query now re-stamps the sources and resolution candidates it\ntraversed, so its answer matches the files it read, including a missing\ncandidate that has since appeared. A new non-terminal checkpoint\noperation validates the whole witness set, ancestor directories and\nmissing paths included, at the four tier checkpoints where the scanner\nalready re-checks its candidate manifest, and the terminal validate still\nruns before any Summary. ping only confirms the worker is alive.\n\nStamps carry ctime, which an unprivileged process cannot restore, so a\nfile modified and put back mid-scan still fails the next checkpoint.\nChanges that appear and vanish between operations were never caught\ndeterministically by the old check either; strict watch mode remains the\nguarantee for those, and its transient-change test still passes.\n\nTests written first: an in-process test counts full validations (ten\nacross three queries and two pings before, none after, one per\ncheckpoint) and another counts stats for one query against 3,000 extra\nwitnesses (6,072 before, under 300 after). Integration tests inject a\nchange before the second query for a cached barrel and for a missing\ncandidate, and the scan still exits 2 without a Summary. The ping test\nnow asserts that ping does not validate and checkpoint does, and the\nconditional-exclusion integration test requires a dependency created mid-\nscan to fail the scan at the next checkpoint, by the candidate manifest or\nthe witness check, naming the path, instead of at an excluded file''s ping.\n\never-gauzy now takes 1,226 seconds with byte-identical output; cal.com''s\napps/web/playwright is unchanged at 171 seconds.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate; changes when the scope worker validates its dependencies\nNot-tested: filesystems without real ctime (FAT/exFAT, some FUSE or network mounts), where a modify-and-restore evades the checkpoint as it also could before\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n\n\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQN8aMyYPOIRTL3Kq6hQ6VdAxf/GbBUtcIGEC6fgFVVKc1JoHBL8Z5UHbOYgv4aNu51\nvDYCVi2gSiJdghcjCO+QI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T02:40:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/8dbd5c2912419fddcff819c1a8467a3dc5750ed0","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDhkYmQ1YzI5MTI0MTlmZGRjZmY4MTljMWE4NDY3YTNkYzU3NTBlZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/c6f0496b827223d9f041172a9a94ed36d742a2e3","sha":"c6f0496b827223d9f041172a9a94ed36d742a2e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c6f0496b827223d9f041172a9a94ed36d742a2e3"}],"sha":"8dbd5c2912419fddcff819c1a8467a3dc5750ed0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/8dbd5c2912419fddcff819c1a8467a3dc5750ed0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c6f0496b827223d9f041172a9a94ed36d742a2e3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T18:10:42Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T18:10:42Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Pin the C locale so non-ASCII identifiers cannot abort a scan\n\nUnder a UTF-8 locale, macOS awk failed with \"towc: multibyte conversion\nfailure\" on non-ASCII identifiers such as Angular''s U+0275-prefixed\nexports (`import { ɵDomSanitizerImpl }`), and the whole scan exited 2.\nStrings, comments, regex literals, and template text were unaffected. A\nfull scan of ever-gauzy stopped after 24 seconds this way. v1.16.3 fails\nidentically; every scanner test pinned LC_ALL=C, which hid it.\n\nThe scanner now exports LANG=C LC_ALL=C LC_CTYPE=C before doing anything\nelse. Its lexers only track ASCII delimiters, which UTF-8 bytes of other\ncharacters never equal, so output bytes are unchanged: a source line with\nKorean, emoji, and a long comment printed identically under C.UTF-8 and C.\nThe other effects are improvements a pre-implementation review listed:\nsort runs in the C order CI already used, argument batching counts bytes,\nand BSD sed/tr/grep no longer fail on Latin-1 bytes. No other shipped\nscript runs awk on source text.\n\nA new test scans a project with non-ASCII identifiers under C.UTF-8 and\nen_US.UTF-8 and requires a complete scan with its #9 hit; it exited 2\nbefore the fix. With the fix, the ever-gauzy scan completed.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; one exported locale at scanner startup\nNot-tested: Linux hosts where en_US.UTF-8 is not generated (the test then runs under C and passes trivially; the pin makes the host locale irrelevant)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"1ecad5897bd273a381fb20e68e0f37a47e97c48e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/1ecad5897bd273a381fb20e68e0f37a47e97c48e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/c6f0496b827223d9f041172a9a94ed36d742a2e3","verification":{"payload":"tree 1ecad5897bd273a381fb20e68e0f37a47e97c48e\nparent f8bfe99506028901d8d06af06e1e3ffb4c21a119\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789755042 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789755042 +0900\n\nPin the C locale so non-ASCII identifiers cannot abort a scan\n\nUnder a UTF-8 locale, macOS awk failed with \"towc: multibyte conversion\nfailure\" on non-ASCII identifiers such as Angular''s U+0275-prefixed\nexports (`import { ɵDomSanitizerImpl }`), and the whole scan exited 2.\nStrings, comments, regex literals, and template text were unaffected. A\nfull scan of ever-gauzy stopped after 24 seconds this way. v1.16.3 fails\nidentically; every scanner test pinned LC_ALL=C, which hid it.\n\nThe scanner now exports LANG=C LC_ALL=C LC_CTYPE=C before doing anything\nelse. Its lexers only track ASCII delimiters, which UTF-8 bytes of other\ncharacters never equal, so output bytes are unchanged: a source line with\nKorean, emoji, and a long comment printed identically under C.UTF-8 and C.\nThe other effects are improvements a pre-implementation review listed:\nsort runs in the C order CI already used, argument batching counts bytes,\nand BSD sed/tr/grep no longer fail on Latin-1 bytes. No other shipped\nscript runs awk on source text.\n\nA new test scans a project with non-ASCII identifiers under C.UTF-8 and\nen_US.UTF-8 and requires a complete scan with its #9 hit; it exited 2\nbefore the fix. With the fix, the ever-gauzy scan completed.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; one exported locale at scanner startup\nNot-tested: Linux hosts where en_US.UTF-8 is not generated (the test then runs under C and passes trivially; the pin makes the host locale irrelevant)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n\n\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPjKnDJTS2bvmg8Rjy0i2uSAypNLXl7AU8fd+uhYFuZkSmTdWk+Wh56Gpb8aOGqRkA\n3z8zrt8yH6ZPNb4nao/Qg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T02:40:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/c6f0496b827223d9f041172a9a94ed36d742a2e3","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGM2ZjA0OTZiODI3MjIzZDlmMDQxMTcyYTlhOTRlZDM2ZDc0MmEyZTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f8bfe99506028901d8d06af06e1e3ffb4c21a119","sha":"f8bfe99506028901d8d06af06e1e3ffb4c21a119","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f8bfe99506028901d8d06af06e1e3ffb4c21a119"}],"sha":"c6f0496b827223d9f041172a9a94ed36d742a2e3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c6f0496b827223d9f041172a9a94ed36d742a2e3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f8bfe99506028901d8d06af06e1e3ffb4c21a119/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T17:58:51Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T17:58:51Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Record one real-repository timing for the scanner hot-path benchmark\n\nThe 1.17.0 hot-path benchmark measured a synthetic, hit-dense fixture and\nsaid in its Limits section that real repositories would not show its\n4.1x gain. This addendum measures one: cal.com''s apps/web/playwright at\ne91bb0c, one run per version on one machine, with the same pinned\nast-grep binary. v1.16.3 took 212 s and the current scanner 192 s, about\n10%. The repository root was refused by both versions'' symbolic-link\npreflight, as designed.\n\nThe outputs differ by one hit. The current scanner reports a #5a\ncandidate at embed-code-generator.e2e.ts:471 that v1.16.3 missed,\nbecause the regex literal /.*Cal\\.ns[^(]+\\(\"ui/ on line 410 contains a\ndouble quote that the older lexer took for the start of a string: the\n1.17.0 regex-literal fix, on real code.\n\never-gauzy was not measured. v1.16.3 was stopped after more than 64\nminutes, with about 52 of them spent as CPU time in scope-worker.py,\nwhich this benchmark did not change and 1.18.0 still ships; that is\nrecorded as an open question, not a result.\n\nConfidence: medium; single runs on one machine\nScope-risk: low; a benchmark README addendum and a changelog line\nNot-tested: repeated runs, other machines, the current scanner on ever-gauzy\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"a36d2400e75b328b2311015400af81b3e72d67ea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/a36d2400e75b328b2311015400af81b3e72d67ea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/f8bfe99506028901d8d06af06e1e3ffb4c21a119","verification":{"payload":"tree a36d2400e75b328b2311015400af81b3e72d67ea\nparent f2f64a0f7fbdbb72d599eea827bffe54c4b4da99\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789754331 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789754331 +0900\n\nRecord one real-repository timing for the scanner hot-path benchmark\n\nThe 1.17.0 hot-path benchmark measured a synthetic, hit-dense fixture and\nsaid in its Limits section that real repositories would not show its\n4.1x gain. This addendum measures one: cal.com''s apps/web/playwright at\ne91bb0c, one run per version on one machine, with the same pinned\nast-grep binary. v1.16.3 took 212 s and the current scanner 192 s, about\n10%. The repository root was refused by both versions'' symbolic-link\npreflight, as designed.\n\nThe outputs differ by one hit. The current scanner reports a #5a\ncandidate at embed-code-generator.e2e.ts:471 that v1.16.3 missed,\nbecause the regex literal /.*Cal\\.ns[^(]+\\(\"ui/ on line 410 contains a\ndouble quote that the older lexer took for the start of a string: the\n1.17.0 regex-literal fix, on real code.\n\never-gauzy was not measured. v1.16.3 was stopped after more than 64\nminutes, with about 52 of them spent as CPU time in scope-worker.py,\nwhich this benchmark did not change and 1.18.0 still ships; that is\nrecorded as an open question, not a result.\n\nConfidence: medium; single runs on one machine\nScope-risk: low; a benchmark README addendum and a changelog line\nNot-tested: repeated runs, other machines, the current scanner on ever-gauzy\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n\n\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQKgsNXGlVWxoVpUR14vkO2umTRf0gYTYqbJsdd9ZTehph2wwuEoQeOIcEHa5FoY5Bt\n4SJkD9wAj4wrfH3yBskQE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T02:40:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f8bfe99506028901d8d06af06e1e3ffb4c21a119","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGY4YmZlOTk1MDYwMjg5MDFkOGQwNmFmMDZlMWUzZmZiNGMyMWExMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f2f64a0f7fbdbb72d599eea827bffe54c4b4da99","sha":"f2f64a0f7fbdbb72d599eea827bffe54c4b4da99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f2f64a0f7fbdbb72d599eea827bffe54c4b4da99"}],"sha":"f8bfe99506028901d8d06af06e1e3ffb4c21a119","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f8bfe99506028901d8d06af06e1e3ffb4c21a119"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f2f64a0f7fbdbb72d599eea827bffe54c4b4da99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T17:36:20Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T17:36:20Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Add contributor verification tooling and define what a release is\n\nContributor-side changes only; no skill behavior changes here.\n\nci-local.sh runs on macOS, so Linux-only behavior reached users unseen:\nthe /usr/bin/sg defect fixed earlier in this release shipped in every\nrelease from 1.11.0 through 1.17.0 and surfaced only when hosted CI\nchanged how it installed ast-grep.\n\nscripts/dev/linux-script-check.sh copies a commit (git archive, which is\nwhat a push sends) into a digest-pinned Ubuntu image, initializes it as a\nGit worktree as a hosted checkout would, and runs the reviewer scanner and\nfour debugger script suites as a non-root user with umask 022. Root would\nmake the unreadable-file tests pass for the wrong reason; Ubuntu''s default\nuser umask of 002 makes test-created tool directories group-writable,\nwhich the debugger scripts correctly refuse. Against v1.17.0 it fails\nseven scanner checks; against the fix it passes all six suites.\n\nA failing or missing suite exits 1. The pre-push hook runs the check for\neach pushed commit whose range touches skills/*/scripts/ or their suites;\nexit 1 blocks the push, and a missing Docker daemon or an apt failure only\nwarns, so local gates stay dependency-free. The hook captures the changed\npath list instead of piping it into grep -q, which under pipefail could\nskip the check on SIGPIPE. E2E_SKILLS_SKIP_LINUX_CHECK=1 bypasses it.\nPushing a commit with one suite removed now exits 1; the first draft only\nwarned, which a pre-release review caught.\n\nA review of every fixed tool path the shipped scripts look up found no\nother name collision: sg was the only one. The debugger artifact readers''\nGNU/BSD stat fallback is now exercised on Linux by the same check.\n\nscripts/dev/refresh-reviewer-evidence-digest.py writes the current\ne2e-reviewer skill digest into the v3 evidence status, using the same\nfunction the check uses, then reruns the check; --check only reports. The\nmismatch message said expected= for the computed value and actual= for the\nrecorded one, which read backwards; it now says computed= and recorded=\nand names the helper.\n\nscripts/evals/generator-live/writescope-demo holds the small todo app the\nlive generator run used, with a runbook: copy it outside the repository,\ncommit a baseline, add two uncommitted user edits, give the fixed request,\nand check the starting snapshot, the Step 3 server approval, the CLI\nguard, the Step 4 tables, the empty-title re-read, the write set, and the\nfinal status. Its .gitignore lists only node_modules on purpose so\ntest-results shows up as runtime output to classify; the root .gitignore\nkeeps any accidental in-place run output out of this repository. It is\nnot part of CI because a run needs a model, a browser, and a user at the\napproval gates. CONTRIBUTING and AGENTS.md point to it for generator\nbehavior changes. A second live run followed the runbook from a fresh\ncopy with no command pre-approved and reached Complete.\n\nCONTRIBUTING gains a Releases section. skills update offers an\nupdate to existing installs when a skill folder''s content hash on main\n(or master) changes, regardless of version (vercel-labs/skills AGENTS.md \"Update\nChecking System\"), while Claude Code plugin installs update only when the\nplugin version changes (\"Pushing new commits without bumping it has no\neffect\", plugins-reference version management). Unbumped skill changes on\nmain therefore reach one install path and not the other, so a push to\nmain that changes skills/ is a release, bumps the version in the same\npush, and unfinished work stays on a branch.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; a new opt-out pre-push step, developer scripts, a runbook fixture, and documentation\nNot-tested: the hook path on a machine without Docker; the runbook on hosts other than Claude Code\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"b44555681ea878132abef5b39ee95f1de8190a65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/b44555681ea878132abef5b39ee95f1de8190a65"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/f2f64a0f7fbdbb72d599eea827bffe54c4b4da99","verification":{"payload":"tree b44555681ea878132abef5b39ee95f1de8190a65\nparent c7ce7bcd52940bc706fae4d059b43d19c46abeb5\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789752980 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789752980 +0900\n\nAdd contributor verification tooling and define what a release is\n\nContributor-side changes only; no skill behavior changes here.\n\nci-local.sh runs on macOS, so Linux-only behavior reached users unseen:\nthe /usr/bin/sg defect fixed earlier in this release shipped in every\nrelease from 1.11.0 through 1.17.0 and surfaced only when hosted CI\nchanged how it installed ast-grep.\n\nscripts/dev/linux-script-check.sh copies a commit (git archive, which is\nwhat a push sends) into a digest-pinned Ubuntu image, initializes it as a\nGit worktree as a hosted checkout would, and runs the reviewer scanner and\nfour debugger script suites as a non-root user with umask 022. Root would\nmake the unreadable-file tests pass for the wrong reason; Ubuntu''s default\nuser umask of 002 makes test-created tool directories group-writable,\nwhich the debugger scripts correctly refuse. Against v1.17.0 it fails\nseven scanner checks; against the fix it passes all six suites.\n\nA failing or missing suite exits 1. The pre-push hook runs the check for\neach pushed commit whose range touches skills/*/scripts/ or their suites;\nexit 1 blocks the push, and a missing Docker daemon or an apt failure only\nwarns, so local gates stay dependency-free. The hook captures the changed\npath list instead of piping it into grep -q, which under pipefail could\nskip the check on SIGPIPE. E2E_SKILLS_SKIP_LINUX_CHECK=1 bypasses it.\nPushing a commit with one suite removed now exits 1; the first draft only\nwarned, which a pre-release review caught.\n\nA review of every fixed tool path the shipped scripts look up found no\nother name collision: sg was the only one. The debugger artifact readers''\nGNU/BSD stat fallback is now exercised on Linux by the same check.\n\nscripts/dev/refresh-reviewer-evidence-digest.py writes the current\ne2e-reviewer skill digest into the v3 evidence status, using the same\nfunction the check uses, then reruns the check; --check only reports. The\nmismatch message said expected= for the computed value and actual= for the\nrecorded one, which read backwards; it now says computed= and recorded=\nand names the helper.\n\nscripts/evals/generator-live/writescope-demo holds the small todo app the\nlive generator run used, with a runbook: copy it outside the repository,\ncommit a baseline, add two uncommitted user edits, give the fixed request,\nand check the starting snapshot, the Step 3 server approval, the CLI\nguard, the Step 4 tables, the empty-title re-read, the write set, and the\nfinal status. Its .gitignore lists only node_modules on purpose so\ntest-results shows up as runtime output to classify; the root .gitignore\nkeeps any accidental in-place run output out of this repository. It is\nnot part of CI because a run needs a model, a browser, and a user at the\napproval gates. CONTRIBUTING and AGENTS.md point to it for generator\nbehavior changes. A second live run followed the runbook from a fresh\ncopy with no command pre-approved and reached Complete.\n\nCONTRIBUTING gains a Releases section. skills update offers an\nupdate to existing installs when a skill folder''s content hash on main\n(or master) changes, regardless of version (vercel-labs/skills AGENTS.md \"Update\nChecking System\"), while Claude Code plugin installs update only when the\nplugin version changes (\"Pushing new commits without bumping it has no\neffect\", plugins-reference version management). Unbumped skill changes on\nmain therefore reach one install path and not the other, so a push to\nmain that changes skills/ is a release, bumps the version in the same\npush, and unfinished work stays on a branch.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; a new opt-out pre-push step, developer scripts, a runbook fixture, and documentation\nNot-tested: the hook path on a machine without Docker; the runbook on hosts other than Claude Code\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n\n\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIrg4KoCnKcSRCCj2rDL5RNNTzjRFR04jugJfoZFBWmD9iz+LbIA6zOM7loBjs3TjA\nJ1aeqg0jS+2UU6rbq9SQY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T02:40:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f2f64a0f7fbdbb72d599eea827bffe54c4b4da99","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGYyZjY0YTBmN2ZiZGJiNzJkNTk5ZWVhODI3YmZmZTU0YzRiNGRhOTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/c7ce7bcd52940bc706fae4d059b43d19c46abeb5","sha":"c7ce7bcd52940bc706fae4d059b43d19c46abeb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c7ce7bcd52940bc706fae4d059b43d19c46abeb5"}],"sha":"f2f64a0f7fbdbb72d599eea827bffe54c4b4da99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f2f64a0f7fbdbb72d599eea827bffe54c4b4da99"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c7ce7bcd52940bc706fae4d059b43d19c46abeb5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T17:18:44Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T17:18:44Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Re-read state after a failed write; close verdict and CLI guard gaps\n\nA live generator run against a small todo app reached Complete but\nsurfaced four gaps; a pre-implementation review corrected the plan.\n\nA failed write''s \"nothing was stored\" was asserted too early. The run''s\nempty-title test asserted toHaveCount(0) right after a 400 on a page that\nnever re-fetched the list, so it would pass even if the server stored the\ntodo; two independent reviews flagged it. verification-rules V4 now\nrequires a reload or a waited re-fetch before asserting that a failed\nwrite stored nothing, and a failed-write probe must turn red at the\nunchanged primary assertion or a declared settled-state gate; red\nelsewhere is CANNOT_VERIFY, or ERROR when the verifier failed, and a\nscenario whose action is itself a rejected write needs no separate\ninjection. SKILL.md Step 4 and code-rules.md point to V4. The reviewer\ncopy of V4 carries the same clause, pinned by a new canonical clause in\ncheck-verification-parity.sh and a drift case in test-parity.sh.\n\nThe reviewer gets the matching Phase 2 note beside #4i: an absence after\na rejected write with no re-read in the spec is #4 [P1], judged from the\nspec alone, and a #4i empty-state SKIP does not clear it. No pattern ID,\nseverity, or scanner rule changes. Reviewer eval 41 uses a new fixture\nwith one true positive and two false-positive guards (a reload, and an\nawaited waitForResponse on the list GET).\n\nThe Playwright CLI had no working guard recipe. Its route command only\nfulfills requests and run-code runs in a bare vm context without URL,\nwhich is why the run''s first guard blocked everything. The recipe now uses\nnetwork.allowedOrigins with the exact origin, run from outside the\nworktree so a project-provided .playwright/cli.config.json is never\nloaded, in a fresh named session, because --config takes effect only when\nopen starts a session and a command sent to an already running session\nkeeps its settings. A fetch to 127.0.0.1:9 must fail with\nnet::ERR_BLOCKED_BY_CLIENT before navigation. Checked against\n@playwright/cli 0.1.19, including reopening one session name with a\nsecond config and sending a command with a different --config to a\nrunning session.\n\nStep 3 now asks for approval of webServer.command when it has to start\nthe app, stops it when exploration ends, and carries that approval into\nthe Step 4 table; the old sentence forbade reading the config''s webServer\nblock before a failed probe, although Step 1 already reads that config.\nThe loopback-fixture approval is requested before the first preflight,\nand only browser exploration tools run outside the worktree; the\npreflight launcher still runs from the target project.\n\nMixed per-scenario verdicts record the most restrictive status with a\nbreakdown, and the completion matrix gains rows for V1-V3: FAIL blocks,\nV1 without evidence is PARTIAL/BLOCKED, V2/V3 CANNOT_VERIFY is reported\nwithout blocking. Step 7 and the PARTIAL/BLOCKED template name V1 too,\nand files under Playwright''s output folders are runtime output, not\nverifier artifacts. The JSON result schema is unchanged.\n\nEvery new sentence has a contract assertion that failed before the edit.\nMutation guards reverse the verdict, re-read, ordering, approval, and\ncode-rules clauses, and five CLI-guard clauses a post-implementation\nreview showed were unpinned: probe before navigation, a loopback probe\nrather than an off-origin URL, the config outside the worktree, the\nabout:blank check, and closing the session. Generator evals 31 and 32\ncover the re-read rule and the CLI guard.\n\nA second live run, following the runbook with no command pre-approved,\nreached Complete with each of these rules observed.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate; changes generator verification and exploration text and adds a reviewer Phase 2 judgement\nNot-tested: hosts other than Claude Code for the live run\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"e060d6eb2128ca089adc1c2a6dfaffb3596ace63","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/e060d6eb2128ca089adc1c2a6dfaffb3596ace63"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/c7ce7bcd52940bc706fae4d059b43d19c46abeb5","verification":{"payload":"tree e060d6eb2128ca089adc1c2a6dfaffb3596ace63\nparent c48fe844f37f0631cd6751daf482ebf5550b767b\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789751924 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789751924 +0900\n\nRe-read state after a failed write; close verdict and CLI guard gaps\n\nA live generator run against a small todo app reached Complete but\nsurfaced four gaps; a pre-implementation review corrected the plan.\n\nA failed write''s \"nothing was stored\" was asserted too early. The run''s\nempty-title test asserted toHaveCount(0) right after a 400 on a page that\nnever re-fetched the list, so it would pass even if the server stored the\ntodo; two independent reviews flagged it. verification-rules V4 now\nrequires a reload or a waited re-fetch before asserting that a failed\nwrite stored nothing, and a failed-write probe must turn red at the\nunchanged primary assertion or a declared settled-state gate; red\nelsewhere is CANNOT_VERIFY, or ERROR when the verifier failed, and a\nscenario whose action is itself a rejected write needs no separate\ninjection. SKILL.md Step 4 and code-rules.md point to V4. The reviewer\ncopy of V4 carries the same clause, pinned by a new canonical clause in\ncheck-verification-parity.sh and a drift case in test-parity.sh.\n\nThe reviewer gets the matching Phase 2 note beside #4i: an absence after\na rejected write with no re-read in the spec is #4 [P1], judged from the\nspec alone, and a #4i empty-state SKIP does not clear it. No pattern ID,\nseverity, or scanner rule changes. Reviewer eval 41 uses a new fixture\nwith one true positive and two false-positive guards (a reload, and an\nawaited waitForResponse on the list GET).\n\nThe Playwright CLI had no working guard recipe. Its route command only\nfulfills requests and run-code runs in a bare vm context without URL,\nwhich is why the run''s first guard blocked everything. The recipe now uses\nnetwork.allowedOrigins with the exact origin, run from outside the\nworktree so a project-provided .playwright/cli.config.json is never\nloaded, in a fresh named session, because --config takes effect only when\nopen starts a session and a command sent to an already running session\nkeeps its settings. A fetch to 127.0.0.1:9 must fail with\nnet::ERR_BLOCKED_BY_CLIENT before navigation. Checked against\n@playwright/cli 0.1.19, including reopening one session name with a\nsecond config and sending a command with a different --config to a\nrunning session.\n\nStep 3 now asks for approval of webServer.command when it has to start\nthe app, stops it when exploration ends, and carries that approval into\nthe Step 4 table; the old sentence forbade reading the config''s webServer\nblock before a failed probe, although Step 1 already reads that config.\nThe loopback-fixture approval is requested before the first preflight,\nand only browser exploration tools run outside the worktree; the\npreflight launcher still runs from the target project.\n\nMixed per-scenario verdicts record the most restrictive status with a\nbreakdown, and the completion matrix gains rows for V1-V3: FAIL blocks,\nV1 without evidence is PARTIAL/BLOCKED, V2/V3 CANNOT_VERIFY is reported\nwithout blocking. Step 7 and the PARTIAL/BLOCKED template name V1 too,\nand files under Playwright''s output folders are runtime output, not\nverifier artifacts. The JSON result schema is unchanged.\n\nEvery new sentence has a contract assertion that failed before the edit.\nMutation guards reverse the verdict, re-read, ordering, approval, and\ncode-rules clauses, and five CLI-guard clauses a post-implementation\nreview showed were unpinned: probe before navigation, a loopback probe\nrather than an off-origin URL, the config outside the worktree, the\nabout:blank check, and closing the session. Generator evals 31 and 32\ncover the re-read rule and the CLI guard.\n\nA second live run, following the runbook with no command pre-approved,\nreached Complete with each of these rules observed.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate; changes generator verification and exploration text and adds a reviewer Phase 2 judgement\nNot-tested: hosts other than Claude Code for the live run\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n\n\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFpHNZwJHqbGAFPmKTVEdH8MBX0ojFfAS66hTmwB/4bBFrdsDaHli5tkzfYub4ZYcW\nT55HI+CUdVZc4FgtoPPQU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T02:40:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/c7ce7bcd52940bc706fae4d059b43d19c46abeb5","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGM3Y2U3YmNkNTI5NDBiYzcwNmZhZTRkMDU5YjQzZDE5YzQ2YWJlYjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/c48fe844f37f0631cd6751daf482ebf5550b767b","sha":"c48fe844f37f0631cd6751daf482ebf5550b767b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c48fe844f37f0631cd6751daf482ebf5550b767b"}],"sha":"c7ce7bcd52940bc706fae4d059b43d19c46abeb5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c7ce7bcd52940bc706fae4d059b43d19c46abeb5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c48fe844f37f0631cd6751daf482ebf5550b767b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T16:31:05Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T16:31:05Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Disclose every file the generator writes and check the write set\n\nThe generator recommended an API-login setup project and shared mock\nhelpers, but only locator files and control files had approval rows. An\nagent could create auth.setup.ts, add helpers, and edit\nplaywright.config.* without disclosing any of them, and the post-run\ngit status check could not tell those writes from verifier artifacts.\n\nStep 4 now has a Proposed generated files table (specs, Page Objects,\nhelpers, fixtures, setup projects, config edits, toHaveScreenshot snapshot\ndirectories, and first-party planner output), and the approval gate\ncovers it.\n\nStep 3 records `git status --porcelain --untracked-files=all` from the\nworktree root, plus a content hash of every path already listed, before\nexploration writes anything. The write set is every status change since,\nplus every hash change on an already-listed path, so an approved edit to\nan already-dirty config is still seen. Already-dirty paths are the user''s\nand are never reverted, cleaned, staged, or attributed to the candidate,\nunless the table lists one as Modified; a path the user says they edited\nduring the task is theirs too. A non-Git target hashes the test directory\nand the listed paths, and says the check covers only those.\n\nBefore completion, artifacts the task''s own verification created are\nremoved and the removal recorded, as verification-rules.md already\nrequired. Playwright''s output folders, an approved setup project''s\nstorageState file, and exploration output are listed separately. Any\nother path outside the approved tables is reported, not deleted, and\nreturns PARTIAL/BLOCKED on a `write set` line of the existing template.\nThe completion matrix gains that row, a report hiding such a path is\ninvalid, the Complete template records the write set, and the cleanup\nrule notes that a gitignored scratch directory must be checked directly.\nNo verdict term or result-schema field changed, so the verification\nparity checks are untouched.\n\nThe existing rule that approval covers only the exact command shown had no\ntest; it is now pinned.\n\nNew contract assertions failed against the previous SKILL.md and pass now,\nwith mutation guards that delete or reverse each rule, including one that\nturns the unlisted-path outcome into Complete. Evals 28-30 cover a\ndisclosed setup project and config edit; a dirty tree with a leftover\nverifier spec, an approved edit to an already-dirty config, runtime\noutput, and one undisclosed helper; and a pipe appended to an approved\ncommand versus a user-typed `cd ... &&` command.\n\nAn adversarial review before release found that the first draft gave an\nunlisted path no final status and told the task not to delete its own\nverifier artifacts, contradicting verification-rules.md; both are fixed\nhere, along with the runtime-output and already-dirty-path gaps.\n\nDerived from a review of cheongfish/bouncer''s scope gates; its commit-time\ncheck and single-argv rule were rejected because this skill never commits\nand users may approve compound commands verbatim.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate; adds an approval table and a completion condition to the generator\nNot-tested: live generator runs against a real project\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"4f2ed4f3ff7e1e80cc0d67df7a945d210b3b9ae3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/4f2ed4f3ff7e1e80cc0d67df7a945d210b3b9ae3"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/c48fe844f37f0631cd6751daf482ebf5550b767b","verification":{"payload":"tree 4f2ed4f3ff7e1e80cc0d67df7a945d210b3b9ae3\nparent 5d1831d2757413004f8dac1e8a420e57e7f35612\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.nore