gitignored scratch directory must be checked directly.\nNo verdict term or result-schema field changed, so the verification\nparity checks are untouched.\n\nThe existing rule that approval covers only the exact command shown had no\ntest; it is now pinned.\n\nNew contract assertions failed against the previous SKILL.md and pass now,\nwith mutation guards that delete or reverse each rule, including one that\nturns the unlisted-path outcome into Complete. Evals 28-30 cover a\ndisclosed setup project and config edit; a dirty tree with a leftover\nverifier spec, an approved edit to an already-dirty config, runtime\noutput, and one undisclosed helper; and a pipe appended to an approved\ncommand versus a user-typed `cd ... &&` command.\n\nAn adversarial review before release found that the first draft gave an\nunlisted path no final status and told the task not to delete its own\nverifier artifacts, contradicting verification-rules.md; both are fixed\nhere, along with the runtime-output and already-dirty-path gaps.\n\nDerived from a review of cheongfish/bouncer''s scope gates; its commit-time\ncheck and single-argv rule were rejected because this skill never commits\nand users may approve compound commands verbatim.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate; adds an approval table and a completion condition to the generator\nNot-tested: live generator runs against a real project\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n\n\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQH9TMQJvap3uCZfgGzQZv753VXgOzFnOPHVWfSL88T4p6gd84AX9Br5z3lYupcPnwX\nyg7mkkh5JPNEF/NbxyhAQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T02:40:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/c48fe844f37f0631cd6751daf482ebf5550b767b","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGM0OGZlODQ0ZjM3ZjA2MzFjZDY3NTFkYWY0ODJlYmY1NTUwYjc2N2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/5d1831d2757413004f8dac1e8a420e57e7f35612","sha":"5d1831d2757413004f8dac1e8a420e57e7f35612","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/5d1831d2757413004f8dac1e8a420e57e7f35612"}],"sha":"c48fe844f37f0631cd6751daf482ebf5550b767b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c48fe844f37f0631cd6751daf482ebf5550b767b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/5d1831d2757413004f8dac1e8a420e57e7f35612/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T15:42:17Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T15:42:17Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Stop the reviewer scanner from running Linux /usr/bin/sg as ast-grep\n\nOn Debian and Ubuntu, /usr/bin/sg is the shadow-utils group command. The\nscanner''s fixed ast-grep candidate list ended with the three sg paths, so a\nLinux host without ast-grep ran `sg scan ...` as newgrp, and Tier 2 ended\nINCOMPLETE with exit 2 instead of reaching the pinned npx fallback. The\nlist has carried those paths since 1.11.0.\n\nHosted CI hid this while it installed @ast-grep/cli globally, which put\n/usr/local/bin/ast-grep ahead of /usr/bin/sg. 1.17.0 switched CI to an\nintegrity-pinned binary passed through E2E_SMELL_AST_GREP_BIN, and six\nscanner tests that clear that variable failed on Linux only.\n\nThe fixed list now names only ast-grep. Every ast-grep installer that\nships sg also ships ast-grep beside it, which is the rule the post-fix\nverifier already follows. E2E_SMELL_AST_GREP_BIN still accepts an explicit\npath; it should name ast-grep, because a current Homebrew sg is a shim\nthat looks up ast-grep on PATH, which the scanner pins. ci-local.sh''s\navailability warning uses the same list.\nA static check pins the list; it fails on the previous list.\n\nIn a python:3.12-slim container, where /usr/bin/sg links to newgrp, the\nprevious scanner printed \"newgrp: unrecognized option ''--rule''\" and exited\n2 on a one-file project; the fixed scanner completed with exit 0.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; three candidate paths removed from a fixed lookup list\nNot-tested: hosted CI, pending push\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"80ed31e64bf5ebe03df9e974fa5529d61378bc27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/80ed31e64bf5ebe03df9e974fa5529d61378bc27"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/5d1831d2757413004f8dac1e8a420e57e7f35612","verification":{"payload":"tree 80ed31e64bf5ebe03df9e974fa5529d61378bc27\nparent ac5a322d1c7beed7ba143a482f483674cba2cd32\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789746137 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789746137 +0900\n\nStop the reviewer scanner from running Linux /usr/bin/sg as ast-grep\n\nOn Debian and Ubuntu, /usr/bin/sg is the shadow-utils group command. The\nscanner''s fixed ast-grep candidate list ended with the three sg paths, so a\nLinux host without ast-grep ran `sg scan ...` as newgrp, and Tier 2 ended\nINCOMPLETE with exit 2 instead of reaching the pinned npx fallback. The\nlist has carried those paths since 1.11.0.\n\nHosted CI hid this while it installed @ast-grep/cli globally, which put\n/usr/local/bin/ast-grep ahead of /usr/bin/sg. 1.17.0 switched CI to an\nintegrity-pinned binary passed through E2E_SMELL_AST_GREP_BIN, and six\nscanner tests that clear that variable failed on Linux only.\n\nThe fixed list now names only ast-grep. Every ast-grep installer that\nships sg also ships ast-grep beside it, which is the rule the post-fix\nverifier already follows. E2E_SMELL_AST_GREP_BIN still accepts an explicit\npath; it should name ast-grep, because a current Homebrew sg is a shim\nthat looks up ast-grep on PATH, which the scanner pins. ci-local.sh''s\navailability warning uses the same list.\nA static check pins the list; it fails on the previous list.\n\nIn a python:3.12-slim container, where /usr/bin/sg links to newgrp, the\nprevious scanner printed \"newgrp: unrecognized option ''--rule''\" and exited\n2 on a one-file project; the fixed scanner completed with exit 0.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; three candidate paths removed from a fixed lookup list\nNot-tested: hosted CI, pending push\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n\n\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQE2FsJct3MUHKreFAcT9h0/xbG3mREIaMp3V9ADhIaWimJPyUswk7N65zQHaEg3xf5\nek60R0ZH18uwQGczcksAA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-19T02:40:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/5d1831d2757413004f8dac1e8a420e57e7f35612","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDVkMTgzMWQyNzU3NDEzMDA0ZjhkYWMxZThhNDIwZTU3ZTdmMzU2MTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/ac5a322d1c7beed7ba143a482f483674cba2cd32","sha":"ac5a322d1c7beed7ba143a482f483674cba2cd32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/ac5a322d1c7beed7ba143a482f483674cba2cd32"}],"sha":"5d1831d2757413004f8dac1e8a420e57e7f35612","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/5d1831d2757413004f8dac1e8a420e57e7f35612"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/ac5a322d1c7beed7ba143a482f483674cba2cd32/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T04:27:59Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T04:27:59Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Suppress the HOL scanner false positive on a frozen healer snapshot\n\nThe HOL Plugin Scanner failed on push a8b9381 with HARDCODED_SECRET in\nbenchmarks/healer-perturbation-v1/source-snapshots/0fc0e068....json,\nwhich was added in 1.17.0. The snapshot embeds a byte copy of\nskills/e2e-reviewer/scripts/scan.sh, so this is the same false positive on\nthe #14 credential rule definitions that .plugin-scanner.toml already\nsuppresses for scan.sh itself. The snapshot is digest-pinned evidence and\ncannot be edited, so only that exact path is added, to the config and to\nthe exact-set pin in test-security-gates.py.\n\nReproduced locally with plugin-scanner==2.0.864 against git archive HEAD:\ntwo findings before, zero after, exit 0.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; one exact path added to a third-party scanner''s ignore list\nNot-tested: hosted HOL run, pending this push\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"641c55ddb0875587d6689559ace4433c0350a732","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/641c55ddb0875587d6689559ace4433c0350a732"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/ac5a322d1c7beed7ba143a482f483674cba2cd32","verification":{"payload":"tree 641c55ddb0875587d6689559ace4433c0350a732\nparent a8b93814b5839507589f5e2112c20b1e3a06756a\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789705679 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789705679 +0900\n\nSuppress the HOL scanner false positive on a frozen healer snapshot\n\nThe HOL Plugin Scanner failed on push a8b9381 with HARDCODED_SECRET in\nbenchmarks/healer-perturbation-v1/source-snapshots/0fc0e068....json,\nwhich was added in 1.17.0. The snapshot embeds a byte copy of\nskills/e2e-reviewer/scripts/scan.sh, so this is the same false positive on\nthe #14 credential rule definitions that .plugin-scanner.toml already\nsuppresses for scan.sh itself. The snapshot is digest-pinned evidence and\ncannot be edited, so only that exact path is added, to the config and to\nthe exact-set pin in test-security-gates.py.\n\nReproduced locally with plugin-scanner==2.0.864 against git archive HEAD:\ntwo findings before, zero after, exit 0.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; one exact path added to a third-party scanner''s ignore list\nNot-tested: hosted HOL run, pending this push\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMh1jm3cty2UeF2lVEY/mDT59y50Z6Nqvj9MWc5nMmWkcBctuvbXZhYydgK5ai3HFO\ngWO8VxwsjWCmw578QZgw4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T04:28:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/ac5a322d1c7beed7ba143a482f483674cba2cd32","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGFjNWEzMjJkMWM3YmVlZDdiYTE0M2E0ODJmNDgzNjc0Y2JhMmNkMzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/a8b93814b5839507589f5e2112c20b1e3a06756a","sha":"a8b93814b5839507589f5e2112c20b1e3a06756a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/a8b93814b5839507589f5e2112c20b1e3a06756a"}],"sha":"ac5a322d1c7beed7ba143a482f483674cba2cd32","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/ac5a322d1c7beed7ba143a482f483674cba2cd32"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/a8b93814b5839507589f5e2112c20b1e3a06756a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:24:52Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T02:46:47Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Release v1.17.0 as the single published version\n\nTwo interim version bumps, 1.16.4 and 1.17.1, were made while this work was\nsplit across phases and were never published; their content ships here, in\none release. All four SKILL.md files and all three plugin manifests carry\n1.17.0, and the changelog keeps one dated section instead of three.\n\nTwo evidence gaps close with it. The refused #4l rule now records the sources\nbehind the Phase 2 item it became - the tautological-test idea and the\nPlaywright/Cypress mocking guidance that separates the defect from the shape\nthis bundle recommends - so a later reader can see what the refusal rested\non. The healer benchmark records what the public record contains: a bounded\nsearch on 2026-09-18 across web, arXiv, microsoft/playwright issues and\ndiscussions, official video subtitles, and playwright.dev found no published\nmeasurement of Playwright''s own Test Agents healer, the closest artifact\nbeing one practitioner write-up with author-judged outcomes, and the widely\nrepeated \"~75% success\" figure appears in no Playwright source and is not\ncited. The three convergence sources are marked as measuring other systems,\nand the transferable-patterns table shows the two rows whose status changed\nwhen 1.17.0 shipped: the recorded-trace idea is partially adopted through\nimported manual cases, and the non-isolated-green principle through the\nStep 5 baseline run.\n\nA review of the whole range against origin found one specification gap and\nthree bookkeeping defects, fixed here. The baseline rule had no outcome for a\nrepository with no existing coverage of the target area - the first generated\ntest, which is exactly the tracer case - so a literal reading left it unable\nto reach Complete; that case is now \"baseline not applicable\", which keeps V5\ninterpretable, with the contract test extended. The evidence-ledger intro\nstill counted 59 sources, the performance record cited a rebased-away commit\nand its own superseded 3.4x figure, and the eval entry sat under Unreleased\nalthough the tag includes it.\n\nA focused review of the three generator features found six specification\ngaps, fixed here. A product with one error message by design but no\ndocumented rule had no recordable value; it is now\nGENERIC_BY_CONTRACT: NEEDS_PRODUCT_CONTEXT, surfaced at the approval gate.\nA read-only scenario had no evidence path, because V4 proves only writes.\nV3 had no fault direction under GENERIC_BY_CONTRACT; it now turns the\nfailure into the success the scenario denies, and a fault that leaves the\nsame screen is CANNOT_VERIFY rather than FAIL. Two secondary-outcome skip\nconditions collided with V4 and with the primary outcome, and an imported\ncase''s contradicted steps were dropped silently instead of being reported\nat the approval gate. Evals 24-27 now test each of these, including one\nmeaning-reversing mutation guard.\n\nSkill prose paragraphs are now one physical line each, as CONTRIBUTING.md\nalready required: a hard-wrapped paragraph shifts every later line number\non any edit. Only standalone paragraphs were joined; list items, tables,\ncode, frontmatter, and frozen benchmark evidence are untouched, and every\nreflowed file matches its previous version after whitespace\nnormalization. The four SKILL.md files now run 302 to 434 lines with\ntheir word counts unchanged. Contract assertions that matched a hard-wrap\nnewline now match the joined text, and the reviewer evidence status\nrecords the new skill digest.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; version metadata, changelog structure, evidence prose, generator specification gaps, and a whitespace-only reflow of skill prose\nNot-tested: hosted CI; Reddit could not be searched from this environment, so the healer search is bounded rather than exhaustive\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaud