 cases, and the non-isolated-green principle through the\nStep 5 baseline run.\n\nA review of the whole range against origin found one specification gap and\nthree bookkeeping defects, fixed here. The baseline rule had no outcome for a\nrepository with no existing coverage of the target area - the first generated\ntest, which is exactly the tracer case - so a literal reading left it unable\nto reach Complete; that case is now \"baseline not applicable\", which keeps V5\ninterpretable, with the contract test extended. The evidence-ledger intro\nstill counted 59 sources, the performance record cited a rebased-away commit\nand its own superseded 3.4x figure, and the eval entry sat under Unreleased\nalthough the tag includes it.\n\nA focused review of the three generator features found six specification\ngaps, fixed here. A product with one error message by design but no\ndocumented rule had no recordable value; it is now\nGENERIC_BY_CONTRACT: NEEDS_PRODUCT_CONTEXT, surfaced at the approval gate.\nA read-only scenario had no evidence path, because V4 proves only writes.\nV3 had no fault direction under GENERIC_BY_CONTRACT; it now turns the\nfailure into the success the scenario denies, and a fault that leaves the\nsame screen is CANNOT_VERIFY rather than FAIL. Two secondary-outcome skip\nconditions collided with V4 and with the primary outcome, and an imported\ncase''s contradicted steps were dropped silently instead of being reported\nat the approval gate. Evals 24-27 now test each of these, including one\nmeaning-reversing mutation guard.\n\nSkill prose paragraphs are now one physical line each, as CONTRIBUTING.md\nalready required: a hard-wrapped paragraph shifts every later line number\non any edit. Only standalone paragraphs were joined; list items, tables,\ncode, frontmatter, and frozen benchmark evidence are untouched, and every\nreflowed file matches its previous version after whitespace\nnormalization. The four SKILL.md files now run 302 to 434 lines with\ntheir word counts unchanged. Contract assertions that matched a hard-wrap\nnewline now match the joined text, and the reviewer evidence status\nrecords the new skill digest.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; version metadata, changelog structure, evidence prose, generator specification gaps, and a whitespace-only reflow of skill prose\nNot-tested: hosted CI; Reddit could not be searched from this environment, so the healer search is bounded rather than exhaustive\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLIf3UJ+TN87ERBW8W5yxcV21KF+pnpqnxTQ5CiyDRwL96sbf+6GCfK6a2SAXjfIB3\nLrHXrEc62JQyc4C5AZagI=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T03:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/a8b93814b5839507589f5e2112c20b1e3a06756a","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGE4YjkzODE0YjU4Mzk1MDc1ODlmNWUyMTEyYzIwYjFlM2EwNjc1NmE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/29aff5182e161e835092361597b80cf090e52488","sha":"29aff5182e161e835092361597b80cf090e52488","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/29aff5182e161e835092361597b80cf090e52488"}],"sha":"a8b93814b5839507589f5e2112c20b1e3a06756a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/a8b93814b5839507589f5e2112c20b1e3a06756a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/29aff5182e161e835092361597b80cf090e52488/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:20:39Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:24:39Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Judge eleven swallowed-catch candidates in one eval\n\nPhase 1 reports every `.catch(() => {})` as a #3 candidate because grep\ncannot see whether the test can still fail. This eval fixes what Phase 2\nmust conclude for eleven of them in one file: three are P0 - a sole\nswallowed assertion, the same shape split across lines, and a swallowed\nhalf of a two-part promise whose surviving assertion proves only the other\nhalf - and eight must not be reported, including an `expect.soft` whose\nfailure is recorded rather than thrown, a synchronous matcher that throws\nbefore `.catch` attaches, a locally shadowed `expect`, and a `finally` that\nthrows unconditionally.\n\nThe fixture came from a 2026-09-07 worktree that was removed during cleanup;\nit is the only content there that main did not already carry.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none; one eval fixture and one eval case\nNot-tested: the judgement is documentary, as every reviewer eval is; the scanner''s Phase 1 output for the fixture was captured before writing it\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"456660fe8ce53423d14243bba6ce7e85a6d4c709","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/456660fe8ce53423d14243bba6ce7e85a6d4c709"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/29aff5182e161e835092361597b80cf090e52488","verification":{"payload":"tree 456660fe8ce53423d14243bba6ce7e85a6d4c709\nparent ebde6ce3071d89f782a149652775842f17e2fb91\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789694439 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789694679 +0900\n\nJudge eleven swallowed-catch candidates in one eval\n\nPhase 1 reports every `.catch(() => {})` as a #3 candidate because grep\ncannot see whether the test can still fail. This eval fixes what Phase 2\nmust conclude for eleven of them in one file: three are P0 - a sole\nswallowed assertion, the same shape split across lines, and a swallowed\nhalf of a two-part promise whose surviving assertion proves only the other\nhalf - and eight must not be reported, including an `expect.soft` whose\nfailure is recorded rather than thrown, a synchronous matcher that throws\nbefore `.catch` attaches, a locally shadowed `expect`, and a `finally` that\nthrows unconditionally.\n\nThe fixture came from a 2026-09-07 worktree that was removed during cleanup;\nit is the only content there that main did not already carry.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none; one eval fixture and one eval case\nNot-tested: the judgement is documentary, as every reviewer eval is; the scanner''s Phase 1 output for the fixture was captured before writing it\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFwDAi2lcSFW30c/XxLeiDB3mo44kbtqGDB8T6DF0h1Ao1VnwsyzuVE8dYA1hJQGHe\nx4KfjRQ9ymuGdl7MT6jww=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T03:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/29aff5182e161e835092361597b80cf090e52488","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDI5YWZmNTE4MmUxNjFlODM1MDkyMzYxNTk3YjgwY2YwOTBlNTI0ODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/ebde6ce3071d89f782a149652775842f17e2fb91","sha":"ebde6ce3071d89f782a149652775842f17e2fb91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/ebde6ce3071d89f782a149652775842f17e2fb91"}],"sha":"29aff5182e161e835092361597b80cf090e52488","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/29aff5182e161e835092361597b80cf090e52488"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/ebde6ce3071d89f782a149652775842f17e2fb91/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T21:06:26Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:23:29Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Audit three self-repair sources into the evidence ledger\n\nThe healer benchmark cited external convergence in prose; the ledger now\ncarries those sources under its own status rules, as rows 60-62, and audits\n62 sources.\n\nLee''s 2026 industrial preprint is Verified primary for the failure classes:\nit documents assertion weakening and test-case deletion during autonomous\nrepair over 300 execution reports on one enterprise Playwright prototype,\nwhich is a single-system case study rather than a transferable rate. The\nSelf-Repair Trap preprint is Qualified because its studied surface is\nunit-level regression-oracle completion, not browser E2E. The practitioner\nfalse-heal article is Qualified because it states its sample - 136 controlled\nUI perturbations, two applications, four resolvers - but does not publish the\nunderlying data, and covers locator healing rather than assertion semantics.\n\nThe IJESR healer case study was read and left out: its venue could not be\nestablished as a durable peer-reviewed original, and the ledger does not\ncarry sources it cannot clear.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; ledger rows, their CI counts, and the four README editions'' source count\nNot-tested: none beyond the ledger contract test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"e3b8f236287cf404c7ee0552198977f0f8674b90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/e3b8f236287cf404c7ee0552198977f0f8674b90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/ebde6ce3071d89f782a149652775842f17e2fb91","verification":{"payload":"tree e3b8f236287cf404c7ee0552198977f0f8674b90\nparent c7dc042ef60dc73ec0bcf7869ca93be0fc313c01\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789679186 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789694609 +0900\n\nAudit three self-repair sources into the evidence ledger\n\nThe healer benchmark cited external convergence in prose; the ledger now\ncarries those sources under its own status rules, as rows 60-62, and audits\n62 sources.\n\nLee''s 2026 industrial preprint is Verified primary for the failure classes:\nit documents assertion weakening and test-case deletion during autonomous\nrepair over 300 execution reports on one enterprise Playwright prototype,\nwhich is a single-system case study rather than a transferable rate. The\nSelf-Repair Trap preprint is Qualified because its studied surface is\nunit-level regression-oracle completion, not browser E2E. The practitioner\nfalse-heal article is Qualified because it states its sample - 136 controlled\nUI perturbations, two applications, four resolvers - but does not publish the\nunderlying data, and covers locator healing rather than assertion semantics.\n\nThe IJESR healer case study was read and left out: its venue could not be\nestablished as a durable peer-reviewed original, and the ledger does not\ncarry sources it cannot clear.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; ledger rows, their CI counts, and the four README editions'' source count\nNot-tested: none beyond the ledger contract test\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQGqmq+1qSk8zYQNWz2fHiloAzhscgcUbUABeMtKw2oF1ITUNIEDHfE7P17XAKu/pmJ\nDKgD0EhHfyvo4LxKEDOQ8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T03:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/ebde6ce3071d89f782a149652775842f17e2fb91","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGViZGU2Y2UzMDcxZDg5Zjc4MmExNDk2NTI3NzU4NDJmMTdlMmZiOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/c7dc042ef60dc73ec0bcf7869ca93be0fc313c01","sha":"c7dc042ef60dc73ec0bcf7869ca93be0fc313c01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c7dc042ef60dc73ec0bcf7869ca93be0fc313c01"}],"sha":"ebde6ce3071d89f782a149652775842f17e2fb91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/ebde6ce3071d89f782a149652775842f17e2fb91"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c7dc042ef60dc73ec0bcf7869ca93be0fc313c01/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T20:33:49Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:23:29Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Stop re-lexing each file once per reported hit\n\nA timestamped bash -x trace attributed the scanner''s per-hit cost before\nanything was changed. `_line_is_justified` ran one awk pass per hit and each\npass lexed the file from line 1, so a dense file paid quadratic time for a\nmarker convention. The same awk program now reports every justified line in\none pass per file, and the per-hit check is a cached membership test; the\nclassification rules are untouched.\n\nTwo smaller forks went with it: `absolute_hit_file` re-resolved the same few\npaths through a subshell for every filtered hit, and `allocate_temp` spawned\nmktemp for every scratch file. Resolution is memoized per spelling, failures\nincluded, and file allocation uses a private counter inside the scanner''s own\n0700 temp root. Both caches are parallel arrays walked linearly, because bash\n3.2 has no associative arrays and the security policy refuses eval in shipped\nshell; directory allocation still uses mktemp.\n\nThe acceptance gate is byte-identical output, not speed: stdout and exit code\nare unchanged on the pinned 300-hit fixture, on this repository''s skills/,\nscripts/, and evals/files/ trees, and on ten adversarial fixtures covering\nJUSTIFIED forms, quote-bearing regex literals, option-object chains,\nmulti-line chain heads, CRLF, tokenizer edges, paths with spaces, and\nfocused-suite forms. The fixture, method, and numbers are recorded in\nbenchmarks/scanner-hot-path-v1: 30.9 s to 7.5 s for 300 hits, 4.1x.\n\nRejected: an associative-array cache | bash 3.2 has none, and eval is blocked by the security policy\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: medium; the justification driver changed for every tier, which is why output equality was checked on twelve trees rather than asserted\nNot-tested: Linux timings; the measurement is one machine and one synthetic dense shape\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"3c750f8cf22ea1c31bd707b8b68f282140644ccc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/3c750f8cf22ea1c31bd707b8b68f282140644ccc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/c7dc042ef60dc73ec0bcf7869ca93be0fc313c01","verification":{"payload":"tree 3c750f8cf22ea1c31bd707b8b68f282140644ccc\nparent b2c5faec97254ae75a45f692df2ad29beb784363\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789677229 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789694609 +0900\n\nStop re-lexing each file once per reported hit\n\nA timestamped bash -x trace attributed the scanner''s per-hit cost before\nanything was changed. `_line_is_justified` ran one awk pass per hit and each\npass lexed the file from line 1, so a dense file paid quadratic time for a\nmarker convention. The same awk program now reports every justified line in\none pass per file, and the per-hit check is a cached membership test; the\nclassification rules are untouched.\n\nTwo smaller forks went with it: `absolute_hit_file` re-resolved the same few\npaths through a subshell for every filtered hit, and `allocate_temp` spawned\nmktemp for every scratch file. Resolution is memoized per spelling, failures\nincluded, and file allocation uses a private counter inside the scanner''s own\n0700 temp root. Both caches are parallel arrays walked linearly, because bash\n3.2 has no associative arrays and the security policy refuses eval in shipped\nshell; directory allocation still uses mktemp.\n\nThe acceptance gate is byte-identical output, not speed: stdout and exit code\nare unchanged on the pinned 300-hit fixture, on this repository''s skills/,\nscripts/, and evals/files/ trees, and on ten adversarial fixtures covering\nJUSTIFIED forms, quote-bearing regex literals, option-object chains,\nmulti-line chain heads, CRLF, tokenizer edges, paths with spaces, and\nfocused-suite forms. The fixture, method, and numbers are recorded in\nbenchmarks/scanner-hot-path-v1: 30.9 s to 7.5 s for 300 hits, 4.1x.\n\nRejected: an associative-array cache | bash 3.2 has none, and eval is blocked by the security policy\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: medium; the justification driver changed for every tier, which is why output equality was checked on twelve trees rather than asserted\nNot-tested: Linux timings; the measurement is one machine and one synthetic dense shape\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOOUP7tx0Y9gjUUKH6fI9ZCE+x3mpt+V00E1ZJyyS0C6jmWVfT81EovJ5z4y3LSwCa\ntgTRndOJfUHfaO6jGyfAo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T03:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/c7dc042ef60dc73ec0bcf7869ca93be0fc313c01","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGM3ZGMwNDJlZjYwZGM3M2VjMGJjZjc4NjljYTkzYmUwZmMzMTNjMDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/b2c5faec97254ae75a45f692df2ad29beb784363","sha":"b2c5faec97254ae75a45f692df2ad29beb784363","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/b2c5faec97254ae75a45f692df2ad29beb784363"}],"sha":"c7dc042ef60dc73ec0bcf7869ca93be0fc313c01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c7dc042ef60dc73ec0bcf7869ca93be0fc313c01"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/b2c5faec97254ae75a45f692df2ad29beb784363/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T19:35:02Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:23:28Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Refuse the #4l scanner rule on its own measurement\n\nStub-echo-v1 ran against the twelve pinned field-scan-v1 repositories. The\ndeterministic collector found 78 candidates in two of them, and adjudicating\nevery one against the frozen rubric produced zero STUB_ECHO instances: 71\nassertions read a real backend response - jhipster registers cy.intercept as\na spy with no canned reply, and open-mercato''s page.route handlers pass the\nobserved methods through with route.continue(), including the 409 the\napplication itself returns - and 7 stubbed routes are observed only as a\nsynchronization wait before assertions on rendered rows, which is the shape\n\nG1 therefore fails and G2 has no positives to bound, so the frozen\nconsequence applies: the shape is documented in the #4 Phase 2 procedure\ntogether with its three lookalikes, and no scanner rule is added. A rule\nkeyed on the collector''s surface would have fired on 78 correct tests in this\nsample. G3 and G4 were not run because the decision no longer depended on\nthem, and nothing about them is claimed.\n\nConstraint: thresholds and consequences were committed in caab223 before collection\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; one Phase 2 paragraph in the reviewer contract, plus published evidence\nNot-tested: prevalence outside this twelve-repository popularity sample; the collector only sees specs that stub and observe a response in the same file\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"b8ddcb03418f512233bf9f61174c514eba8e2df4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/b8ddcb03418f512233bf9f61174c514eba8e2df4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/b2c5faec97254ae75a45f692df2ad29beb784363","verification":{"payload":"tree b8ddcb03418f512233bf9f61174c514eba8e2df4\nparent f9acf2396e4a5171bd79b76bea1523514710ceea\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789673702 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789694608 +0900\n\nRefuse the #4l scanner rule on its own measurement\n\nStub-echo-v1 ran against the twelve pinned field-scan-v1 repositories. The\ndeterministic collector found 78 candidates in two of them, and adjudicating\nevery one against the frozen rubric produced zero STUB_ECHO instances: 71\nassertions read a real backend response - jhipster registers cy.intercept as\na spy with no canned reply, and open-mercato''s page.route handlers pass the\nobserved methods through with route.continue(), including the 409 the\napplication itself returns - and 7 stubbed routes are observed only as a\nsynchronization wait before assertions on rendered rows, which is the shape\n\nG1 therefore fails and G2 has no positives to bound, so the frozen\nconsequence applies: the shape is documented in the #4 Phase 2 procedure\ntogether with its three lookalikes, and no scanner rule is added. A rule\nkeyed on the collector''s surface would have fired on 78 correct tests in this\nsample. G3 and G4 were not run because the decision no longer depended on\nthem, and nothing about them is claimed.\n\nConstraint: thresholds and consequences were committed in caab223 before collection\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; one Phase 2 paragraph in the reviewer contract, plus published evidence\nNot-tested: prevalence outside this twelve-repository popularity sample; the collector only sees specs that stub and observe a response in the same file\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQD/JL+TP+ChiAaCazzGRnGcRznAv78OX9eJKLI3obHTEJhBxDUdPy1VuRxbA8QNegU\na7e8p3xZoAXA7JzJfL1wk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T03:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/b2c5faec97254ae75a45f692df2ad29beb784363","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGIyYzVmYWVjOTcyNTRhZTc1YTQ1ZjY5MmRmMmFkMjliZWI3ODQzNjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f9acf2396e4a5171bd79b76bea1523514710ceea","sha":"f9acf2396e4a5171bd79b76bea1523514710ceea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f9acf2396e4a5171bd79b76bea1523514710ceea"}],"sha":"b2c5faec97254ae75a45f692df2ad29beb784363","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/b2c5faec97254ae75a45f692df2ad29beb784363"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f9acf2396e4a5171bd79b76bea1523514710ceea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:59:44Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:23:28Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Freeze the stub-echo-v1 measurement before collecting it\n\nThe proposed reviewer sub-pattern #4l would flag an assertion whose subject\nis a response the same test stubbed. Its risk is that the correct fix this\nbundle already documents for #20 - stub the network, assert the rendered\noutput - looks superficially similar, so a rule that cannot separate the two\nwould flag its own guidance.\n\nThis freezes what would justify the rule before any candidate is seen: the\ncorpus is field-scan-v1''s twelve pinned repositories with its contamination\nexclusion, the collector is deterministic and publishes every hit, every\ncandidate is adjudicated against a fixed rubric where UNDECIDABLE counts\nagainst precision, and four gates decide the outcome - prevalence, a Wilson\nlower bound for separability, an executable proof that the shape is an\nalways-pass, and a guard set that must stay silent. Each failing gate has a\nnamed consequence, including \"document it in Phase 2 and add no rule\".\n\nStatus is NOT_RUN: nothing has been collected yet.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none; new benchmark directory only\nNot-tested: the collector has not been run against a checkout yet\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"4981d4f4b6c34edba52c9030d6d12b2012cabaa0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/4981d4f4b6c34edba52c9030d6d12b2012cabaa0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/f9acf2396e4a5171bd79b76bea1523514710ceea","verification":{"payload":"tree 4981d4f4b6c34edba52c9030d6d12b2012cabaa0\nparent 35319ad921cf0a640f5b37050bfc4fa85dd7168c\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789671584 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789694608 +0900\n\nFreeze the stub-echo-v1 measurement before collecting it\n\nThe proposed reviewer sub-pattern #4l would flag an assertion whose subject\nis a response the same test stubbed. Its risk is that the correct fix this\nbundle already documents for #20 - stub the network, assert the rendered\noutput - looks superficially similar, so a rule that cannot separate the two\nwould flag its own guidance.\n\nThis freezes what would justify the rule before any candidate is seen: the\ncorpus is field-scan-v1''s twelve pinned repositories with its contamination\nexclusion, the collector is deterministic and publishes every hit, every\ncandidate is adjudicated against a fixed rubric where UNDECIDABLE counts\nagainst precision, and four gates decide the outcome - prevalence, a Wilson\nlower bound for separability, an executable proof that the shape is an\nalways-pass, and a guard set that must stay silent. Each failing gate has a\nnamed consequence, including \"document it in Phase 2 and add no rule\".\n\nStatus is NOT_RUN: nothing has been collected yet.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none; new benchmark directory only\nNot-tested: the collector has not been run against a checkout yet\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNZgP5FBohoKi1uTV8BO1BfK5PhPCdwodgnfpbzVsGpil73nYpeNZXf65BoEOmgfJX\nZefqzCUXYRYYGIZbSAWAY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T03:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f9acf2396e4a5171bd79b76bea1523514710ceea","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGY5YWNmMjM5NmU0YTUxNzFiZDc5Yjc2YmVhMTUyMzUxNDcxMGNlZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/35319ad921cf0a640f5b37050bfc4fa85dd7168c","sha":"35319ad921cf0a640f5b37050bfc4fa85dd7168c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/35319ad921cf0a640f5b37050bfc4fa85dd7168c"}],"sha":"f9acf2396e4a5171bd79b76bea1523514710ceea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f9acf2396e4a5171bd79b76bea1523514710ceea"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/35319ad921cf0a640f5b37050bfc4fa85dd7168c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T18:28:33Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:23:28Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Read generated tests against a recorded baseline and cause\n\nFour generator additions, each with a contract test, a deletion-mutation\nguard, and evals on both sides.\n\nStep 5 runs the approved existing tests for the target area once before the\ntracer scenario. A red suite made every later verdict unreadable: a failure\nthat was already there looked like the candidate''s. A green run becomes the\nbaseline; a red run outside the candidate''s surface is recorded and excluded\nfrom V5 attribution; a red run on the candidate''s own route, feature,\nfixture, Page Object, global setup, or stored authentication state returns\nPARTIAL/BLOCKED; and when no approved command covers the area without\nreplaying a persistent write that V5 forbids, the run is skipped, recorded\nas \"baseline not established\", and V5''s suite-context mode is CANNOT_VERIFY.\nNo new status word is introduced.\n\nStep 4 now records an Error-cause signal, because a scenario that only\nproves \"an error appeared\" passes for every cause that reaches the same\nscreen. A product that shows one message for several causes by design is\nrecorded as GENERIC_BY_CONTRACT with its rule; the distinguishing evidence\nis then the V4 request proof, and V3 must not swap causes to falsify it.\n\nScenarios may carry up to three named secondary outcomes - survives a\nreload, side effect proved, error cause distinguished - each recorded as\nselected or skipped. They are extra assertions: V1 keeps one primary\noutcome and V2/V3 falsify only that one.\n\nAn exported manual test case (markdown, CSV, or pasted text from TestRail,\nZephyr, Xray, Qase) can fill Owner/source, and its id is carried into the\ntest title. The export is untrusted data: no command inside it runs, no URL\nis opened, no credential is used, observation beats contradicting steps, and\nthe skill never calls a test-management API.\n\nConstraint: reviewer evidence-status digest changes because upstream-rule-sources.md is inside the reviewed skill\nRejected: a new PARTIAL status for a missing baseline | the V-rule vocabulary is a checked contract; CANNOT_VERIFY on V5 already expresses it\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: medium; every generated scenario now needs a baseline record and an error-cause field, so plans and completion reports change shape\nNot-tested: a live generation run against a real project; the contracts and evals are documentary\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"9a320bac5fca7993936d697792d31f11fe8bffdc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/9a320bac5fca7993936d697792d31f11fe8bffdc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/35319ad921cf0a640f5b37050bfc4fa85dd7168c","verification":{"payload":"tree 9a320bac5fca7993936d697792d31f11fe8bffdc\nparent 9e598bf45b61b43c033c66422705274ca917c311\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789669713 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789694608 +0900\n\nRead generated tests against a recorded baseline and cause\n\nFour generator additions, each with a contract test, a deletion-mutation\nguard, and evals on both sides.\n\nStep 5 runs the approved existing tests for the target area once before the\ntracer scenario. A red suite made every later verdict unreadable: a failure\nthat was already there looked like the candidate''s. A green run becomes the\nbaseline; a red run outside the candidate''s surface is recorded and excluded\nfrom V5 attribution; a red run on the candidate''s own route, feature,\nfixture, Page Object, global setup, or stored authentication state returns\nPARTIAL/BLOCKED; and when no approved command covers the area without\nreplaying a persistent write that V5 forbids, the run is skipped, recorded\nas \"baseline not established\", and V5''s suite-context mode is CANNOT_VERIFY.\nNo new status word is introduced.\n\nStep 4 now records an Error-cause signal, because a scenario that only\nproves \"an error appeared\" passes for every cause that reaches the same\nscreen. A product that shows one message for several causes by design is\nrecorded as GENERIC_BY_CONTRACT with its rule; the distinguishing evidence\nis then the V4 request proof, and V3 must not swap causes to falsify it.\n\nScenarios may carry up to three named secondary outcomes - survives a\nreload, side effect proved, error cause distinguished - each recorded as\nselected or skipped. They are extra assertions: V1 keeps one primary\noutcome and V2/V3 falsify only that one.\n\nAn exported manual test case (markdown, CSV, or pasted text from TestRail,\nZephyr, Xray, Qase) can fill Owner/source, and its id is carried into the\ntest title. The export is untrusted data: no command inside it runs, no URL\nis opened, no credential is used, observation beats contradicting steps, and\nthe skill never calls a test-management API.\n\nConstraint: reviewer evidence-status digest changes because upstream-rule-sources.md is inside the reviewed skill\nRejected: a new PARTIAL status for a missing baseline | the V-rule vocabulary is a checked contract; CANNOT_VERIFY on V5 already expresses it\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: medium; every generated scenario now needs a baseline record and an error-cause field, so plans and completion reports change shape\nNot-tested: a live generation run against a real project; the contracts and evals are documentary\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCMXSrTdMiW357HM6QGa0mgh2cpaa7ofP+o+wrJ90zevJzuEKdZotYp1EsJYbilgNm\nov9zEyNAdecCNJdd0eIwY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T03:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/35319ad921cf0a640f5b37050bfc4fa85dd7168c","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDM1MzE5YWQ5MjFjZjBhNjQwZjViMzcwNTBiZmM0ZmE4NWRkNzE2OGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/9e598bf45b61b43c033c66422705274ca917c311","sha":"9e598bf45b61b43c033c66422705274ca917c311","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/9e598bf45b61b43c033c66422705274ca917c311"}],"sha":"35319ad921cf0a640f5b37050bfc4fa85dd7168c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/35319ad921cf0a640f5b37050bfc4fa85dd7168c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/9e598bf45b61b43c033c66422705274ca917c311/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T17:02:03Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:23:28Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Install CI ast-grep from a verified platform package\n\nnpm i -g @ast-grep/cli ran the package''s postinstall, which links the\nnative binary from a platform package. Adding --ignore-scripts alone would\nleave the shim, which prints a message and exits 1. The hosted workflow now\npacks @ast-grep/cli-linux-x64-gnu@0.39.7 with scripts disabled, compares its\nsha512 with the registry integrity pinned in the workflow, extracts the\nbinary, and exports it as E2E_SMELL_AST_GREP_BIN. review.sh requires that\nshape instead of the old npm i -g line.\n\nRejected: npm i -g --ignore-scripts | leaves the exit-1 shim in place of the binary\nConfidence: medium\nScope-risk: low; only the hosted e2e-skills-ci job''s Tier 2 setup\nNot-tested: the hosted ubuntu-latest run; the step was dry-run on macOS up to integrity and extraction, without executing the Linux binary\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n\nCheck the workflow''s new ast-grep install in the gate test\n\ntest-security-gates.py still required the removed `npm i -g\n''@ast-grep/cli@0.39.7''` line and exactly three hardened shell steps, so\nci-local.sh failed on the previous commit. It now requires the packed\nplatform package, its pinned sha512, the absence of any `npm i -g`, and the\nfourth hardened shell step.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none; one CI assertion block\nNot-tested: none\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n\nRun Tier 2 from a sha256-pinned ast-grep download\n\nThe documented opt-in download (E2E_SMELL_NO_AST_GREP_DOWNLOAD=0) could\nnever run: @ast-grep/cli ships a shim that its postinstall replaces with the\nnative binary, so with lifecycle scripts disabled every invocation printed a\nmessage and exited 1, and each opted-in scan ended INCOMPLETE. The fake-npx\ntests could not see it, because a fake npx never resolves the real package.\n\nTier 2 now fetches the platform package, which carries the binary itself,\nthrough the same private pinned npm environment, copies it into private\nstorage, and runs it only when its sha256 matches the value pinned here for\nmacOS arm64/x64 and glibc Linux x64/arm64. An unpinned platform, a musl\nhost, a missing binary, or any digest mismatch records a Tier 2\ninfrastructure failure, so the tier still fails closed instead of running\nunverified bytes. The sanitized-environment test now asserts the refusal and\nthe pinned digests.\n\nConstraint: each pinned digest is the ast-grep binary inside the 0.39.7 platform tarball whose sha512 matched the registry integrity\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; only the opt-in download path, which never worked\nNot-tested: Linux hosts and musl detection; verified end to end on macOS arm64, where the downloaded binary reproduced the installed binary''s Tier 2 output\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"20cfa067277b6700e1296b8cac65f8fe9b707c2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/20cfa067277b6700e1296b8cac65f8fe9b707c2c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/9e598bf45b61b43c033c66422705274ca917c311","verification":{"payload":"tree 20cfa067277b6700e1296b8cac65f8fe9b707c2c\nparent 0c5595142e28c818f8d8ee6b1666921eafc10594\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789664523 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789694608 +0900\n\nInstall CI ast-grep from a verified platform package\n\nnpm i -g @ast-grep/cli ran the package''s postinstall, which links the\nnative binary from a platform package. Adding --ignore-scripts alone would\nleave the shim, which prints a message and exits 1. The hosted workflow now\npacks @ast-grep/cli-linux-x64-gnu@0.39.7 with scripts disabled, compares its\nsha512 with the registry integrity pinned in the workflow, extracts the\nbinary, and exports it as E2E_SMELL_AST_GREP_BIN. review.sh requires that\nshape instead of the old npm i -g line.\n\nRejected: npm i -g --ignore-scripts | leaves the exit-1 shim in place of the binary\nConfidence: medium\nScope-risk: low; only the hosted e2e-skills-ci job''s Tier 2 setup\nNot-tested: the hosted ubuntu-latest run; the step was dry-run on macOS up to integrity and extraction, without executing the Linux binary\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n\nCheck the workflow''s new ast-grep install in the gate test\n\ntest-security-gates.py still required the removed `npm i -g\n''@ast-grep/cli@0.39.7''` line and exactly three hardened shell steps, so\nci-local.sh failed on the previous commit. It now requires the packed\nplatform package, its pinned sha512, the absence of any `npm i -g`, and the\nfourth hardened shell step.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none; one CI assertion block\nNot-tested: none\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n\nRun Tier 2 from a sha256-pinned ast-grep download\n\nThe documented opt-in download (E2E_SMELL_NO_AST_GREP_DOWNLOAD=0) could\nnever run: @ast-grep/cli ships a shim that its postinstall replaces with the\nnative binary, so with lifecycle scripts disabled every invocation printed a\nmessage and exited 1, and each opted-in scan ended INCOMPLETE. The fake-npx\ntests could not see it, because a fake npx never resolves the real package.\n\nTier 2 now fetches the platform package, which carries the binary itself,\nthrough the same private pinned npm environment, copies it into private\nstorage, and runs it only when its sha256 matches the value pinned here for\nmacOS arm64/x64 and glibc Linux x64/arm64. An unpinned platform, a musl\nhost, a missing binary, or any digest mismatch records a Tier 2\ninfrastructure failure, so the tier still fails closed instead of running\nunverified bytes. The sanitized-environment test now asserts the refusal and\nthe pinned digests.\n\nConstraint: each pinned digest is the ast-grep binary inside the 0.39.7 platform tarball whose sha512 matched the registry integrity\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; only the opt-in download path, which never worked\nNot-tested: Linux hosts and musl detection; verified end to end on macOS arm64, where the downloaded binary reproduced the installed binary''s Tier 2 output\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMtk4O1grSJTa1OdCtJ0S4NqP2GPN1CPBeCsw7zXMF/LjuK3mkcJ/342h0zTh6JXGf\nk+DLOL+Vql/k8QaT+6FgA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T03:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/9e598bf45b61b43c033c66422705274ca917c311","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDllNTk4YmY0NWI2MWI0M2MwMzNjNjY0MjI3MDUyNzRjYTkxN2MzMTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/0c5595142e28c818f8d8ee6b1666921eafc10594","sha":"0c5595142e28c818f8d8ee6b1666921eafc10594","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/0c5595142e28c818f8d8ee6b1666921eafc10594"}],"sha":"9e598bf45b61b43c033c66422705274ca917c311","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/9e598bf45b61b43c033c66422705274ca917c311"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/0c5595142e28c818f8d8ee6b1666921eafc10594/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T16:28:39Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:23:28Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Refresh the local install only when pushing HEAD to main\n\nreinstall-skills.sh copies the working tree, not the pushed ref, so the\npre-push hook left the global install on unpushed content whenever a\nfeature branch was pushed or skills/ had uncommitted edits. The hook now\nreads the pushed refs and refreshes only when the checked-out HEAD goes to\nmain with a clean skills/ tree; every other push prints why it skipped.\nThe security and review gates still run on every push. AGENTS.md and\ninstall-hooks.sh describe the new condition.\n\nRejected: gate on the remote ref alone | pushing main from another checkout would still install this working tree\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; contributors who relied on feature-branch pushes refreshing their install must run reinstall-skills.sh directly\nNot-tested: a real git push through the hook; the decision block was exercised in a scratch repository\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"7afc88486f95f84d7a5da5daa5b84c615502ee5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/7afc88486f95f84d7a5da5daa5b84c615502ee5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/0c5595142e28c818f8d8ee6b1666921eafc10594","verification":{"payload":"tree 7afc88486f95f84d7a5da5daa5b84c615502ee5d\nparent 22c14c797b30e6288337dfc79c18ed0ad5e47b64\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789662519 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789694608 +0900\n\nRefresh the local install only when pushing HEAD to main\n\nreinstall-skills.sh copies the working tree, not the pushed ref, so the\npre-push hook left the global install on unpushed content whenever a\nfeature branch was pushed or skills/ had uncommitted edits. The hook now\nreads the pushed refs and refreshes only when the checked-out HEAD goes to\nmain with a clean skills/ tree; every other push prints why it skipped.\nThe security and review gates still run on every push. AGENTS.md and\ninstall-hooks.sh describe the new condition.\n\nRejected: gate on the remote ref alone | pushing main from another checkout would still install this working tree\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; contributors who relied on feature-branch pushes refreshing their install must run reinstall-skills.sh directly\nNot-tested: a real git push through the hook; the decision block was exercised in a scratch repository\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAJmngd5i3eRzIdo3nhKrO56GGZK3Dxhe1nBZ/Nhxa/PkxjLyslUWjTZr+jSpKFmNh\nY/dDtI8yt3dyW+lN3kZws=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T03:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/0c5595142e28c818f8d8ee6b1666921eafc10594","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDBjNTU5NTE0MmUyOGM4MThmOGQ4ZWU2YjE2NjY5MjFlYWZjMTA1OTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/22c14c797b30e6288337dfc79c18ed0ad5e47b64","sha":"22c14c797b30e6288337dfc79c18ed0ad5e47b64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/22c14c797b30e6288337dfc79c18ed0ad5e47b64"}],"sha":"0c5595142e28c818f8d8ee6b1666921eafc10594","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/0c5595142e28c818f8d8ee6b1666921eafc10594"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/22c14c797b30e6288337dfc79c18ed0ad5e47b64/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T16:26:53Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:23:27Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Guard the manual install and qualify evidence claims\n\nThe manual Claude Code install in all four README editions now links\nnothing when any skill name already exists; ln -s onto an existing\ndirectory exits 0 and nests the link, so the old commands kept a stale copy\nwhile claiming to fail. review.sh requires the guard, and its seven\npython3-unavailable checks fail instead of warning.\n\nREADME and the roadmap now say the generated field-review ledger is a lower\nbound: it sees only pull requests whose body names the skill, so the merged\ncalcom/cal.diy#28486 in the curated table is outside it. The AI-reviewer\n13/15 check is labeled raw agreement on 15 items without calibration,\nAGENTS.md describes the Install section as it is, the healer benchmark\nrecords external convergence without importing its figures, and the\nchangelog covers this patch.\n\nConstraint: translation README-CANONICAL-REVISION digests must match README.md in the same commit\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; documentation and review.sh only\nNot-tested: rendered GitHub appearance; translations were written directly, not through translation-mcp\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"ab6cbd65b429793cf571158ce8b98329bf529b26","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/ab6cbd65b429793cf571158ce8b98329bf529b26"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/22c14c797b30e6288337dfc79c18ed0ad5e47b64","verification":{"payload":"tree ab6cbd65b429793cf571158ce8b98329bf529b26\nparent 514459dbbecc01f993ef967d5a6f3c1400ebf386\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789662413 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789694607 +0900\n\nGuard the manual install and qualify evidence claims\n\nThe manual Claude Code install in all four README editions now links\nnothing when any skill name already exists; ln -s onto an existing\ndirectory exits 0 and nests the link, so the old commands kept a stale copy\nwhile claiming to fail. review.sh requires the guard, and its seven\npython3-unavailable checks fail instead of warning.\n\nREADME and the roadmap now say the generated field-review ledger is a lower\nbound: it sees only pull requests whose body names the skill, so the merged\ncalcom/cal.diy#28486 in the curated table is outside it. The AI-reviewer\n13/15 check is labeled raw agreement on 15 items without calibration,\nAGENTS.md describes the Install section as it is, the healer benchmark\nrecords external convergence without importing its figures, and the\nchangelog covers this patch.\n\nConstraint: translation README-CANONICAL-REVISION digests must match README.md in the same commit\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; documentation and review.sh only\nNot-tested: rendered GitHub appearance; translations were written directly, not through translation-mcp\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHpSY+Ul6VpdEo2fj4BzH21+JHPp/DrZCZVAplyNzfIiY47BJtlLG7wwGDTJ+IKp81\nwbcmWq2BCtwWPKLIWiOgE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T03:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/22c14c797b30e6288337dfc79c18ed0ad5e47b64","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDIyYzE0Yzc5N2IzMGU2Mjg4MzM3ZGZjNzljMThlZDBhZDVlNDdiNjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/514459dbbecc01f993ef967d5a6f3c1400ebf386","sha":"514459dbbecc01f993ef967d5a6f3c1400ebf386","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/514459dbbecc01f993ef967d5a6f3c1400ebf386"}],"sha":"22c14c797b30e6288337dfc79c18ed0ad5e47b64","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/22c14c797b30e6288337dfc79c18ed0ad5e47b64"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/514459dbbecc01f993ef967d5a6f3c1400ebf386/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T16:26:53Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:23:27Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Correct debugger and generator command guidance\n\ncypress-debugger''s F13 exclusion now requires the handler to rethrow\nnon-matching errors, matching reviewer #3b: an assertion followed by an\nunconditional return false still swallows every error. The trace CLI\nexample opens the trace before querying it, as Playwright 1.62''s\ntrace actions and trace snapshot take no trace path. playwright-agents.md\nsetup commands use npx --no-install, per the generator''s no-download rule.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; F13 classification changes for handlers that assert and then return false\nNot-tested: trace snapshot -- eval against a real trace; only trace --help output of Playwright 1.62.0 was checked\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"567f7be2da706aba09f26e430b9f6615af9529fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/567f7be2da706aba09f26e430b9f6615af9529fb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/514459dbbecc01f993ef967d5a6f3c1400ebf386","verification":{"payload":"tree 567f7be2da706aba09f26e430b9f6615af9529fb\nparent f40d9a73d830d7b1031a5a38a55b9b11675f3a2f\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789662413 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789694607 +0900\n\nCorrect debugger and generator command guidance\n\ncypress-debugger''s F13 exclusion now requires the handler to rethrow\nnon-matching errors, matching reviewer #3b: an assertion followed by an\nunconditional return false still swallows every error. The trace CLI\nexample opens the trace before querying it, as Playwright 1.62''s\ntrace actions and trace snapshot take no trace path. playwright-agents.md\nsetup commands use npx --no-install, per the generator''s no-download rule.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; F13 classification changes for handlers that assert and then return false\nNot-tested: trace snapshot -- eval against a real trace; only trace --help output of Playwright 1.62.0 was checked\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQGI2EGtkoMk2Fha68uTpLfZ997fdBM+EXXurKZ9ZV757rsjCFTG/hWumc/zUWHpC3L\nUfqlhNudAo97CXT7XGtQo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T03:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/514459dbbecc01f993ef967d5a6f3c1400ebf386","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDUxNDQ1OWRiYmVjYzAxZjk5M2VmOTY3ZDVhNmYzYzE0MDBlYmYzODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f40d9a73d830d7b1031a5a38a55b9b11675f3a2f","sha":"f40d9a73d830d7b1031a5a38a55b9b11675f3a2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f40d9a73d830d7b1031a5a38a55b9b11675f3a2f"}],"sha":"514459dbbecc01f993ef967d5a6f3c1400ebf386","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/514459dbbecc01f993ef967d5a6f3c1400ebf386"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f40d9a73d830d7b1031a5a38a55b9b11675f3a2f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T16:26:53Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:23:27Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Fix reviewer scanner lexing and contract drift\n\nSeventeen awk lexers and the Python conditional-discovery port had no\nregex-literal state, so a quote inside /don''t/ opened a string that hid\nlater #4f P0 findings, #16 and #5a candidates, and JUSTIFIED markers. They\nnow use lexical_target_line''s regex-start rule with byte-safe comparisons,\nand the focused-test lexer''s unreachable regex state is entered. #7 now\nreports test.describe.serial.only and parallel.only; a JUSTIFIED marker\ncovers chain lines after an option object; #8a skips the head of a\nmulti-line member chain; invalid E2E_SMELL_FAIL_ON is rejected before\nscanning; the INCOMPLETE summary names each rule once.\n\nThe reviewer docs now agree with themselves and the scanner: #4i scopes\nproof to the test''s execution path, #10c lists all exemptions, sub-ID lists\ninclude #4k and #10d-#10f, the Cypress timeout: 0 wording no longer implies\nscanner coverage, and evals E1/E12 cite the right lines and tiers. The\nholdout v3 evidence status records the resulting skill digest.\n\nConstraint: evidence-status.json current_skill_sha256 must equal the e2e-reviewer skill digest in the same commit\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: medium; finding counts change where regex literals, option-object chains, or chain heads occur\nNot-tested: awk implementations other than macOS one-true-awk and the CI Ubuntu awk\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"de6cd0279923bcadbefe1f7eea471dfcba9f5de7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/de6cd0279923bcadbefe1f7eea471dfcba9f5de7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/f40d9a73d830d7b1031a5a38a55b9b11675f3a2f","verification":{"payload":"tree de6cd0279923bcadbefe1f7eea471dfcba9f5de7\nparent bf018d96051edf2c9024f92a9316b55de368ad86\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789662413 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789694607 +0900\n\nFix reviewer scanner lexing and contract drift\n\nSeventeen awk lexers and the Python conditional-discovery port had no\nregex-literal state, so a quote inside /don''t/ opened a string that hid\nlater #4f P0 findings, #16 and #5a candidates, and JUSTIFIED markers. They\nnow use lexical_target_line''s regex-start rule with byte-safe comparisons,\nand the focused-test lexer''s unreachable regex state is entered. #7 now\nreports test.describe.serial.only and parallel.only; a JUSTIFIED marker\ncovers chain lines after an option object; #8a skips the head of a\nmulti-line member chain; invalid E2E_SMELL_FAIL_ON is rejected before\nscanning; the INCOMPLETE summary names each rule once.\n\nThe reviewer docs now agree with themselves and the scanner: #4i scopes\nproof to the test''s execution path, #10c lists all exemptions, sub-ID lists\ninclude #4k and #10d-#10f, the Cypress timeout: 0 wording no longer implies\nscanner coverage, and evals E1/E12 cite the right lines and tiers. The\nholdout v3 evidence status records the resulting skill digest.\n\nConstraint: evidence-status.json current_skill_sha256 must equal the e2e-reviewer skill digest in the same commit\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: medium; finding counts change where regex literals, option-object chains, or chain heads occur\nNot-tested: awk implementations other than macOS one-true-awk and the CI Ubuntu awk\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQJoWiYNqfqxBEKCFxU6HcXOw/RMN0plgPc0lnDZAknS6BGkzupwnUoi4RrnVeyKs+9\ndVgTwcao7wFcTb37/DKQQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T03:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f40d9a73d830d7b1031a5a38a55b9b11675f3a2f","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGY0MGQ5YTczZDgzMGQ3YjEwMzFhNWEzOGE1NWI5YjExNjc1ZjNhMmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/bf018d96051edf2c9024f92a9316b55de368ad86","sha":"bf018d96051edf2c9024f92a9316b55de368ad86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/bf018d96051edf2c9024f92a9316b55de368ad86"}],"sha":"f40d9a73d830d7b1031a5a38a55b9b11675f3a2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f40d9a73d830d7b1031a5a38a55b9b11675f3a2f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/bf018d96051edf2c9024f92a9316b55de368ad86/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T16:26:53Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:23:27Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Harden secret, parity, and eval-runner gates\n\nThe secret scanner now matches Anthropic API/OAuth tokens, npm access\ntokens, and GitHub OAuth/app/refresh tokens; the OpenAI-style pattern\nstopped at the hyphen after sk-ant, so the credential the live holdout\nrunner stages could pass the pre-push gate. The drift smoke test now\nrequires review.sh to exit non-zero on each mutation instead of only\nprinting the expected message. The holdout runner refuses an --output that\nnames one of its inputs, because the initial INCOMPLETE report is written\nbefore the first model call, and its --version probe runs with an empty\nprivate HOME. install-hooks.sh no longer replaces an existing\ncore.hooksPath, and ci-local.sh warns when ast-grep is unavailable so a\nTier-3-only self-scan is visible.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; a repository that already contains a matching token shape now fails the security gate\nNot-tested: hosted CI; ci-local.sh was run on this host with ast-grep present, so the warning path was checked only by reading\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE","tree":{"sha":"26d5f5d087a414faf149fb7a1404d7e511041e68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/26d5f5d087a414faf149fb7a1404d7e511041e68"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/bf018d96051edf2c9024f92a9316b55de368ad86","verification":{"payload":"tree 26d5f5d087a414faf149fb7a1404d7e511041e68\nparent 24a1d33aa8cf7863d63e8f298674b3251bd7a8b3\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789662413 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789694607 +0900\n\nHarden secret, parity, and eval-runner gates\n\nThe secret scanner now matches Anthropic API/OAuth tokens, npm access\ntokens, and GitHub OAuth/app/refresh tokens; the OpenAI-style pattern\nstopped at the hyphen after sk-ant, so the credential the live holdout\nrunner stages could pass the pre-push gate. The drift smoke test now\nrequires review.sh to exit non-zero on each mutation instead of only\nprinting the expected message. The holdout runner refuses an --output that\nnames one of its inputs, because the initial INCOMPLETE report is written\nbefore the first model call, and its --version probe runs with an empty\nprivate HOME. install-hooks.sh no longer replaces an existing\ncore.hooksPath, and ci-local.sh warns when ast-grep is unavailable so a\nTier-3-only self-scan is visible.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: low; a repository that already contains a matching token shape now fails the security gate\nNot-tested: hosted CI; ci-local.sh was run on this host with ast-grep present, so the warning path was checked only by reading\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01K8ioip1UShGozdJWH3zuXE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFoq+a4LH3SSRllKiHVtRDRfMYMmw5FPdNmlv764RBL/l7OYuXk11kzuXuNJGkSOUU\nyyPmYdJHBmYIAQN8my0gg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T03:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/bf018d96051edf2c9024f92a9316b55de368ad86","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGJmMDE4ZDk2MDUxZWRmMmM5MDI0ZjkyYTkzMTZiNTVkZTM2OGFkODY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/24a1d33aa8cf7863d63e8f298674b3251bd7a8b3","sha":"24a1d33aa8cf7863d63e8f298674b3251bd7a8b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/24a1d33aa8cf7863d63e8f298674b3251bd7a8b3"}],"sha":"bf018d96051edf2c9024f92a9316b55de368ad86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/bf018d96051edf2c9024f92a9316b55de368ad86"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/24a1d33aa8cf7863d63e8f298674b3251bd7a8b3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T14:22:23Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:23:27Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Fix confirmed findings from independent product reviews\n\nIndependent product-review attempts on the four skills reported 21 Medium\nfindings. Each was re-checked against the current code before any change:\nten were confirmed and fixed, four were already handled or not defects, and\nfour product-policy questions were settled by the operator.\n\nGenerator: approve the project-local CLI probe before running it, align the\nPython floor wording, discover configs the way Playwright loads them, give\nV6-blocked candidates a reporting path, and define the snippet variables.\nDebuggers: route probe and list commands through the empty-environment\ngate, run the F1/F7 probe only after the execution safety and trust gates,\nstop counting interrupted results as unexpected, reject boolean retry\nindexes, reject non-finite Cypress floats, name the supported reporter\nrange in the fail-closed outcome rejection, and publish a failing local\nPlaywright run only when its report validates. Reviewer: fail closed when a\nsource lexer invocation fails instead of silently dropping framework scope,\nand make the symlink preflight abort actionable without adding an override.\n\nThe healer benchmark test hashed live product files against frozen\npreparation digests, so any product edit failed CI. Verify those five\nsurfaces against a content-addressed snapshot of the preparation-commit\nbytes instead, keep the live check for benchmark-owned fixtures, and compare\nthe snapshot with git blobs when the preparation commit is available. The\nprotocol and freeze records are unchanged. Refresh the reviewer holdout v3\nevidence-status skill digest for the new reviewer bytes.\n\nConstraint: frozen benchmark protocols, freeze records, and digests unchanged\nRejected: an allowlist knob for the symlink preflight; the operator chose guidance only\nRejected: relaxing the Playwright outcome gate to warn; kept fail-closed\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: debugger publisher now accepts exit status 1 for any child whose JSON report validates\nNot-tested: hosted Linux CI; Playwright reporter releases between 1.55.1, 1.60.0, and 1.62.1\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HWJxAWRg2deEnx8H4katR9\n\nUpdate README benchmark status for product-review v11\n\nReplace the stale \"v10 is frozen but not run\" sentence in the English README\nand its three translations: v11 joins the failed robustness gates, v10 is\nsuperseded after one of its three attempts by v11 on the same frozen review\ninput, and v1-v11 remain legacy evidence rather than release gates. Refresh\nthe translations'' canonical README revision digests.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none; one status sentence per README and digest lines\nNot-tested: rendered appearance on GitHub; translations were edited without translation-mcp\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HWJxAWRg2deEnx8H4katR9","tree":{"sha":"c6591c1c50bdb4de173828113d0e18c9a3c705d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/c6591c1c50bdb4de173828113d0e18c9a3c705d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/24a1d33aa8cf7863d63e8f298674b3251bd7a8b3","verification":{"payload":"tree c6591c1c50bdb4de173828113d0e18c9a3c705d1\nparent a607fc9329c57659d1a39ec51f5fef3859cda22c\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789654943 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789694607 +0900\n\nFix confirmed findings from independent product reviews\n\nIndependent product-review attempts on the four skills reported 21 Medium\nfindings. Each was re-checked against the current code before any change:\nten were confirmed and fixed, four were already handled or not defects, and\nfour product-policy questions were settled by the operator.\n\nGenerator: approve the project-local CLI probe before running it, align the\nPython floor wording, discover configs the way Playwright loads them, give\nV6-blocked candidates a reporting path, and define the snippet variables.\nDebuggers: route probe and list commands through the empty-environment\ngate, run the F1/F7 probe only after the execution safety and trust gates,\nstop counting interrupted results as unexpected, reject boolean retry\nindexes, reject non-finite Cypress floats, name the supported reporter\nrange in the fail-closed outcome rejection, and publish a failing local\nPlaywright run only when its report validates. Reviewer: fail closed when a\nsource lexer invocation fails instead of silently dropping framework scope,\nand make the symlink preflight abort actionable without adding an override.\n\nThe healer benchmark test hashed live product files against frozen\npreparation digests, so any product edit failed CI. Verify those five\nsurfaces against a content-addressed snapshot of the preparation-commit\nbytes instead, keep the live check for benchmark-owned fixtures, and compare\nthe snapshot with git blobs when the preparation commit is available. The\nprotocol and freeze records are unchanged. Refresh the reviewer holdout v3\nevidence-status skill digest for the new reviewer bytes.\n\nConstraint: frozen benchmark protocols, freeze records, and digests unchanged\nRejected: an allowlist knob for the symlink preflight; the operator chose guidance only\nRejected: relaxing the Playwright outcome gate to warn; kept fail-closed\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: debugger publisher now accepts exit status 1 for any child whose JSON report validates\nNot-tested: hosted Linux CI; Playwright reporter releases between 1.55.1, 1.60.0, and 1.62.1\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HWJxAWRg2deEnx8H4katR9\n\nUpdate README benchmark status for product-review v11\n\nReplace the stale \"v10 is frozen but not run\" sentence in the English README\nand its three translations: v11 joins the failed robustness gates, v10 is\nsuperseded after one of its three attempts by v11 on the same frozen review\ninput, and v1-v11 remain legacy evidence rather than release gates. Refresh\nthe translations'' canonical README revision digests.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none; one status sentence per README and digest lines\nNot-tested: rendered appearance on GitHub; translations were edited without translation-mcp\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HWJxAWRg2deEnx8H4katR9\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIwE4WcY81wSB4Nk8kKGMzCD/fhaQb06Z6oVYxBOjPWWd4ImvOC6tOwq23/WSWf4Gw\ngft0YuhZ6ReF/jDnAd0wM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T03:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/24a1d33aa8cf7863d63e8f298674b3251bd7a8b3","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDI0YTFkMzNhYThjZjc4NjNkNjNlOGYyOTg2NzRiMzI1MWJkN2E4YjM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/a607fc9329c57659d1a39ec51f5fef3859cda22c","sha":"a607fc9329c57659d1a39ec51f5fef3859cda22c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/a607fc9329c57659d1a39ec51f5fef3859cda22c"}],"sha":"24a1d33aa8cf7863d63e8f298674b3251bd7a8b3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/24a1d33aa8cf7863d63e8f298674b3251bd7a8b3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/a607fc9329c57659d1a39ec51f5fef3859cda22c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T09:28:55Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:23:27Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Supersede product-review v10 with a v11 completion successor\n\nIndependent product-review v10 consumed its first attempt (claude-opus-5,\nvalid FAIL at 88.67, C0/H0/M8, target V8-T4 reopened mechanically) and then\ncould never reserve r2 or r3. The frozen runner wrote\nsuperseded_phase_record_sha256 into every integrity snapshot, while the\nfrozen evidence validator built its expectation without that key and\ncompared the whole dictionary, so the pre-reservation archive check rejected\nr1. The v10 unit suite built its integrity fixture by hand from the\nvalidator''s key list and never saw a runner-produced snapshot.\n\nRecord v10 as SUPERSEDED_AFTER_MEASURED_INFRASTRUCTURE_FINDING and freeze\nv11 as a completion successor. v11 inherits the v10 packet, prompt, rubric,\nremediation ledger, model catalog, host matrix, model order, and exact\nClaude Code 2.1.220 pin by digest, carries the consumed r1 as schedule\nindex 0, and runs only the two never-reserved slots as fresh attempts. Only\nharness bytes change: one INTEGRITY_KEYS contract shared by runner and\nvalidator, a protocol-bound 1800 s timeout recorded per attempt, a\npre-reservation integrity and chronology check, runner/validator parity for\noversized integer literals and clock steps, accepted post-raw recovery, and\nclean errors instead of validator tracebacks. The gate is predetermined FAIL\nunder the FAIL-first rule, and every post-hoc design choice is disclosed in\nthe protocol and the supersession record.\n\nFrozen v10 bytes are unchanged. The v11 suite pins the original defect\nagainst the frozen v10 validator, proves integrity key-set parity with\nmutation checks, and drives fresh attempts through the real run_review.\n\nConstraint: frozen v10 files and pinned shared tools must stay byte-identical\nRejected: three fresh v11 attempts on the same prompt; a re-roll after a known FAIL\nRejected: re-freezing on v1.16.3 surfaces; changes the evidence object and needs post-hoc caps\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: README still says v10 is frozen but not run; deferred until r2/r3 results exist\nNot-tested: live r2/r3 model calls; Linux hosted CI run of the v11 suite\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HWJxAWRg2deEnx8H4katR9\n\nRecord completed v11 product-review attempts\n\nRun the two fresh v11 attempts from the frozen worktree at 7299588 with the\npinned Claude Code 2.1.220 binary. v11-r2 (claude-fable-5) passed on its own\nat 90.5 with 0 Critical, 0 High, and 5 Medium findings and reopened no\nbound target. v11-r3 (claude-opus-5) failed at 87.67 with 0 Critical,\n0 High, and 8 Medium findings and reopened V8-T4 mechanically through a\nMedium false_positive_control finding in scan.sh, not a recurrence of the\nhistorical defect. The evidence wrapper reports FAIL, 3/3: the archive is\ncomplete and the gate is FAIL, as the carried r1 had already fixed under the\nFAIL-first rule.\n\nUpdate STATUS and CHANGELOG with the per-attempt results. README still\ndescribes v10 as frozen but not run and is updated at merge time.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none; harness and frozen inputs unchanged since 7299588\nNot-tested: hosted Linux CI for the completed archive state\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HWJxAWRg2deEnx8H4katR9","tree":{"sha":"c5475a5902bd2fec9f50d4e6f9c056c3f1e15684","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/c5475a5902bd2fec9f50d4e6f9c056c3f1e15684"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/a607fc9329c57659d1a39ec51f5fef3859cda22c","verification":{"payload":"tree c5475a5902bd2fec9f50d4e6f9c056c3f1e15684\nparent 27f22e175a7c43ffdfa5631a95c63c68ff9995d2\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789637335 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789694607 +0900\n\nSupersede product-review v10 with a v11 completion successor\n\nIndependent product-review v10 consumed its first attempt (claude-opus-5,\nvalid FAIL at 88.67, C0/H0/M8, target V8-T4 reopened mechanically) and then\ncould never reserve r2 or r3. The frozen runner wrote\nsuperseded_phase_record_sha256 into every integrity snapshot, while the\nfrozen evidence validator built its expectation without that key and\ncompared the whole dictionary, so the pre-reservation archive check rejected\nr1. The v10 unit suite built its integrity fixture by hand from the\nvalidator''s key list and never saw a runner-produced snapshot.\n\nRecord v10 as SUPERSEDED_AFTER_MEASURED_INFRASTRUCTURE_FINDING and freeze\nv11 as a completion successor. v11 inherits the v10 packet, prompt, rubric,\nremediation ledger, model catalog, host matrix, model order, and exact\nClaude Code 2.1.220 pin by digest, carries the consumed r1 as schedule\nindex 0, and runs only the two never-reserved slots as fresh attempts. Only\nharness bytes change: one INTEGRITY_KEYS contract shared by runner and\nvalidator, a protocol-bound 1800 s timeout recorded per attempt, a\npre-reservation integrity and chronology check, runner/validator parity for\noversized integer literals and clock steps, accepted post-raw recovery, and\nclean errors instead of validator tracebacks. The gate is predetermined FAIL\nunder the FAIL-first rule, and every post-hoc design choice is disclosed in\nthe protocol and the supersession record.\n\nFrozen v10 bytes are unchanged. The v11 suite pins the original defect\nagainst the frozen v10 validator, proves integrity key-set parity with\nmutation checks, and drives fresh attempts through the real run_review.\n\nConstraint: frozen v10 files and pinned shared tools must stay byte-identical\nRejected: three fresh v11 attempts on the same prompt; a re-roll after a known FAIL\nRejected: re-freezing on v1.16.3 surfaces; changes the evidence object and needs post-hoc caps\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: README still says v10 is frozen but not run; deferred until r2/r3 results exist\nNot-tested: live r2/r3 model calls; Linux hosted CI run of the v11 suite\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HWJxAWRg2deEnx8H4katR9\n\nRecord completed v11 product-review attempts\n\nRun the two fresh v11 attempts from the frozen worktree at 7299588 with the\npinned Claude Code 2.1.220 binary. v11-r2 (claude-fable-5) passed on its own\nat 90.5 with 0 Critical, 0 High, and 5 Medium findings and reopened no\nbound target. v11-r3 (claude-opus-5) failed at 87.67 with 0 Critical,\n0 High, and 8 Medium findings and reopened V8-T4 mechanically through a\nMedium false_positive_control finding in scan.sh, not a recurrence of the\nhistorical defect. The evidence wrapper reports FAIL, 3/3: the archive is\ncomplete and the gate is FAIL, as the carried r1 had already fixed under the\nFAIL-first rule.\n\nUpdate STATUS and CHANGELOG with the per-attempt results. README still\ndescribes v10 as frozen but not run and is updated at merge time.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none; harness and frozen inputs unchanged since 7299588\nNot-tested: hosted Linux CI for the completed archive state\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HWJxAWRg2deEnx8H4katR9\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOHzJ3BO2PBF9OWz3JApVhOAKQadRMMuUyoZ2REQmcnZxjWLDe091GMOz1YFMy+kvo\npVWExkfQ2m9QwOwmVZjw0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T03:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/a607fc9329c57659d1a39ec51f5fef3859cda22c","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGE2MDdmYzkzMjljNTc2NTlkMWEzOWVjNTFmNWZlZjM4NTljZGEyMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/27f22e175a7c43ffdfa5631a95c63c68ff9995d2","sha":"27f22e175a7c43ffdfa5631a95c63c68ff9995d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/27f22e175a7c43ffdfa5631a95c63c68ff9995d2"}],"sha":"a607fc9329c57659d1a39ec51f5fef3859cda22c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/a607fc9329c57659d1a39ec51f5fef3859cda22c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/27f22e175a7c43ffdfa5631a95c63c68ff9995d2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T01:23:03Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-18T01:23:26Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Accept pinned no-wrapper holdout reports in the comparator\n\nThe runner allows no-wrapper live runs for its pinned built-in corpus and\nprotocol digests, including the v5 and v6 \"public-development\" corpus, but\nvalidate_provenance accepted no-wrapper reports only for the literal \"public\"\nlabel. Every v5/v6 report therefore became a report_integrity_error and both\ncomparison modes returned INCONCLUSIVE regardless of results. The arm gate\nalso named only reviewer-holdout-v5, so --compare-arms raised for v6 even\nthough its arm contract is byte-identical.\n\nAccept a no-wrapper report only when its corpus and protocol digests match a\nrunner PINNED_LIVE_INPUTS pair, and gate arm comparison on the runner''s\nARM_COMPARISON_PROTOCOL_IDS. Unpinned non-public reports still require the\nexternal-wrapper provenance. Existing tests mocked recompute_report, which\nhid the defect; the new tests call validate_provenance directly and fail on\nthe previous comparator.\n\nThis changes decision code before any v5 measured cell and before the fresh\nv6 matrix. The frozen protocol JSON, corpus, and evaluator digests are\nunchanged.\n\nConstraint: frozen v5/v6 protocol bytes and version policies must not change\nRejected: cutting a v7 protocol; the defect is in comparator code, not the protocol\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: v4 public-pre-publication reports are now also accepted without a wrapper, matching the runner\nNot-tested: comparison of real live v5/v6 reports; none exist yet\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HWJxAWRg2deEnx8H4katR9","tree":{"sha":"3cd119285aff70050535b81ad17669cccb09176f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/3cd119285aff70050535b81ad17669cccb09176f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/27f22e175a7c43ffdfa5631a95c63c68ff9995d2","verification":{"payload":"tree 3cd119285aff70050535b81ad17669cccb09176f\nparent 8ea32c99c3c52e113fce2f6d6e0a3f1cb14ae959\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789608183 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789694606 +0900\n\nAccept pinned no-wrapper holdout reports in the comparator\n\nThe runner allows no-wrapper live runs for its pinned built-in corpus and\nprotocol digests, including the v5 and v6 \"public-development\" corpus, but\nvalidate_provenance accepted no-wrapper reports only for the literal \"public\"\nlabel. Every v5/v6 report therefore became a report_integrity_error and both\ncomparison modes returned INCONCLUSIVE regardless of results. The arm gate\nalso named only reviewer-holdout-v5, so --compare-arms raised for v6 even\nthough its arm contract is byte-identical.\n\nAccept a no-wrapper report only when its corpus and protocol digests match a\nrunner PINNED_LIVE_INPUTS pair, and gate arm comparison on the runner''s\nARM_COMPARISON_PROTOCOL_IDS. Unpinned non-public reports still require the\nexternal-wrapper provenance. Existing tests mocked recompute_report, which\nhid the defect; the new tests call validate_provenance directly and fail on\nthe previous comparator.\n\nThis changes decision code before any v5 measured cell and before the fresh\nv6 matrix. The frozen protocol JSON, corpus, and evaluator digests are\nunchanged.\n\nConstraint: frozen v5/v6 protocol bytes and version policies must not change\nRejected: cutting a v7 protocol; the defect is in comparator code, not the protocol\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: v4 public-pre-publication reports are now also accepted without a wrapper, matching the runner\nNot-tested: comparison of real live v5/v6 reports; none exist yet\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01HWJxAWRg2deEnx8H4katR9\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOo3ajyQNDDj9JYsNGmJOJbV63yRqL4qzQi2SYKZf8ZtbbNF9cytWxhJ2U6X3A+nEH\n0XMlm85OgJtxFstf4mLQA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-18T03:54:19Z"}},"committer":{"ava