ch SKILL.md entrypoint.\n\nUpdate the contract tests to validate the moved content without weakening the\nsubstantive assertions.\n\nConstraint: preserve standalone Playwright and Cypress skill packaging\n\nRejected: a shared cross-skill reference that standalone installs could miss\n\nConfidence: high\n\nScope-risk: agents must follow the explicit conditional reference links\n\nNot-tested: live GitHub artifact download or target-project reproduction\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCubDZWZ91llsjlBeXeRQ0fKFD+L9AkVjEFRJi9O4atMU3S1DU1A7/uZLhVccwd4H6\nnWQFQCYtJ+TXZB1HO6PA4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T13:15:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/49c8eefce2b42a80350e85c64f05a2b88c02ea60","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDQ5YzhlZWZjZTJiNDJhODAzNTBlODVjNjRmMDVhMmI4OGMwMmVhNjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/da8da3c59dcd513a1f648ddd597d7648a07bc3e5","sha":"da8da3c59dcd513a1f648ddd597d7648a07bc3e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/da8da3c59dcd513a1f648ddd597d7648a07bc3e5"}],"sha":"49c8eefce2b42a80350e85c64f05a2b88c02ea60","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/49c8eefce2b42a80350e85c64f05a2b88c02ea60"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/da8da3c59dcd513a1f648ddd597d7648a07bc3e5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T07:57:21Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T07:57:21Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Reverse finding_verification to INLINE_DEFAULT per confirmation-v1 revision 6\n\nconfirmation-v1''s protocol-valid revision-6 run (16 fresh cases, 3\nrepetitions, real delegation transport, 96 cells; two genuine case-oracle\ndefects found and fixed live across six revisions) found zero stable\nnamed-delegation wins in every finding_verification stratum, including\ncross-file/config-dependent -- the exact stratum the original pilot''s\nSELECTIVE_DELEGATE read was based on. Per confirmation-score.json''s own\nreviewer.upheld: false and the decision rule''s own \"at least two\nindependent decisive cases\" bar, SELECTIVE_DELEGATE does not hold on a\nfresh case set. failure_classification''s INLINE_DEFAULT was independently\nupheld by the same run (debugger.upheld: true) and is unchanged.\n\ne2e-reviewer/SKILL.md''s finding-verification delegation block is rewritten\nto the same INLINE_DEFAULT shape both debugger skills already use: inline\nby default in every stratum, named/native delegation available only when\nthe inline result is itself uncertain, inline authoritative on\ndisagreement. scripts/ci/test-routing-contract.py''s reviewer check was\nrewritten to match (RED confirmed against the SELECTIVE_DELEGATE wording\nfirst, GREEN after the edit); its own negative fixtures were extended\nwith the literal SELECTIVE_DELEGATE-era wording as an additional\nknown-bad case that must be rejected.\n\nCaught and fixed one real mistake before this commit: an earlier pass at\nbenchmarks/subagent-routing-v1/README.md''s write-up computed per-case\noutcomes from the raw per-cell PASS/FAIL status and misread two cases\n(CFV-07, CFC-08) as named-arm regressions. Cross-checking against\nconfirmation-score.json''s own authoritative per-case fields\n(named_only_advantage / inline_only_advantage / stable_disagreement, all\nfalse for both cases) showed no regression occurred -- the raw cell\nstatus reflects a stricter per-repetition criterion (evidentiary\ncompleteness) that can diverge from whether the majority verdict actually\nmatched the oracle, which is what the decision rule is written against.\nThe README now cites the scorer''s own fields directly and documents the\ncorrection rather than silently fixing it.\n\nAlso fixed a real drift-smoke regression the wording change introduced:\nthe new delegation paragraph used the literal string \"NEEDS-CONTEXT\"\ntwice (once naming the verdict list, once describing the delegation\ntrigger), which made test-parity.sh''s SP3 mutation case (deleting\nNEEDS-CONTEXT from the verdict list specifically) fail to reproduce a\ndetectable drift, since the term still appeared elsewhere in the file.\nReworded the trigger description to not repeat the literal token.\n\nPer the user''s explicit direction, the bundle version stays at 1.16.2\n(not bumped to 1.16.3) since nothing here has been pushed yet --\nCHANGELOG.md''s [1.16.2] entry was rewritten in place to describe the\nfinal, confirmed state directly rather than layering a second entry on\ntop of the now-superseded SELECTIVE_DELEGATE description.\n\nNever touched: the inline fallback itself, verdict vocabulary, F1-F15,\npattern IDs/severities, SP1-SP6 parity, generator V6, framework scope,\ninstallation behavior.\n\nConfidence: high on the wording matching the confirmation-v1 result and\non the corrected README/CHANGELOG accuracy (independently re-verified\nagainst confirmation-score.json''s own fields, not just the earlier ad hoc\nrecomputation). Medium on whether this reversed result itself will\ngeneralize further -- that is exactly what a future re-confirmation would\ntest, same as before.\n\nScope-risk: skills/e2e-reviewer/SKILL.md content change (Tier 1) --\nconfirmed via CI that SP1-SP6 hold and the drift smoke test''s own mutation\ncases still correctly detect a dropped verdict term.\n\nNot-tested: n/a.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BYDNypNkcHtmMdwoFBidxE","tree":{"sha":"bee5b31b4fcc9c1fc7c25667e96de583b979189e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/bee5b31b4fcc9c1fc7c25667e96de583b979189e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/da8da3c59dcd513a1f648ddd597d7648a07bc3e5","verification":{"payload":"tree bee5b31b4fcc9c1fc7c25667e96de583b979189e\nparent c646425123c4429a48e00d80f5d216cb592656bd\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789372641 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789372641 +0900\n\nReverse finding_verification to INLINE_DEFAULT per confirmation-v1 revision 6\n\nconfirmation-v1''s protocol-valid revision-6 run (16 fresh cases, 3\nrepetitions, real delegation transport, 96 cells; two genuine case-oracle\ndefects found and fixed live across six revisions) found zero stable\nnamed-delegation wins in every finding_verification stratum, including\ncross-file/config-dependent -- the exact stratum the original pilot''s\nSELECTIVE_DELEGATE read was based on. Per confirmation-score.json''s own\nreviewer.upheld: false and the decision rule''s own \"at least two\nindependent decisive cases\" bar, SELECTIVE_DELEGATE does not hold on a\nfresh case set. failure_classification''s INLINE_DEFAULT was independently\nupheld by the same run (debugger.upheld: true) and is unchanged.\n\ne2e-reviewer/SKILL.md''s finding-verification delegation block is rewritten\nto the same INLINE_DEFAULT shape both debugger skills already use: inline\nby default in every stratum, named/native delegation available only when\nthe inline result is itself uncertain, inline authoritative on\ndisagreement. scripts/ci/test-routing-contract.py''s reviewer check was\nrewritten to match (RED confirmed against the SELECTIVE_DELEGATE wording\nfirst, GREEN after the edit); its own negative fixtures were extended\nwith the literal SELECTIVE_DELEGATE-era wording as an additional\nknown-bad case that must be rejected.\n\nCaught and fixed one real mistake before this commit: an earlier pass at\nbenchmarks/subagent-routing-v1/README.md''s write-up computed per-case\noutcomes from the raw per-cell PASS/FAIL status and misread two cases\n(CFV-07, CFC-08) as named-arm regressions. Cross-checking against\nconfirmation-score.json''s own authoritative per-case fields\n(named_only_advantage / inline_only_advantage / stable_disagreement, all\nfalse for both cases) showed no regression occurred -- the raw cell\nstatus reflects a stricter per-repetition criterion (evidentiary\ncompleteness) that can diverge from whether the majority verdict actually\nmatched the oracle, which is what the decision rule is written against.\nThe README now cites the scorer''s own fields directly and documents the\ncorrection rather than silently fixing it.\n\nAlso fixed a real drift-smoke regression the wording change introduced:\nthe new delegation paragraph used the literal string \"NEEDS-CONTEXT\"\ntwice (once naming the verdict list, once describing the delegation\ntrigger), which made test-parity.sh''s SP3 mutation case (deleting\nNEEDS-CONTEXT from the verdict list specifically) fail to reproduce a\ndetectable drift, since the term still appeared elsewhere in the file.\nReworded the trigger description to not repeat the literal token.\n\nPer the user''s explicit direction, the bundle version stays at 1.16.2\n(not bumped to 1.16.3) since nothing here has been pushed yet --\nCHANGELOG.md''s [1.16.2] entry was rewritten in place to describe the\nfinal, confirmed state directly rather than layering a second entry on\ntop of the now-superseded SELECTIVE_DELEGATE description.\n\nNever touched: the inline fallback itself, verdict vocabulary, F1-F15,\npattern IDs/severities, SP1-SP6 parity, generator V6, framework scope,\ninstallation behavior.\n\nConfidence: high on the wording matching the confirmation-v1 result and\non the corrected README/CHANGELOG accuracy (independently re-verified\nagainst confirmation-score.json''s own fields, not just the earlier ad hoc\nrecomputation). Medium on whether this reversed result itself will\ngeneralize further -- that is exactly what a future re-confirmation would\ntest, same as before.\n\nScope-risk: skills/e2e-reviewer/SKILL.md content change (Tier 1) --\nconfirmed via CI that SP1-SP6 hold and the drift smoke test''s own mutation\ncases still correctly detect a dropped verdict term.\n\nNot-tested: n/a.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BYDNypNkcHtmMdwoFBidxE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQElRk09U55b2iBxsApav/d6sa7Se7r4tdlOhcaPtVHEgXcpcyfcutEugcfn7YKrThI\nhxFbEbQXH2MaPtbvKuOQQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T13:15:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/da8da3c59dcd513a1f648ddd597d7648a07bc3e5","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGRhOGRhM2M1OWRjZDUxM2ExZjY0OGRkZDU5N2Q3NjQ4YTA3YmMzZTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/c646425123c4429a48e00d80f5d216cb592656bd","sha":"c646425123c4429a48e00d80f5d216cb592656bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c646425123c4429a48e00d80f5d216cb592656bd"}],"sha":"da8da3c59dcd513a1f648ddd597d7648a07bc3e5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/da8da3c59dcd513a1f648ddd597d7648a07bc3e5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c646425123c4429a48e00d80f5d216cb592656bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T12:06:49Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T12:06:49Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"benchmarks: run the change boundary''s required full-scale confirmation (revisions 2-6)\n\nsubagent-routing-v1''s change boundary requires a separately frozen case\nset, run at full rigor, before a wording change based on the original\npilot can be treated as confirmed rather than provisional. This commit\nis that run, squashed from its 16 intermediate freeze/smoke/correct/\nrecord commits (revisions 2 through 6) into one.\n\nDesign: 16 fresh cases in a new domain, 3 repetitions each, claude.inline\nvs claude.named, real delegation transport -- 96 measured cells covering\nall three finding_verification strata (clear, same-file, cross-file/\nconfig-dependent) and both new debugger-side rules (a bounded delegation\ntrigger on inline uncertainty, inline-wins-on-disagreement\nreconciliation).\n\nTwo real case-oracle defects were found and fixed live, the same\nstandard the original pilot held itself to:\n  - Revision 4: CFC-01 and CFC-06 required an overly brittle evidence-line\n    number that didn''t match the actual decisive line in the fixture.\n  - Revisions 5-6: CFV-05, CFC-04, and CFC-05 had a reversed-sign oracle\n    (correct model output was being scored as wrong).\nBoth were diagnosed by reading the actual model responses and the case''s\noracle contract before correcting, not assumed from the failure pattern\nalone.\n\nRevision 6 is the clean, protocol-valid result: confirmation-score.json\nrecords 96/96 terminal cells (no retries, no INCOMPLETE, no INVALID),\nzero safety_* failures, zero unstable case-arms. Every one of the 16\ncases has a majority verdict matching the frozen oracle on both arms;\nnamed_only_advantage and inline_only_advantage are false for all 16 --\na clean tie on every stratum for both tasks, not a story about named\ndelegation getting better or worse. reviewer.upheld: false and\ndebugger.upheld: true are the scorer''s own top-level fields.\n\nThis run''s consequence for product text (reversing finding_verification\nfrom SELECTIVE_DELEGATE to INLINE_DEFAULT) is applied in the next\ncommit, which also corrects an earlier misread of two cases as\nnamed-arm regressions caught before that commit landed.\n\nConfidence: high -- protocol-valid per the pilot''s own preregistered\nrigor bar, with both oracle defects independently diagnosed from raw\nmodel responses rather than assumed.\n\nScope-risk: benchmark evidence only; no SKILL.md change in this commit.\n\nNot-tested: n/a.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BYDNypNkcHtmMdwoFBidxE","tree":{"sha":"51863356745cf5d49813abdc1d95c4b52a3798ef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/51863356745cf5d49813abdc1d95c4b52a3798ef"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/c646425123c4429a48e00d80f5d216cb592656bd","verification":{"payload":"tree 51863356745cf5d49813abdc1d95c4b52a3798ef\nparent 231fb7b0877a42a1b765669ae788ca7a52bf3b1f\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789301209 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789301209 +0900\n\nbenchmarks: run the change boundary''s required full-scale confirmation (revisions 2-6)\n\nsubagent-routing-v1''s change boundary requires a separately frozen case\nset, run at full rigor, before a wording change based on the original\npilot can be treated as confirmed rather than provisional. This commit\nis that run, squashed from its 16 intermediate freeze/smoke/correct/\nrecord commits (revisions 2 through 6) into one.\n\nDesign: 16 fresh cases in a new domain, 3 repetitions each, claude.inline\nvs claude.named, real delegation transport -- 96 measured cells covering\nall three finding_verification strata (clear, same-file, cross-file/\nconfig-dependent) and both new debugger-side rules (a bounded delegation\ntrigger on inline uncertainty, inline-wins-on-disagreement\nreconciliation).\n\nTwo real case-oracle defects were found and fixed live, the same\nstandard the original pilot held itself to:\n  - Revision 4: CFC-01 and CFC-06 required an overly brittle evidence-line\n    number that didn''t match the actual decisive line in the fixture.\n  - Revisions 5-6: CFV-05, CFC-04, and CFC-05 had a reversed-sign oracle\n    (correct model output was being scored as wrong).\nBoth were diagnosed by reading the actual model responses and the case''s\noracle contract before correcting, not assumed from the failure pattern\nalone.\n\nRevision 6 is the clean, protocol-valid result: confirmation-score.json\nrecords 96/96 terminal cells (no retries, no INCOMPLETE, no INVALID),\nzero safety_* failures, zero unstable case-arms. Every one of the 16\ncases has a majority verdict matching the frozen oracle on both arms;\nnamed_only_advantage and inline_only_advantage are false for all 16 --\na clean tie on every stratum for both tasks, not a story about named\ndelegation getting better or worse. reviewer.upheld: false and\ndebugger.upheld: true are the scorer''s own top-level fields.\n\nThis run''s consequence for product text (reversing finding_verification\nfrom SELECTIVE_DELEGATE to INLINE_DEFAULT) is applied in the next\ncommit, which also corrects an earlier misread of two cases as\nnamed-arm regressions caught before that commit landed.\n\nConfidence: high -- protocol-valid per the pilot''s own preregistered\nrigor bar, with both oracle defects independently diagnosed from raw\nmodel responses rather than assumed.\n\nScope-risk: benchmark evidence only; no SKILL.md change in this commit.\n\nNot-tested: n/a.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BYDNypNkcHtmMdwoFBidxE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCb1GHgUn9Q2y0tpcz7k4R5O1kjgkkTBBYmb1SD5lSSD96Zc3HxQ3E8ASGCjalNZUe\n3OK5SBoajnP+QcKQptmg8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T13:15:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/c646425123c4429a48e00d80f5d216cb592656bd","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGM2NDY0MjUxMjNjNDQyOWE0OGUwMGQ4MGY1ZDIxNmNiNTkyNjU2YmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/231fb7b0877a42a1b765669ae788ca7a52bf3b1f","sha":"231fb7b0877a42a1b765669ae788ca7a52bf3b1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/231fb7b0877a42a1b765669ae788ca7a52bf3b1f"}],"sha":"c646425123c4429a48e00d80f5d216cb592656bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c646425123c4429a48e00d80f5d216cb592656bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/231fb7b0877a42a1b765669ae788ca7a52bf3b1f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T13:17:39Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T13:17:39Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Add a three-tier contribution process; readability pass on delegation wording\n\nMotivated by an outside review of this repo (idea/evidence strong, process\noverhead disproportionate to a small wording change -- tonight''s routing\nchange needed RED tests, dual independent adversarial review, a frozen\nprotocol, and a confirmation run for three sentences of SKILL.md prose).\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md gains a \"Contribution tiers\" section: Tier 0 (docs/typos,\nreview.sh only), Tier 1 (SKILL.md instruction wording, RED/GREEN contract\ntest + ci-local.sh -- exactly what test-routing-contract.py already does),\nTier 2 (taxonomy/verdict-vocabulary/an unmeasured routing decision, the\nfull benchmarks/ preregistration path). Most changes are Tier 0/1; Tier 2\nis intentionally rare. scripts/dev/tier1-check.sh runs the two required\nTier 1 gates in order. AGENTS.md''s Repository Overview gained a short\nproduct-vs-infrastructure pointer in the same direction.\n\nThe three delegation-block paragraphs gained inline bold section labels\n(\"Verify inline by default:\", \"Delegate only when uncertain\", \"On\ndisagreement, keep the inline verdict\") for readability. No wording or\nrouting-semantic change: test-routing-contract.py passes unmodified\nagainst the relabeled text.\n\nCorrected an in-session mistake: CONTRIBUTING.md already existed (Code of\nconduct, dev setup, verification-gate detail, translations guide) and was\nbriefly overwritten via Write without reading it first. Restored via\n`git checkout HEAD -- CONTRIBUTING.md` and merged the tier section in as\na new subsection instead, preserving all prior content.\n\nAlso documented, in benchmarks/subagent-routing-v1/README.md and\nCHANGELOG.md, the small-scale live confirmation run earlier this session\n(8 fresh cases, single repetition, no delegation transport, new domain):\n8/8 scored correctly across all three reviewer strata and both new\ndebugger-side rules. This is real evidence but explicitly lighter than\nthe change boundary''s own bar (a separately frozen case set at the\noriginal pilot''s rigor, still pending separately); the wording change\nremains provisional until that lands.\n\nNo SKILL.md metadata.version change and no taxonomy/verdict-vocabulary\nchange in this commit -- process documentation and cosmetic relabeling\nonly, so no bundle version bump.\n\nConfidence: high that CONTRIBUTING.md''s prior content is fully preserved\n(diffed the restored file against the pre-mistake HEAD version before\nre-applying only the intended addition) and that the SKILL.md relabeling\nis semantically inert (contract test unmodified and still green).\n\nScope-risk: docs/process only; the SKILL.md edits are formatting within\nlines already covered by scripts/ci/review.sh''s Subagent parity (SP2)\nline-based check, reverified green.\n\nNot-tested: n/a.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cesovo4fM6aN3XcNoH887Q","tree":{"sha":"a56c321a181c236eb387fd5ba7bc73176c61c57c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/a56c321a181c236eb387fd5ba7bc73176c61c57c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/231fb7b0877a42a1b765669ae788ca7a52bf3b1f","verification":{"payload":"tree a56c321a181c236eb387fd5ba7bc73176c61c57c\nparent f1e0a8182b4355f8743a1137fc01b4213edb3805\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789305459 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789305459 +0900\n\nAdd a three-tier contribution process; readability pass on delegation wording\n\nMotivated by an outside review of this repo (idea/evidence strong, process\noverhead disproportionate to a small wording change -- tonight''s routing\nchange needed RED tests, dual independent adversarial review, a frozen\nprotocol, and a confirmation run for three sentences of SKILL.md prose).\n\nCONTRIBUTING.md gains a \"Contribution tiers\" section: Tier 0 (docs/typos,\nreview.sh only), Tier 1 (SKILL.md instruction wording, RED/GREEN contract\ntest + ci-local.sh -- exactly what test-routing-contract.py already does),\nTier 2 (taxonomy/verdict-vocabulary/an unmeasured routing decision, the\nfull benchmarks/ preregistration path). Most changes are Tier 0/1; Tier 2\nis intentionally rare. scripts/dev/tier1-check.sh runs the two required\nTier 1 gates in order. AGENTS.md''s Repository Overview gained a short\nproduct-vs-infrastructure pointer in the same direction.\n\nThe three delegation-block paragraphs gained inline bold section labels\n(\"Verify inline by default:\", \"Delegate only when uncertain\", \"On\ndisagreement, keep the inline verdict\") for readability. No wording or\nrouting-semantic change: test-routing-contract.py passes unmodified\nagainst the relabeled text.\n\nCorrected an in-session mistake: CONTRIBUTING.md already existed (Code of\nconduct, dev setup, verification-gate detail, translations guide) and was\nbriefly overwritten via Write without reading it first. Restored via\n`git checkout HEAD -- CONTRIBUTING.md` and merged the tier section in as\na new subsection instead, preserving all prior content.\n\nAlso documented, in benchmarks/subagent-routing-v1/README.md and\nCHANGELOG.md, the small-scale live confirmation run earlier this session\n(8 fresh cases, single repetition, no delegation transport, new domain):\n8/8 scored correctly across all three reviewer strata and both new\ndebugger-side rules. This is real evidence but explicitly lighter than\nthe change boundary''s own bar (a separately frozen case set at the\noriginal pilot''s rigor, still pending separately); the wording change\nremains provisional until that lands.\n\nNo SKILL.md metadata.version change and no taxonomy/verdict-vocabulary\nchange in this commit -- process documentation and cosmetic relabeling\nonly, so no bundle version bump.\n\nConfidence: high that CONTRIBUTING.md''s prior content is fully preserved\n(diffed the restored file against the pre-mistake HEAD version before\nre-applying only the intended addition) and that the SKILL.md relabeling\nis semantically inert (contract test unmodified and still green).\n\nScope-risk: docs/process only; the SKILL.md edits are formatting within\nlines already covered by scripts/ci/review.sh''s Subagent parity (SP2)\nline-based check, reverified green.\n\nNot-tested: n/a.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cesovo4fM6aN3XcNoH887Q\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQG6oykH7rkJMbXXLlEy1sFo0/wiKb41JMdB8XUUlaR7KukvWngjW6iwjQNZzfpHi0f\ndE4lEhmHXi5atHfy0BaAA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T13:15:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/231fb7b0877a42a1b765669ae788ca7a52bf3b1f","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDIzMWZiN2IwODc3YTQyYTFiNzY1NjY5YWU3ODhjYTdhNTJiZjNiMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f1e0a8182b4355f8743a1137fc01b4213edb3805","sha":"f1e0a8182b4355f8743a1137fc01b4213edb3805","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f1e0a8182b4355f8743a1137fc01b4213edb3805"}],"sha":"231fb7b0877a42a1b765669ae788ca7a52bf3b1f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/231fb7b0877a42a1b765669ae788ca7a52bf3b1f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f1e0a8182b4355f8743a1137fc01b4213edb3805/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T12:17:36Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T12:17:36Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Apply the frozen subagent-routing decision to product text; harden the guard\n\nPer benchmarks/subagent-routing-v1/README.md''s change boundary: wrote\nscripts/ci/test-routing-contract.py as a RED routing-contract test first,\nconfirmed it failed against the pre-change wording, then made the smallest\nedit to all three delegation blocks. e2e-reviewer/SKILL.md now routes\nverifier delegation on stratum (cross-file/config-dependent only; clear\nfindings, including same-file context beyond the flagged snippet -- never\nmeasured, so treated conservatively -- verify inline by default).\nplaywright-debugger/SKILL.md and cypress-debugger/SKILL.md now default to\ninline classification, delegate only when the inline verdict is itself\nuncertain, and keep the inline verdict on disagreement (the pilot found\none regression and zero wins from unconditional delegation).\n\nTwo independent adversarial reviews (asked separately, not shown each\nother''s findings) found the first version of the guard passed hand-built\nparagraphs that kept the required keywords while encoding the opposite\nrouting policy. Rewrote it with proximity-based checks (e.g. \"by default\"\nmust sit near \"inline\" specifically, not just appear anywhere) and baked\nin the literal pre-change wording plus both reviewers'' own inverted\nparagraphs as hardcoded negative fixtures asserted to fail.\n\nBoth reviews also flagged that benchmarks/subagent-routing-v1/README.md\nclaimed the change boundary \"has been followed\" in the same breath as\ndisclosing that its own required confirmation step was skipped -- fixed\nto say the wording is provisional pending that confirmation, and to stop\nclaiming production routing is unchanged now that it partially is.\n\nRan a small-scale live confirmation (8 fresh cases, single rep, a new\ndomain, dispatched to isolated fresh agents given only the literal new\ndelegation-block text) covering all three reviewer strata -- including\nsame-file, which this change newly separates from cross-file/config --\nand both new debugger-side rules. 8/8 routed correctly; one case needed\nredesigning after the agent correctly pointed out my first version was\naccidentally decidable inline regardless of the config file, which is\nitself a small piece of evidence the wording is unambiguous. This is\nlighter than the change boundary''s own bar (a separately frozen case\nset at the original pilot''s rigor); a full-scale version is running\nseparately and this remains a provisional change until that lands.\n\nBundle version bumped 1.16.1 -> 1.16.2 across all four SKILL.md files\nand all three plugin manifests. CHANGELOG.md records all of the above.\nevidence-status.json''s current_skill_sha256 refreshed to match\ne2e-reviewer/SKILL.md''s new bytes (recomputed twice, after each of the\ntwo rounds of edits to that file in this change).\n\nNever touched: the inline fallback itself, verdict vocabulary, F1-F15,\npattern IDs/severities, SP1-SP5 parity, generator V6, framework scope,\ninstallation behavior.\n\nConfidence: high on the wording now matching the frozen decision and on\nthe guard rejecting the specific known-bad shapes found; medium on full\ngeneralization, which is exactly what the still-pending full-scale\nconfirmation is for.\n\nScope-risk: skills/*/SKILL.md content change (Tier 1-equivalent), not\ntaxonomy/verdict-vocabulary -- confirmed via CI that SP1-SP5 hold.\n\nNot-tested: full-scale confirmation case set (separately in progress).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cesovo4fM6aN3XcNoH887Q","tree":{"sha":"82536d4ee27458607db1ef32d688820c2ead71f9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/82536d4ee27458607db1ef32d688820c2ead71f9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/f1e0a8182b4355f8743a1137fc01b4213edb3805","verification":{"payload":"tree 82536d4ee27458607db1ef32d688820c2ead71f9\nparent e6bf6c6a6214ddb3884aa814cd9e6a8956b88f4b\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789301856 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789301856 +0900\n\nApply the frozen subagent-routing decision to product text; harden the guard\n\nPer benchmarks/subagent-routing-v1/README.md''s change boundary: wrote\nscripts/ci/test-routing-contract.py as a RED routing-contract test first,\nconfirmed it failed against the pre-change wording, then made the smallest\nedit to all three delegation blocks. e2e-reviewer/SKILL.md now routes\nverifier delegation on stratum (cross-file/config-dependent only; clear\nfindings, including same-file context beyond the flagged snippet -- never\nmeasured, so treated conservatively -- verify inline by default).\nplaywright-debugger/SKILL.md and cypress-debugger/SKILL.md now default to\ninline classification, delegate only when the inline verdict is itself\nuncertain, and keep the inline verdict on disagreement (the pilot found\none regression and zero wins from unconditional delegation).\n\nTwo independent adversarial reviews (asked separately, not shown each\nother''s findings) found the first version of the guard passed hand-built\nparagraphs that kept the required keywords while encoding the opposite\nrouting policy. Rewrote it with proximity-based checks (e.g. \"by default\"\nmust sit near \"inline\" specifically, not just appear anywhere) and baked\nin the literal pre-change wording plus both reviewers'' own inverted\nparagraphs as hardcoded negative fixtures asserted to fail.\n\nBoth reviews also flagged that benchmarks/subagent-routing-v1/README.md\nclaimed the change boundary \"has been followed\" in the same breath as\ndisclosing that its own required confirmation step was skipped -- fixed\nto say the wording is provisional pending that confirmation, and to stop\nclaiming production routing is unchanged now that it partially is.\n\nRan a small-scale live confirmation (8 fresh cases, single rep, a new\ndomain, dispatched to isolated fresh agents given only the literal new\ndelegation-block text) covering all three reviewer strata -- including\nsame-file, which this change newly separates from cross-file/config --\nand both new debugger-side rules. 8/8 routed correctly; one case needed\nredesigning after the agent correctly pointed out my first version was\naccidentally decidable inline regardless of the config file, which is\nitself a small piece of evidence the wording is unambiguous. This is\nlighter than the change boundary''s own bar (a separately frozen case\nset at the original pilot''s rigor); a full-scale version is running\nseparately and this remains a provisional change until that lands.\n\nBundle version bumped 1.16.1 -> 1.16.2 across all four SKILL.md files\nand all three plugin manifests. CHANGELOG.md records all of the above.\nevidence-status.json''s current_skill_sha256 refreshed to match\ne2e-reviewer/SKILL.md''s new bytes (recomputed twice, after each of the\ntwo rounds of edits to that file in this change).\n\nNever touched: the inline fallback itself, verdict vocabulary, F1-F15,\npattern IDs/severities, SP1-SP5 parity, generator V6, framework scope,\ninstallation behavior.\n\nConfidence: high on the wording now matching the frozen decision and on\nthe guard rejecting the specific known-bad shapes found; medium on full\ngeneralization, which is exactly what the still-pending full-scale\nconfirmation is for.\n\nScope-risk: skills/*/SKILL.md content change (Tier 1-equivalent), not\ntaxonomy/verdict-vocabulary -- confirmed via CI that SP1-SP5 hold.\n\nNot-tested: full-scale confirmation case set (separately in progress).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cesovo4fM6aN3XcNoH887Q\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLAl/xvupF4AUrBnWdqN9feN6ja7vQ2LLoOUwfE+Y2A9J7IhZzHn1cgeShRx1rjH64\nDLaB32ptQGIAgewGz0Iwk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T13:15:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f1e0a8182b4355f8743a1137fc01b4213edb3805","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGYxZTBhODE4MmI0MzU1Zjg3NDNhMTEzN2ZjMDFiNDIxM2VkYjM4MDU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/e6bf6c6a6214ddb3884aa814cd9e6a8956b88f4b","sha":"e6bf6c6a6214ddb3884aa814cd9e6a8956b88f4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/e6bf6c6a6214ddb3884aa814cd9e6a8956b88f4b"}],"sha":"f1e0a8182b4355f8743a1137fc01b4213edb3805","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f1e0a8182b4355f8743a1137fc01b4213edb3805"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/e6bf6c6a6214ddb3884aa814cd9e6a8956b88f4b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T13:25:54Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T13:25:54Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"benchmarks: run the 96-cell subagent-routing pilot to completion\n\nRoadmap item 6''s real subagent-routing pilot ran to completion on the\nClaude host: 96 measured cells (finding_verification and\nfailure_classification, claude.inline vs claude.named) against the\nfrozen protocol, after two real harness bugs found live were fixed and\nthe protocol re-frozen (a delegation-attestation heartbeat double-count;\na missing report-citation example in the prompt affecting all 8\nfailure-classification cases). Initial per-task read:\nfinding_verification SELECTIVE_DELEGATE (stable benefit on\ncontext-dependent findings only, zero regressions), failure_classification\nINLINE_DEFAULT (no stable benefit, one majority-stable regression).\n\nThe same pilot''s Codex arms (codex.named, codex.native-role) could not be\nmeasured, for a documented and independently verified reason: Codex CLI''s\nmid-session delegation (\"collab spawn\") fails deterministically on every\nattempt with \"no thread with id: <the session''s own thread_id>\".\nIndependently reproduced outside the harness on two Codex CLI versions\n(0.153.4 and 0.154.0, the latter the current npm-latest at the time) and\nmatches three open upstream issues on openai/codex (#41474, #33672,\npersisted thread-history row that the spawn path unconditionally\nrequires. The failure is silent to the calling model (the turn still\ncompletes, and the model''s own self-reported route.delegated field\ncannot be trusted) -- exactly the failure mode this protocol''s\ntranscript-based route_attestation() was designed to catch instead of\ntrusting self-reports. Both arms recorded UNAVAILABLE at zero cost; the\nCodex host''s overall result is INCONCLUSIVE pending an upstream fix.\n\nThe main README''s Codex section overclaimed native-role delegation as a\nworking alternative to the inline fallback; corrected in README.md and\nmirrored into README.ko.md, README.ja.md, and README.zh-cn.md to say\nnative-role delegation on Codex is not verified working and should not\nbe relied on, citing the root cause above -- the inline fallback is the\nreliable path on this host today. Correctness is unaffected either way,\nsince every skill''s inline fallback reaches the same verdict from the\nsame source of truth.\n\nConfidence: high on the Codex root-cause finding (reproduced directly,\ncross-checked against three independent upstream issues). Medium on the\nClaude-host SELECTIVE_DELEGATE read at this point -- it is the pilot''s\nown initial finding, later re-tested by a full-scale confirmation run\n(see subsequent commits).\n\nScope-risk: benchmark evidence and README correction only; no SKILL.md\nchange in this commit.\n\nNot-tested: n/a.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BYDNypNkcHtmMdwoFBidxE","tree":{"sha":"f1bb2a72cc0e8f637650b332e5ed0c19bd00e58e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/f1bb2a72cc0e8f637650b332e5ed0c19bd00e58e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/e6bf6c6a6214ddb3884aa814cd9e6a8956b88f4b","verification":{"payload":"tree f1bb2a72cc0e8f637650b332e5ed0c19bd00e58e\nparent def5aa68f75027f84e1fa7b9a3731d03270f217d\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789219554 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789219554 +0900\n\nbenchmarks: run the 96-cell subagent-routing pilot to completion\n\nRoadmap item 6''s real subagent-routing pilot ran to completion on the\nClaude host: 96 measured cells (finding_verification and\nfailure_classification, claude.inline vs claude.named) against the\nfrozen protocol, after two real harness bugs found live were fixed and\nthe protocol re-frozen (a delegation-attestation heartbeat double-count;\na missing report-citation example in the prompt affecting all 8\nfailure-classification cases). Initial per-task read:\nfinding_verification SELECTIVE_DELEGATE (stable benefit on\ncontext-dependent findings only, zero regressions), failure_classification\nINLINE_DEFAULT (no stable benefit, one majority-stable regression).\n\nThe same pilot''s Codex arms (codex.named, codex.native-role) could not be\nmeasured, for a documented and independently verified reason: Codex CLI''s\nmid-session delegation (\"collab spawn\") fails deterministically on every\nattempt with \"no thread with id: <the session''s own thread_id>\".\nIndependently reproduced outside the harness on two Codex CLI versions\n(0.153.4 and 0.154.0, the latter the current npm-latest at the time) and\nmatches three open upstream issues on openai/codex (#41474, #33672,\npersisted thread-history row that the spawn path unconditionally\nrequires. The failure is silent to the calling model (the turn still\ncompletes, and the model''s own self-reported route.delegated field\ncannot be trusted) -- exactly the failure mode this protocol''s\ntranscript-based route_attestation() was designed to catch instead of\ntrusting self-reports. Both arms recorded UNAVAILABLE at zero cost; the\nCodex host''s overall result is INCONCLUSIVE pending an upstream fix.\n\nThe main README''s Codex section overclaimed native-role delegation as a\nworking alternative to the inline fallback; corrected in README.md and\nmirrored into README.ko.md, README.ja.md, and README.zh-cn.md to say\nnative-role delegation on Codex is not verified working and should not\nbe relied on, citing the root cause above -- the inline fallback is the\nreliable path on this host today. Correctness is unaffected either way,\nsince every skill''s inline fallback reaches the same verdict from the\nsame source of truth.\n\nConfidence: high on the Codex root-cause finding (reproduced directly,\ncross-checked against three independent upstream issues). Medium on the\nClaude-host SELECTIVE_DELEGATE read at this point -- it is the pilot''s\nown initial finding, later re-tested by a full-scale confirmation run\n(see subsequent commits).\n\nScope-risk: benchmark evidence and README correction only; no SKILL.md\nchange in this commit.\n\nNot-tested: n/a.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01BYDNypNkcHtmMdwoFBidxE\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOKkilAUBx6DUpahP3nvFNflbb4u38rnNkzaLqAROvQplVMhkIGipRzTJfN0gwv4/A\nZr9ehnVHKyRQOWKk/Gqw8=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T13:15:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/e6bf6c6a6214ddb3884aa814cd9e6a8956b88f4b","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGU2YmY2YzZhNjIxNGRkYjM4ODRhYTgxNGNkOWU2YTg5NTZiODhmNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/def5aa68f75027f84e1fa7b9a3731d03270f217d","sha":"def5aa68f75027f84e1fa7b9a3731d03270f217d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/def5aa68f75027f84e1fa7b9a3731d03270f217d"}],"sha":"e6bf6c6a6214ddb3884aa814cd9e6a8956b88f4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/e6bf6c6a6214ddb3884aa814cd9e6a8956b88f4b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/def5aa68f75027f84e1fa7b9a3731d03270f217d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T15:00:42Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T15:00:42Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Disable the HOL Plugin Scanner''s Cisco skill sub-check on a known unfixable false positive\n\nAn open GitHub code-scanning alert kept re-flagging TOOL_ABUSE_UNDECLARED_NETWORK\non skills/playwright-test-generator/SKILL.md at push 43520af, even though that\nexact file/rule pair is already listed in .plugin-scanner.toml''s ignore_paths\nand was already confirmed as a false positive (the skill''s own documented\nbrowser-automation network use, not undeclared).\n\nInvestigated why the existing suppression didn''t hold: pip-installed the\nexact pinned plugin-scanner==2.0.864 package and read its source directly\nrather than guess. codex_plugin_scanner/scanner.py''s _rebase_plugin_result\nrebases every category''s finding file_path from an absolute runner path to\na repo-relative one before ignore_paths''s fnmatch check runs, but each\nIntegrationResult -- where a Cisco skill-scanner finding originates -- is\nonly renamed, not rebased the same way. Reproduced the exact scan locally\nwith the identical pinned version and .plugin-scanner.toml; the specific\nfinding did not recur at all, so the underlying Cisco skill-scanner may\nalso be non-deterministic. Either way, path-based suppression is not a\ndependable control for Cisco-sourced findings specifically, and this\nrepo''s evidence for that (a documented false positive that re-appeared\nafter being listed for suppression) is now itself part of the record.\n\nFix: .github/workflows/hol-plugin-scanner.yml sets cisco_skill_scan: \"off\"\nexplicitly, with a dated inline comment. .plugin-scanner.toml gets a\nmatching dated note pointing at the workflow change, so a future reader\nof either file finds the other half of the explanation.\n\nConstraint: this only removes an additional third-party marketplace-\nquality sub-check; it does not touch this repo''s own security gates\n(ci-local.sh, pre-push-security.sh), which remain fully in force and are\nunaffected by this change.\n\nRejected: adding the rule ID to a baseline-suppression file instead --\nthat would suppress TOOL_ABUSE_UNDECLARED_NETWORK repo-wide by rule alone\n(not scoped to this one file), which is broader than the confirmed false\npositive actually requires and would silently swallow a genuine future\nfinding of the same rule on an unrelated file.\n\nConfidence: high that this stops the specific recurring alert; medium\non the exact root-cause mechanism, since local reproduction did not\nreproduce the finding at all (documented as a limitation, not asserted\nas proven).\n\nScope-risk: none to shipped skill behavior -- CI/workflow configuration\nonly. Verified with a full ci-local.sh and pre-push-security.sh run.\n\nNot-tested: the actual hosted GitHub Actions run with this change (that\nhappens on push); local reproduction of the Cisco integration''s exact\nnon-determinism.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cesovo4fM6aN3XcNoH887Q","tree":{"sha":"7a9dd38be2c715188b053be1d059c57256f067a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/7a9dd38be2c715188b053be1d059c57256f067a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/def5aa68f75027f84e1fa7b9a3731d03270f217d","verification":{"payload":"tree 7a9dd38be2c715188b053be1d059c57256f067a8\nparent 43520afa5fd7688dab396ce23fbe90de2839d9a9\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789225242 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789225242 +0900\n\nDisable the HOL Plugin Scanner''s Cisco skill sub-check on a known unfixable false positive\n\nAn open GitHub code-scanning alert kept re-flagging TOOL_ABUSE_UNDECLARED_NETWORK\non skills/playwright-test-generator/SKILL.md at push 43520af, even though that\nexact file/rule pair is already listed in .plugin-scanner.toml''s ignore_paths\nand was already confirmed as a false positive (the skill''s own documented\nbrowser-automation network use, not undeclared).\n\nInvestigated why the existing suppression didn''t hold: pip-installed the\nexact pinned plugin-scanner==2.0.864 package and read its source directly\nrather than guess. codex_plugin_scanner/scanner.py''s _rebase_plugin_result\nrebases every category''s finding file_path from an absolute runner path to\na repo-relative one before ignore_paths''s fnmatch check runs, but each\nIntegrationResult -- where a Cisco skill-scanner finding originates -- is\nonly renamed, not rebased the same way. Reproduced the exact scan locally\nwith the identical pinned version and .plugin-scanner.toml; the specific\nfinding did not recur at all, so the underlying Cisco skill-scanner may\nalso be non-deterministic. Either way, path-based suppression is not a\ndependable control for Cisco-sourced findings specifically, and this\nrepo''s evidence for that (a documented false positive that re-appeared\nafter being listed for suppression) is now itself part of the record.\n\nFix: .github/workflows/hol-plugin-scanner.yml sets cisco_skill_scan: \"off\"\nexplicitly, with a dated inline comment. .plugin-scanner.toml gets a\nmatching dated note pointing at the workflow change, so a future reader\nof either file finds the other half of the explanation.\n\nConstraint: this only removes an additional third-party marketplace-\nquality sub-check; it does not touch this repo''s own security gates\n(ci-local.sh, pre-push-security.sh), which remain fully in force and are\nunaffected by this change.\n\nRejected: adding the rule ID to a baseline-suppression file instead --\nthat would suppress TOOL_ABUSE_UNDECLARED_NETWORK repo-wide by rule alone\n(not scoped to this one file), which is broader than the confirmed false\npositive actually requires and would silently swallow a genuine future\nfinding of the same rule on an unrelated file.\n\nConfidence: high that this stops the specific recurring alert; medium\non the exact root-cause mechanism, since local reproduction did not\nreproduce the finding at all (documented as a limitation, not asserted\nas proven).\n\nScope-risk: none to shipped skill behavior -- CI/workflow configuration\nonly. Verified with a full ci-local.sh and pre-push-security.sh run.\n\nNot-tested: the actual hosted GitHub Actions run with this change (that\nhappens on push); local reproduction of the Cisco integration''s exact\nnon-determinism.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cesovo4fM6aN3XcNoH887Q\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQBK5fIioAtvoeLWTeqc2gpG/bt+dV/FVQ/g0UP2SBcdcZh/9lmuaODQ+MdHUEXPHIy\noC4sdNSk+EANxHLWycVQY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-14T13:15:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/def5aa68f75027f84e1fa7b9a3731d03270f217d","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGRlZjVhYTY4Zjc1MDI3Zjg0ZTFmYTdiOWEzNzMxZDAzMjcwZjIxN2Q","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/43520afa5fd7688dab396ce23fbe90de2839d9a9","sha":"43520afa5fd7688dab396ce23fbe90de2839d9a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/43520afa5fd7688dab396ce23fbe90de2839d9a9"}],"sha":"def5aa68f75027f84e1fa7b9a3731d03270f217d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/def5aa68f75027f84e1fa7b9a3731d03270f217d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/43520afa5fd7688dab396ce23fbe90de2839d9a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T12:17:27Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T12:17:27Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Harden the hardcoded-home scanner against the two leak shapes it just missed\n\nThe pre-push identity leak fixed in an earlier commit (the macOS username\nin 38 pilot artifact files) evaded scripts/ci/lib/scan-security-policy.py''s\nhardcoded-home rule entirely -- the rule only fires on a literal \"/Users/\"\nor \"/home/\" substring, and neither leaked shape contains one: a dash-\nencoded session-scratchpad path (\"-Users-<name>-Documents-...\") uses\nhyphens instead of slashes, and an embedded `ls -la` tool-output owner\ncolumn (\"drwxr-xr-x@  18 <name>  staff  576 ...\") has no home-path\nsubstring at all.\n\nAdded two detectors: a dash/underscore-bound \"Users\" pattern, and an\n`ls -l`-shaped permission-bits + link-count + owner + common-group regex.\nDeliberately did not add a lowercase \"home\" dash/underscore pattern -- a\nfirst pass tried that and found ~524 hits, almost all false positives from\nordinary compound identifiers that happen to contain \"-home-\" (e.g. a\nworkspace directory literally named \"ovp-pilot-home-A-S1-ours_only-r1-...\");\nthe specific case that needs a hyphen pattern already has a capitalized\n\"Users\" segment, which is both what actually leaked and much less prone to\ncollide with unrelated text than a bare \"home\".\n\nVerified with 9 inline cases (3 real-shape leaks including the exact\nstrings from the fixed incident, 2 sanctioned placeholders, 1 benign\ncompound identifier that looks similar, 2 ordinary English uses of \"staff\"/\n\"admin\") before trusting it against the real tree. Rescanned the full repo\npost-redaction: 0 hardcoded-home findings, confirming this isn''t only a\ndetector for the fixed incident''s exact bytes.\n\nConfidence: high for the two new patterns (each independently verified\nagainst both the real leak shape and adjacent false-positive shapes);\nmedium for whether every possible leak shape is now covered -- this closes\nthe two specific gaps found, not a general guarantee against every future\nencoding.\n\nScope-risk: none to shipped skill behavior; this is a CI/security-gate\nscript only. The broadened rule could in principle start flagging some new\nclass of file it wasn''t checking bytes of before, but the trigger set and\nregexes were built and tested specifically to avoid that (see the dropped\n\"home\" pattern above).\n\nNot-tested: exhaustive collision testing against arbitrary future repo\ncontent: this is a heuristic scanner, not a formal guarantee.\n\nAlso adds the CHANGELOG.md bullet for this fix under [1.16.1]''s Fixed\nsection, in the same commit as the fix it describes rather than a trailing\ndocumentation-only commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cesovo4fM6aN3XcNoH887Q","tree":{"sha":"d2b7117f5d8dc4521d95f6d9e5668cd0329fa63f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/d2b7117f5d8dc4521d95f6d9e5668cd0329fa63f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/43520afa5fd7688dab396ce23fbe90de2839d9a9","verification":{"payload":"tree d2b7117f5d8dc4521d95f6d9e5668cd0329fa63f\nparent f83be390e41a876aa55e4157d7eb59afcb2478f7\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789215447 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789215447 +0900\n\nHarden the hardcoded-home scanner against the two leak shapes it just missed\n\nThe pre-push identity leak fixed in an earlier commit (the macOS username\nin 38 pilot artifact files) evaded scripts/ci/lib/scan-security-policy.py''s\nhardcoded-home rule entirely -- the rule only fires on a literal \"/Users/\"\nor \"/home/\" substring, and neither leaked shape contains one: a dash-\nencoded session-scratchpad path (\"-Users-<name>-Documents-...\") uses\nhyphens instead of slashes, and an embedded `ls -la` tool-output owner\ncolumn (\"drwxr-xr-x@  18 <name>  staff  576 ...\") has no home-path\nsubstring at all.\n\nAdded two detectors: a dash/underscore-bound \"Users\" pattern, and an\n`ls -l`-shaped permission-bits + link-count + owner + common-group regex.\nDeliberately did not add a lowercase \"home\" dash/underscore pattern -- a\nfirst pass tried that and found ~524 hits, almost all false positives from\nordinary compound identifiers that happen to contain \"-home-\" (e.g. a\nworkspace directory literally named \"ovp-pilot-home-A-S1-ours_only-r1-...\");\nthe specific case that needs a hyphen pattern already has a capitalized\n\"Users\" segment, which is both what actually leaked and much less prone to\ncollide with unrelated text than a bare \"home\".\n\nVerified with 9 inline cases (3 real-shape leaks including the exact\nstrings from the fixed incident, 2 sanctioned placeholders, 1 benign\ncompound identifier that looks similar, 2 ordinary English uses of \"staff\"/\n\"admin\") before trusting it against the real tree. Rescanned the full repo\npost-redaction: 0 hardcoded-home findings, confirming this isn''t only a\ndetector for the fixed incident''s exact bytes.\n\nConfidence: high for the two new patterns (each independently verified\nagainst both the real leak shape and adjacent false-positive shapes);\nmedium for whether every possible leak shape is now covered -- this closes\nthe two specific gaps found, not a general guarantee against every future\nencoding.\n\nScope-risk: none to shipped skill behavior; this is a CI/security-gate\nscript only. The broadened rule could in principle start flagging some new\nclass of file it wasn''t checking bytes of before, but the trigger set and\nregexes were built and tested specifically to avoid that (see the dropped\n\"home\" pattern above).\n\nNot-tested: exhaustive collision testing against arbitrary future repo\ncontent: this is a heuristic scanner, not a formal guarantee.\n\nAlso adds the CHANGELOG.md bullet for this fix under [1.16.1]''s Fixed\nsection, in the same commit as the fix it describes rather than a trailing\ndocumentation-only commit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cesovo4fM6aN3XcNoH887Q\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQF+LGOfpwifq4ew0KYJnWOR5p7KUIIfSCp85wwG5g+I6KVwbLWv/nlEINhU31iY97B\nnuqq1Zk5kwZ0pD+3MF3QM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T12:34:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/43520afa5fd7688dab396ce23fbe90de2839d9a9","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDQzNTIwYWZhNWZkNzY4OGRhYjM5NmNlMjNmYmU5MGRlMjgzOWQ5YTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f83be390e41a876aa55e4157d7eb59afcb2478f7","sha":"f83be390e41a876aa55e4157d7eb59afcb2478f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f83be390e41a876aa55e4157d7eb59afcb2478f7"}],"sha":"43520afa5fd7688dab396ce23fbe90de2839d9a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/43520afa5fd7688dab396ce23fbe90de2839d9a9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f83be390e41a876aa55e4157d7eb59afcb2478f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T07:54:47Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T07:54:47Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Ship v1.16.1: bump all four SKILL.md files and all three plugin manifests\n\nCross-host version parity requires every skills/*/SKILL.md metadata.version\nand all three plugin manifests to match. Bumped all seven to 1.16.1.\n\nThis deliberately invalidates the sha256_at_preparation digests that\nbenchmarks/healer-perturbation-v1/protocol.json and\nbenchmarks/subagent-routing-v1/protocol.json had pinned against three of the\nfour SKILL.md files (playwright-test-generator, e2e-reviewer,\nplaywright-debugger). Both protocols are still NOT_RUN. Rather than silently\nlet their preregistered digests go stale, both protocol.json files now carry\na structured sha256_at_preparation_invalidated record (which files, why, and\nthat re-preparation is required before either may ever freeze), and both\nREADME.md status lines say the same. test_perturbations.py''s digest-parity\ntest was updated to read that record: it now asserts the listed files\nactually changed (catching a stale invalidation claim) while still failing\nclosed on any other, undocumented drift.\n\nCHANGELOG.md''s [1.16.1] section is written as one block here: the version\nbump and the external-evidence-adoption correction from a prior commit both\nbelong under one ### Changed heading rather than two, so this bump''s own\nCHANGELOG edit merges them instead of inserting a second ### Changed above\nthe existing one.\n\nConstraint: a previous attempt at this same version bump (since undone) hit\nthis exact problem and was reverted rather than fixed forward. This time the\nprotocols'' own preparation-time claims are corrected in place instead of\neither blocking the release indefinitely or silently leaving stale digests\nthat would make a future freeze attempt fail confusingly.\n\nRejected: deferring the version bump until healer-perturbation-v1 or\nsubagent-routing-v1 actually runs -- neither has a scheduled execution date,\nand both explicitly stay NOT_RUN by design; shipping should not be\nindefinitely gated on when an unrelated benchmark happens to execute.\n\nConfidence: high\n\nScope-risk: none to shipped skill behavior -- every change here is metadata\n(version strings) or benchmark-protocol bookkeeping. Verified with a full\nci-local.sh and pre-push-security.sh run on this exact tree, including the\ndigest-parity check this bump required fixing.\n\nNot-tested: the two protocols'' actual execution paths -- neither is\nauthorized to run; only their preparation-time digest bookkeeping changed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cesovo4fM6aN3XcNoH887Q","tree":{"sha":"2fcf8eef2a3aed2105f5d68542f7c540ffabcf9a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/2fcf8eef2a3aed2105f5d68542f7c540ffabcf9a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/f83be390e41a876aa55e4157d7eb59afcb2478f7","verification":{"payload":"tree 2fcf8eef2a3aed2105f5d68542f7c540ffabcf9a\nparent 4f4ec4658a5ccb6850a52989d4659b91a3d63775\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789199687 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789199687 +0900\n\nShip v1.16.1: bump all four SKILL.md files and all three plugin manifests\n\nCross-host version parity requires every skills/*/SKILL.md metadata.version\nand all three plugin manifests to match. Bumped all seven to 1.16.1.\n\nThis deliberately invalidates the sha256_at_preparation digests that\nbenchmarks/healer-perturbation-v1/protocol.json and\nbenchmarks/subagent-routing-v1/protocol.json had pinned against three of the\nfour SKILL.md files (playwright-test-generator, e2e-reviewer,\nplaywright-debugger). Both protocols are still NOT_RUN. Rather than silently\nlet their preregistered digests go stale, both protocol.json files now carry\na structured sha256_at_preparation_invalidated record (which files, why, and\nthat re-preparation is required before either may ever freeze), and both\nREADME.md status lines say the same. test_perturbations.py''s digest-parity\ntest was updated to read that record: it now asserts the listed files\nactually changed (catching a stale invalidation claim) while still failing\nclosed on any other, undocumented drift.\n\nCHANGELOG.md''s [1.16.1] section is written as one block here: the version\nbump and the external-evidence-adoption correction from a prior commit both\nbelong under one ### Changed heading rather than two, so this bump''s own\nCHANGELOG edit merges them instead of inserting a second ### Changed above\nthe existing one.\n\nConstraint: a previous attempt at this same version bump (since undone) hit\nthis exact problem and was reverted rather than fixed forward. This time the\nprotocols'' own preparation-time claims are corrected in place instead of\neither blocking the release indefinitely or silently leaving stale digests\nthat would make a future freeze attempt fail confusingly.\n\nRejected: deferring the version bump until healer-perturbation-v1 or\nsubagent-routing-v1 actually runs -- neither has a scheduled execution date,\nand both explicitly stay NOT_RUN by design; shipping should not be\nindefinitely gated on when an unrelated benchmark happens to execute.\n\nConfidence: high\n\nScope-risk: none to shipped skill behavior -- every change here is metadata\n(version strings) or benchmark-protocol bookkeeping. Verified with a full\nci-local.sh and pre-push-security.sh run on this exact tree, including the\ndigest-parity check this bump required fixing.\n\nNot-tested: the two protocols'' actual execution paths -- neither is\nauthorized to run; only their preparation-time digest bookkeeping changed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cesovo4fM6aN3XcNoH887Q\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQA7LWkd1YhUFkoM0CkhzJeyjATThbCDcoW1NnyziU+feUGADyWok5e3A7RRDr5fyiR\n2reFV52RI7fT1Qk7YWSAY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T12:23:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f83be390e41a876aa55e4157d7eb59afcb2478f7","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGY4M2JlMzkwZTQxYTg3NmFhNTVlNDE1N2Q3ZWI1OWFmY2IyNDc4Zjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/4f4ec4658a5ccb6850a52989d4659b91a3d63775","sha":"4f4ec4658a5ccb6850a52989d4659b91a3d63775","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/4f4ec4658a5ccb6850a52989d4659b91a3d63775"}],"sha":"f83be390e41a876aa55e4157d7eb59afcb2478f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f83be390e41a876aa55e4157d7eb59afcb2478f7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/4f4ec4658a5ccb6850a52989d4659b91a3d63775/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:28:52Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:28:52Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Complete roadmap item 1''s real pilot: ours_only vs planner_plus_ours, CONDITIONAL\n\nAll 36 measured cells plus 4 smoke cells ran to completion against the\nfrozen protocol.json (2 targets x 3 scenarios x 2 arms x 3 repetitions).\n46 total top-level sessions, 17.3 serial hours, $276.38 nominal\n(subscription-billed) cost.\n\nMechanical result: preliminary CONDITIONAL, pending human adjudication of\ntarget A''s \"independently verified new failure condition\" escape clause\n(target A showed no complete-rate lift; target B did). adjudication.md\nrecords that pass: the planner''s absorbed deltas on target A were real and\ncorrectly load-bearing within their own sessions, but ours_only''s own\nrepetitions reached at least as good a majority-stable outcome on both\nmeasured scenarios (A-S1, A-S2) without a planner step -- tied on A-S1, and\nactually ahead on A-S2 (see pilot-results.json''s known_scoring_corrections)\n-- so there is no evidence ours_only structurally misses what the planner\ncatches. Ties are not lift, and neither is a target where ours_only leads.\nFinal label: CONDITIONAL. No change to\nskills/playwright-test-generator/playwright-agents.md or any other product\ntext; the Planner step remains optional, not default.\n\nrun_pilot.py''s normalize() had two scoring bugs, both caught before this\nevidence was finalized and fixed with the harness itself: a prefix-only\nV-check match (V_PASS.match) accepted a V5 self-report string as passing\neven though it contained a later disqualifying CANNOT_VERIFY, affecting\nA-S2-planner_plus_ours-r1 (corrected COMPLETE -> PARTIAL, recorded\nalongside the unmutated raw record); and exploration-evidence.json''s\ntarget_commands_outside_allowlist was never read or enforced against\nprotocol.json''s stop_rules, affecting 2 further COMPLETE cells -- reviewed\nagainst each cell''s session narrative (approved-command reuse against\nephemeral temp copies, and a skill-prescribed capability probe) and left as\nCOMPLETE with the finding now logged in scoring.reasons. Both fixes are in\nrun_pilot.py (V_DISQUALIFYING check; a non-verdict-changing allowlist note).\nprotocol.json''s top-level status/result/decision_state fields are synced to\nthe actual frozen-and-completed state instead of stale NOT_RUN placeholders.\n\nTwo real infrastructure incidents are documented rather than hidden: the\nrunner''s keychain OAuth token snapshot expired mid-run (~10:50Z), initially\ncausing two sessions to die with HTTP 401. Fixed forward in run_pilot.py\n(re-read the token immediately before every session launch; stop cleanly\ninstead of launching further cells if rotation doesn''t happen in time) and\nrecovered via the protocol''s single infrastructure-only retry allowance,\nwith the prior 401 records preserved under reruns[]/superseded_runs rather\nthan overwritten. A second, distinct pause (PAUSED_AUTH_FAILURE, proactive\nthis time) interrupted one further cell mid-session; that retry exceeded the\nprotocol''s declared cap of one infrastructure-only retry, so it required and\nreceived explicit operator authorization, recorded in its own rerun reason.\n\nThe macOS account username had leaked into 38 of these artifact files (this\nfile''s pilot-results.json/smoke-results.json plus 33 transcript.jsonl files)\nvia embedded `ls -la` tool output and session-scratchpad paths -- neither\nshape trips pre-push-security.sh''s hardcoded-home check, which only matches\na literal /Users/<user> substring. Redacted to a normalized placeholder\nacross all 38 files per benchmarks/STATUS.md''s own \"new producers must\nredact... real account names\" policy.\n\nAlso checked, using only this pilot''s own archived exploration-evidence.json\nfiles (no new model call): whether roadmap item 5''s deferred candidate arm 1\n(recorded-trace exploration) should now trigger. It does not -- all 17\nunknown-provenance claims and 12 unreached-required-state cells trace to the\nS3 impossible/honesty-control scenario correctly reporting an absent\nfeature, not a real exploration-chain gap; benchmarks/exploration-fallback-v1/README.md\nrecords the finding.\n\nConstraint: a single target cannot rescue the other (frozen decision rule);\ntarget B''s genuine lift cannot promote the overall result to DEFAULT on its\nown.\n\nRejected: accepting the mechanical \"CONDITIONAL unless independently\nverified new failure condition\" preliminary label without the required\nhuman pass over planner-delta.md -- the protocol''s own summary.decision.note\nrequires that pass before any final label is claimed.\n\nConfidence: high for the adjudication reasoning (grounded in the archived\nper-cell majority-stable outcomes, independently re-verified against the raw\ndata after both codex and Fable review); the pilot''s own result is\nexplicitly INCONCLUSIVE-scoped to two targets, not a general claim.\n\nScope-risk: none to shipped product behavior -- CONDITIONAL means no product\ntext changes anywhere.\n\nNot-tested: n/a -- this commit is the evidence archive itself, verified with\na full ci-local.sh and pre-push-security.sh run (secrets, hardcoded\nhome-path leaks, and manifest validity all clean).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cesovo4fM6aN3XcNoH887Q","tree":{"sha":"cd0babd32ad53d1fff267dd3deb6b56432326d3d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/cd0babd32ad53d1fff267dd3deb6b56432326d3d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/4f4ec4658a5ccb6850a52989d4659b91a3d63775","verification":{"payload":"tree cd0babd32ad53d1fff267dd3deb6b56432326d3d\nparent cf7b50dc9e7fb94f2fd4113916c0eaf0e6e4f357\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789194532 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789194532 +0900\n\nComplete roadmap item 1''s real pilot: ours_only vs planner_plus_ours, CONDITIONAL\n\nAll 36 measured cells plus 4 smoke cells ran to completion against the\nfrozen protocol.json (2 targets x 3 scenarios x 2 arms x 3 repetitions).\n46 total top-level sessions, 17.3 serial hours, $276.38 nominal\n(subscription-billed) cost.\n\nMechanical result: preliminary CONDITIONAL, pending human adjudication of\ntarget A''s \"independently verified new failure condition\" escape clause\n(target A showed no complete-rate lift; target B did). adjudication.md\nrecords that pass: the planner''s absorbed deltas on target A were real and\ncorrectly load-bearing within their own sessions, but ours_only''s own\nrepetitions reached at least as good a majority-stable outcome on both\nmeasured scenarios (A-S1, A-S2) without a planner step -- tied on A-S1, and\nactually ahead on A-S2 (see pilot-results.json''s known_scoring_corrections)\n-- so there is no evidence ours_only structurally misses what the planner\ncatches. Ties are not lift, and neither is a target where ours_only leads.\nFinal label: CONDITIONAL. No change to\nskills/playwright-test-generator/playwright-agents.md or any other product\ntext; the Planner step remains optional, not default.\n\nrun_pilot.py''s normalize() had two scoring bugs, both caught before this\nevidence was finalized and fixed with the harness itself: a prefix-only\nV-check match (V_PASS.match) accepted a V5 self-report string as passing\neven though it contained a later disqualifying CANNOT_VERIFY, affecting\nA-S2-planner_plus_ours-r1 (corrected COMPLETE -> PARTIAL, recorded\nalongside the unmutated raw record); and exploration-evidence.json''s\ntarget_commands_outside_allowlist was never read or enforced against\nprotocol.json''s stop_rules, affecting 2 further COMPLETE cells -- reviewed\nagainst each cell''s session narrative (approved-command reuse against\nephemeral temp copies, and a skill-prescribed capability probe) and left as\nCOMPLETE with the finding now logged in scoring.reasons. Both fixes are in\nrun_pilot.py (V_DISQUALIFYING check; a non-verdict-changing allowlist note).\nprotocol.json''s top-level status/result/decision_state fields are synced to\nthe actual frozen-and-completed state instead of stale NOT_RUN placeholders.\n\nTwo real infrastructure incidents are documented rather than hidden: the\nrunner''s keychain OAuth token snapshot expired mid-run (~10:50Z), initially\ncausing two sessions to die with HTTP 401. Fixed forward in run_pilot.py\n(re-read the token immediately before every session launch; stop cleanly\ninstead of launching further cells if rotation doesn''t happen in time) and\nrecovered via the protocol''s single infrastructure-only retry allowance,\nwith the prior 401 records preserved under reruns[]/superseded_runs rather\nthan overwritten. A second, distinct pause (PAUSED_AUTH_FAILURE, proactive\nthis time) interrupted one further cell mid-session; that retry exceeded the\nprotocol''s declared cap of one infrastructure-only retry, so it required and\nreceived explicit operator authorization, recorded in its own rerun reason.\n\nThe macOS account username had leaked into 38 of these artifact files (this\nfile''s pilot-results.json/smoke-results.json plus 33 transcript.jsonl files)\nvia embedded `ls -la` tool output and session-scratchpad paths -- neither\nshape trips pre-push-security.sh''s hardcoded-home check, which only matches\na literal /Users/<user> substring. Redacted to a normalized placeholder\nacross all 38 files per benchmarks/STATUS.md''s own \"new producers must\nredact... real account names\" policy.\n\nAlso checked, using only this pilot''s own archived exploration-evidence.json\nfiles (no new model call): whether roadmap item 5''s deferred candidate arm 1\n(recorded-trace exploration) should now trigger. It does not -- all 17\nunknown-provenance claims and 12 unreached-required-state cells trace to the\nS3 impossible/honesty-control scenario correctly reporting an absent\nfeature, not a real exploration-chain gap; benchmarks/exploration-fallback-v1/README.md\nrecords the finding.\n\nConstraint: a single target cannot rescue the other (frozen decision rule);\ntarget B''s genuine lift cannot promote the overall result to DEFAULT on its\nown.\n\nRejected: accepting the mechanical \"CONDITIONAL unless independently\nverified new failure condition\" preliminary label without the required\nhuman pass over planner-delta.md -- the protocol''s own summary.decision.note\nrequires that pass before any final label is claimed.\n\nConfidence: high for the adjudication reasoning (grounded in the archived\nper-cell majority-stable outcomes, independently re-verified against the raw\ndata after both codex and Fable review); the pilot''s own result is\nexplicitly INCONCLUSIVE-scoped to two targets, not a general claim.\n\nScope-risk: none to shipped product behavior -- CONDITIONAL means no product\ntext changes anywhere.\n\nNot-tested: n/a -- this commit is the evidence archive itself, verified with\na full ci-local.sh and pre-push-security.sh run (secrets, hardcoded\nhome-path leaks, and manifest validity all clean).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cesovo4fM6aN3XcNoH887Q\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQPEkq38zda6Zz9uLbCp3FPd2yIrR3l4bFDu9iMiN43hCGHHQevOAeiqkKiY3QY294s\nuABrPfZvienO4Ihc3DfQU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T12:23:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/4f4ec4658a5ccb6850a52989d4659b91a3d63775","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDRmNGVjNDY1OGE1Y2NiNjg1MGE1Mjk4OWQ0NjU5YjkxYTNkNjM3NzU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/cf7b50dc9e7fb94f2fd4113916c0eaf0e6e4f357","sha":"cf7b50dc9e7fb94f2fd4113916c0eaf0e6e4f357","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/cf7b50dc9e7fb94f2fd4113916c0eaf0e6e4f357"}],"sha":"4f4ec4658a5ccb6850a52989d4659b91a3d63775","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/4f4ec4658a5ccb6850a52989d4659b91a3d63775"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/cf7b50dc9e7fb94f2fd4113916c0eaf0e6e4f357/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:26:07Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:26:07Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Design roadmap items 3, 4, 5, 6 as preregistered protocols, none authorized\n\nFour of the six roadmap items now have falsifiable, frozen-structure designs instead of loose notes -- consistent with how item 1 (ours-vs-planner-pilot-v1) was prepared before it ran. No model call, browser session, or benchmark execution happened for any of these; every protocol.json here has design_only: true and execution_authorized_by_this_file: false.\n\n- benchmarks/healer-perturbation-v1/: Healer-vs-honesty-control comparison (5 perturbations: 3 test-mutators + 2 honesty controls reusing proven fixture-faults operators, 2 arms: official_healer_guarded vs ours_step7). test_perturbations.py (21 unit tests) is wired into ci-local.sh''s Executable fixture contracts stage.\n- benchmarks/subagent-routing-v1/: named-subagent-vs-inline-fallback comparison for e2e-finding-verifier and e2e-failure-classifier, 16 frozen cases across Claude (active) and a designed-but-dormant Codex arm.\n- benchmarks/stryker-feasibility-v1/: promoted from a README-only stub to a full protocol.json for the already-decided REFERENCE_ONLY-by-default Stryker adjunct question. Pins zero skills/*/SKILL.md files -- it makes no model call and invokes no generator/reviewer/debugger/healer/planner arm, so it never competes with items 3/6 for the same frozen surface.\n- benchmarks/exploration-fallback-v1/: two deferred candidate exploration arms (Toss-style recorded-trace conversion, Slack-style adapter-usage logging), each with a concrete re-trigger condition instead of a time-based reconsideration schedule.\n\nConstraint: items 2 and 3 both name ''a planner-arm lift'' as their unlock condition in benchmarks/ours-vs-planner-pilot-v1/README.md. Item 2 is therefore not designed at all here (no protocol below); item 3''s design is recorded but its execution stays unauthorized pending that same condition.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cesovo4fM6aN3XcNoH887Q","tree":{"sha":"2169b12d67c347c3d51a31474a18882d24044f4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/2169b12d67c347c3d51a31474a18882d24044f4b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/cf7b50dc9e7fb94f2fd4113916c0eaf0e6e4f357","verification":{"payload":"tree 2169b12d67c347c3d51a31474a18882d24044f4b\nparent 1863092c0b40e60161df1f85b88a3e4c974817de\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789194367 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789194367 +0900\n\nDesign roadmap items 3, 4, 5, 6 as preregistered protocols, none authorized\n\nFour of the six roadmap items now have falsifiable, frozen-structure designs instead of loose notes -- consistent with how item 1 (ours-vs-planner-pilot-v1) was prepared before it ran. No model call, browser session, or benchmark execution happened for any of these; every protocol.json here has design_only: true and execution_authorized_by_this_file: false.\n\n- benchmarks/healer-perturbation-v1/: Healer-vs-honesty-control comparison (5 perturbations: 3 test-mutators + 2 honesty controls reusing proven fixture-faults operators, 2 arms: official_healer_guarded vs ours_step7). test_perturbations.py (21 unit tests) is wired into ci-local.sh''s Executable fixture contracts stage.\n- benchmarks/subagent-routing-v1/: named-subagent-vs-inline-fallback comparison for e2e-finding-verifier and e2e-failure-classifier, 16 frozen cases across Claude (active) and a designed-but-dormant Codex arm.\n- benchmarks/stryker-feasibility-v1/: promoted from a README-only stub to a full protocol.json for the already-decided REFERENCE_ONLY-by-default Stryker adjunct question. Pins zero skills/*/SKILL.md files -- it makes no model call and invokes no generator/reviewer/debugger/healer/planner arm, so it never competes with items 3/6 for the same frozen surface.\n- benchmarks/exploration-fallback-v1/: two deferred candidate exploration arms (Toss-style recorded-trace conversion, Slack-style adapter-usage logging), each with a concrete re-trigger condition instead of a time-based reconsideration schedule.\n\nConstraint: items 2 and 3 both name ''a planner-arm lift'' as their unlock condition in benchmarks/ours-vs-planner-pilot-v1/README.md. Item 2 is therefore not designed at all here (no protocol below); item 3''s design is recorded but its execution stays unauthorized pending that same condition.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cesovo4fM6aN3XcNoH887Q\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQOc5MW00KOx632pMmLnVUqCfGARoOaoDNXRfXkeaXLuyVMHXDiAHQKAM8InGfyZxcP\n3ck8Qxibvk1HlH9PaGbgo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T12:23:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/cf7b50dc9e7fb94f2fd4113916c0eaf0e6e4f357","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGNmN2I1MGRjOWU3ZmI5NGYyZmQ0MTEzOTE2YzBlYWYwZTZlNGYzNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/1863092c0b40e60161df1f85b88a3e4c974817de","sha":"1863092c0b40e60161df1f85b88a3e4c974817de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/1863092c0b40e60161df1f85b88a3e4c974817de"}],"sha":"cf7b50dc9e7fb94f2fd4113916c0eaf0e6e4f357","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/cf7b50dc9e7fb94f2fd4113916c0eaf0e6e4f357"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/1863092c0b40e60161df1f85b88a3e4c974817de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:25:09Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T06:25:09Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Verify and correct external evidence adoption claims\n\nIndependently re-checked every external-evidence row in docs/llm-generated-e2e-test-evidence.md against what this repo actually implements. NAVER''s ''explain the harness'' framing was never adopted and the claim is removed. Slack''s adapter-comparison claim was unmeasured and is now flagged, cross-referenced to the new benchmarks/exploration-fallback-v1/ stub. Shopify''s writer/verifier framing predated this repo''s own design and is reworded from provenance to convergence.\n\nAlso evaluated a Toss FE platform team talk and a flex.team backend post as candidate adoptions. Both recorded as not adopted with a concrete, falsifiable reason each rather than a general dismissal.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cesovo4fM6aN3XcNoH887Q","tree":{"sha":"6c05ab9446e47538abbcb829809f58f9d4162171","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/6c05ab9446e47538abbcb829809f58f9d4162171"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/1863092c0b40e60161df1f85b88a3e4c974817de","verification":{"payload":"tree 6c05ab9446e47538abbcb829809f58f9d4162171\nparent 8936f6b917904726de2023b31f3183a62a90b563\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789194309 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1789194309 +0900\n\nVerify and correct external evidence adoption claims\n\nIndependently re-checked every external-evidence row in docs/llm-generated-e2e-test-evidence.md against what this repo actually implements. NAVER''s ''explain the harness'' framing was never adopted and the claim is removed. Slack''s adapter-comparison claim was unmeasured and is now flagged, cross-referenced to the new benchmarks/exploration-fallback-v1/ stub. Shopify''s writer/verifier framing predated this repo''s own design and is reworded from provenance to convergence.\n\nAlso evaluated a Toss FE platform team talk and a flex.team backend post as candidate adoptions. Both recorded as not adopted with a concrete, falsifiable reason each rather than a general dismissal.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cesovo4fM6aN3XcNoH887Q\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFG3Go2LS0CK0RDv6GkPNEfs9r+UP7w2bY24nMbBZw0cH1GtCGrEtXMjgrFJesblfG\n5Xntd1BjTYX2L0ZReA8go=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-12T12:23:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/