9-01T14:23:01Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Correct holdout claims and harden CI contracts\n\nCorrect the false account of why reviewer holdout v5 and v6 stalled,\nrestore the live-exploration scope in package metadata, and record identity\npolicy only when an identity check actually ran.\n\nDerive reviewer ordering from the active taxonomy, cite the manifest limits,\nrescale load-sensitive process-cleanup tests, and rename the taxonomy module\nto match its current responsibility.\n\nConstraint: the v1.14.0 tag remains immutable; released notes are corrected\nby the later changelog entry.\nRejected: keep two adjacent corrective commits, or rewrite the tagged release.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: process-cleanup tests now take several seconds longer.\nNot-tested: no v6 matrix was rerun with a manually fetched Claude build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"729d2deac0879a6f586bb83b40453c9a8e346252","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/729d2deac0879a6f586bb83b40453c9a8e346252"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/3dd88ca92be45f2545b0a8a2e69d41c83005dd0c","verification":{"payload":"tree 729d2deac0879a6f586bb83b40453c9a8e346252\nparent d86ac9833d7c92cb62972a530c567d441d3a1d99\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1788272581 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1788272581 +0900\n\nCorrect holdout claims and harden CI contracts\n\nCorrect the false account of why reviewer holdout v5 and v6 stalled,\nrestore the live-exploration scope in package metadata, and record identity\npolicy only when an identity check actually ran.\n\nDerive reviewer ordering from the active taxonomy, cite the manifest limits,\nrescale load-sensitive process-cleanup tests, and rename the taxonomy module\nto match its current responsibility.\n\nConstraint: the v1.14.0 tag remains immutable; released notes are corrected\nby the later changelog entry.\nRejected: keep two adjacent corrective commits, or rewrite the tagged release.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: process-cleanup tests now take several seconds longer.\nNot-tested: no v6 matrix was rerun with a manually fetched Claude build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQCqpA+2kBzPXUDo/K5Q8d8oxVLBC7A9mKKmHtVe5A5NGNFK6DRqPb77rOBgGsOjZKE\nz4knkiTdl5Z6I/i/OfLAE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-01T18:38:01Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/3dd88ca92be45f2545b0a8a2e69d41c83005dd0c","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDNkZDg4Y2E5MmJlNDVmMjU0NWIwYThhMmU2OWQ0MWM4MzAwNWRkMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/d86ac9833d7c92cb62972a530c567d441d3a1d99","sha":"d86ac9833d7c92cb62972a530c567d441d3a1d99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/d86ac9833d7c92cb62972a530c567d441d3a1d99"}],"sha":"3dd88ca92be45f2545b0a8a2e69d41c83005dd0c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/3dd88ca92be45f2545b0a8a2e69d41c83005dd0c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/d86ac9833d7c92cb62972a530c567d441d3a1d99/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:12:43Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-31T16:12:43Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Release 1.15.0: enforce Codex directory rules, stop storing taxonomy in manifests\n\nThree changes, none of which alter skill behavior.\n\nCI now checks the Codex directory submission rules that nothing was checking:\ndescription against 1024 characters, the listing strings against 30,\nlongDescription against 4000, developer name against 80, and category against\nthe supported thirteen-value taxonomy. The repository was violating two of them\nsilently. .codex-plugin/plugin.json declared the category \"Testing\", which is\nnot a supported value, and a 57-character shortDescription against a\n30-character limit. Both are fixed; the category is now \"Developer Tools\".\n\nManifest descriptions stop storing the reviewer taxonomy. All 24 pattern\nphrases previously had to appear in order inside three manifest descriptions,\nwhich made every pattern rename a four-file edit and pushed the description to\n1138 characters, past the submission limit. The canonical order now lives in\nmanifest_phrase_contract.py alone and review.sh still checks all 24 ids,\ntitles, order, and severities against the e2e-reviewer Quick Reference. Nothing\nleft enforcement; it moved from prose to data. Keyword discovery is unaffected\nbecause the 52-entry keywords array and the 818-character longDescription still\ncarry the pattern vocabulary.\n\nEvery public skill gains evals/trigger-evals.json with sixteen cases, eight\nthat must trigger and eight adjacent negatives that must not: a Playwright\nreport with a TimeoutError belongs to the debugger, not the reviewer, and a\nrequest to write new coverage belongs to the generator. review.sh validates\nstructure, unique kebab-case ids, multi-word queries, and the per-label floor,\nand never calls a model.\n\nConstraint: the generator''s live-exploration scope phrase had to stay on a\nsurface something actually reads, so it lives in SKILL.md frontmatter and\nagents/openai.yaml rather than the now-short package description.\nRejected: leading the description with false-green detection — README states\nthat is \"one important part of the review workflow, not the bundle''s entire\npurpose\", so headlining it would misdescribe a four-skill bundle; keeping the\ntaxonomy in manifest prose (blocks directory submission and makes renames a\nfour-file edit); a patch version (public listing copy changed and every skill\npackage gains a file).\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: test-generator-contracts.py pins the package description as an\nexact string, so any future copy edit fails that test rather than a parity\ncheck. Left as-is to keep this change scoped; worth relocating to review.sh\nparity later.\nNot-tested: measured trigger rates. The fixtures are validated structurally\nonly; model-based trigger-rate measurement stays outside ordinary CI by design.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7c3bbef1818b5116bf1accdf00fef4d6478cdef7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/7c3bbef1818b5116bf1accdf00fef4d6478cdef7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/d86ac9833d7c92cb62972a530c567d441d3a1d99","verification":{"payload":"tree 7c3bbef1818b5116bf1accdf00fef4d6478cdef7\nparent 19352df388d340b951d442cb279a788c5d8d977b\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1788192763 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1788192763 +0900\n\nRelease 1.15.0: enforce Codex directory rules, stop storing taxonomy in manifests\n\nThree changes, none of which alter skill behavior.\n\nCI now checks the Codex directory submission rules that nothing was checking:\ndescription against 1024 characters, the listing strings against 30,\nlongDescription against 4000, developer name against 80, and category against\nthe supported thirteen-value taxonomy. The repository was violating two of them\nsilently. .codex-plugin/plugin.json declared the category \"Testing\", which is\nnot a supported value, and a 57-character shortDescription against a\n30-character limit. Both are fixed; the category is now \"Developer Tools\".\n\nManifest descriptions stop storing the reviewer taxonomy. All 24 pattern\nphrases previously had to appear in order inside three manifest descriptions,\nwhich made every pattern rename a four-file edit and pushed the description to\n1138 characters, past the submission limit. The canonical order now lives in\nmanifest_phrase_contract.py alone and review.sh still checks all 24 ids,\ntitles, order, and severities against the e2e-reviewer Quick Reference. Nothing\nleft enforcement; it moved from prose to data. Keyword discovery is unaffected\nbecause the 52-entry keywords array and the 818-character longDescription still\ncarry the pattern vocabulary.\n\nEvery public skill gains evals/trigger-evals.json with sixteen cases, eight\nthat must trigger and eight adjacent negatives that must not: a Playwright\nreport with a TimeoutError belongs to the debugger, not the reviewer, and a\nrequest to write new coverage belongs to the generator. review.sh validates\nstructure, unique kebab-case ids, multi-word queries, and the per-label floor,\nand never calls a model.\n\nConstraint: the generator''s live-exploration scope phrase had to stay on a\nsurface something actually reads, so it lives in SKILL.md frontmatter and\nagents/openai.yaml rather than the now-short package description.\nRejected: leading the description with false-green detection — README states\nthat is \"one important part of the review workflow, not the bundle''s entire\npurpose\", so headlining it would misdescribe a four-skill bundle; keeping the\ntaxonomy in manifest prose (blocks directory submission and makes renames a\nfour-file edit); a patch version (public listing copy changed and every skill\npackage gains a file).\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: test-generator-contracts.py pins the package description as an\nexact string, so any future copy edit fails that test rather than a parity\ncheck. Left as-is to keep this change scoped; worth relocating to review.sh\nparity later.\nNot-tested: measured trigger rates. The fixtures are validated structurally\nonly; model-based trigger-rate measurement stays outside ordinary CI by design.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLRg5x25LgA4okYZ9cWqZDMPgqqr2umtbe9WNml/w+9pLghKTJZQhiJaSSFa1gZi8C\nkYxsag1AFc/gPd0r8oAAQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-31T16:13:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/d86ac9833d7c92cb62972a530c567d441d3a1d99","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGQ4NmFjOTgzM2Q3YzkyY2I2Mjk3MmE1MzBjNTY3ZDQ0MWQzYTFkOTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/19352df388d340b951d442cb279a788c5d8d977b","sha":"19352df388d340b951d442cb279a788c5d8d977b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/19352df388d340b951d442cb279a788c5d8d977b"}],"sha":"d86ac9833d7c92cb62972a530c567d441d3a1d99","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/d86ac9833d7c92cb62972a530c567d441d3a1d99"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/19352df388d340b951d442cb279a788c5d8d977b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T15:39:14Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T15:39:14Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Release 1.14.0: make agents/openai.yaml the schema Codex actually reads\n\ncodex-cli reads skills/<name>/agents/openai.yaml for every discovered skill,\nplugin-installed or not, and its parser accepts only interface, policy, and\ndependencies. The repository shipped name, description, metadata, and a\ntop-level allow_implicit_invocation instead. That loader has no\ndeny_unknown_fields and warns then falls back to defaults, so all four files\nwere inert: no display name, no short description, no default prompt in the\nCodex UI, and no error anywhere saying so.\n\nVerified after the fix by reinstalling from this tree and opening a Codex\nsession: all four now render as \"E2E Reviewer — Audit E2E tests and diffs\" and\nthe rest, alongside skills that already used the official shape.\n\nallow_implicit_invocation moves under policy, where it is read. Its default is\ntrue, so behavior is unchanged; the field only matters when set to false. The\ntrigger surface was never this file — SKILL.md frontmatter is, and already\ncarries longer text than the copy being removed.\n\nplaywright-test-generator keeps its live-exploration scope phrase, moved from\nthe discarded description into interface.default_prompt, so the V5-T2 safety\ncontract stays on a surface something actually reads.\n\nThe repository''s own fail-closed parser was duplicated in review.sh and\npre-push-security.sh; it now lives once in scripts/ci/lib/skill_metadata_contract.py\nand adds the runtime length and brand_color limits, because codex drops an\nover-length field rather than truncating it. The directory binding the removed\nname field used to provide is now the $<skill> invocation required in each\ndefault_prompt. Four mutation cases cover unknown top-level keys, a missing\ninterface, a non-boolean policy value, and a dropped invocation.\n\nREADME documents what Codex can and cannot install: plugins cannot deliver\ne2e-finding-verifier or e2e-failure-classifier, because the manifest has no\nagents field and agent roles load only from config layers. The two supported\npaths are the global installer and a repository checkout. Translations follow.\n\nConstraint: skills/<name>/agents/openai.yaml is a fixed path the validator and\nthe runtime both read, so the repository schema and the shipped schema cannot\ndiverge. v5/v6 benchmark digests forbid editing frozen protocol inputs.\nRejected: generating the official shape at packaging time (makes the committed\ntree differ from the artifact, which is the drift this repository''s CI exists to\nprevent); keeping the invented schema (it was silently discarded); dropping the\nscope phrase with the description (removes a safety claim a past review\nrequired).\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: review.sh and pre-push-security.sh now import a shared module;\nbenchmarks/reviewer-holdout-v3/evidence-status.json records the current skill\ndigest and was refreshed because the skill changed.\nNot-tested: no Codex plugin marketplace install was performed; verification used\nthe skills CLI install path and a live Codex session listing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eedcba453cc55e81ee95b13a129a630e9b884313","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/eedcba453cc55e81ee95b13a129a630e9b884313"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/19352df388d340b951d442cb279a788c5d8d977b","verification":{"payload":"tree eedcba453cc55e81ee95b13a129a630e9b884313\nparent eb6b1825098fce238eac07006a30d67a8de1adeb\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1788017954 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1788017954 +0900\n\nRelease 1.14.0: make agents/openai.yaml the schema Codex actually reads\n\ncodex-cli reads skills/<name>/agents/openai.yaml for every discovered skill,\nplugin-installed or not, and its parser accepts only interface, policy, and\ndependencies. The repository shipped name, description, metadata, and a\ntop-level allow_implicit_invocation instead. That loader has no\ndeny_unknown_fields and warns then falls back to defaults, so all four files\nwere inert: no display name, no short description, no default prompt in the\nCodex UI, and no error anywhere saying so.\n\nVerified after the fix by reinstalling from this tree and opening a Codex\nsession: all four now render as \"E2E Reviewer — Audit E2E tests and diffs\" and\nthe rest, alongside skills that already used the official shape.\n\nallow_implicit_invocation moves under policy, where it is read. Its default is\ntrue, so behavior is unchanged; the field only matters when set to false. The\ntrigger surface was never this file — SKILL.md frontmatter is, and already\ncarries longer text than the copy being removed.\n\nplaywright-test-generator keeps its live-exploration scope phrase, moved from\nthe discarded description into interface.default_prompt, so the V5-T2 safety\ncontract stays on a surface something actually reads.\n\nThe repository''s own fail-closed parser was duplicated in review.sh and\npre-push-security.sh; it now lives once in scripts/ci/lib/skill_metadata_contract.py\nand adds the runtime length and brand_color limits, because codex drops an\nover-length field rather than truncating it. The directory binding the removed\nname field used to provide is now the $<skill> invocation required in each\ndefault_prompt. Four mutation cases cover unknown top-level keys, a missing\ninterface, a non-boolean policy value, and a dropped invocation.\n\nREADME documents what Codex can and cannot install: plugins cannot deliver\ne2e-finding-verifier or e2e-failure-classifier, because the manifest has no\nagents field and agent roles load only from config layers. The two supported\npaths are the global installer and a repository checkout. Translations follow.\n\nConstraint: skills/<name>/agents/openai.yaml is a fixed path the validator and\nthe runtime both read, so the repository schema and the shipped schema cannot\ndiverge. v5/v6 benchmark digests forbid editing frozen protocol inputs.\nRejected: generating the official shape at packaging time (makes the committed\ntree differ from the artifact, which is the drift this repository''s CI exists to\nprevent); keeping the invented schema (it was silently discarded); dropping the\nscope phrase with the description (removes a safety claim a past review\nrequired).\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: review.sh and pre-push-security.sh now import a shared module;\nbenchmarks/reviewer-holdout-v3/evidence-status.json records the current skill\ndigest and was refreshed because the skill changed.\nNot-tested: no Codex plugin marketplace install was performed; verification used\nthe skills CLI install path and a live Codex session listing.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQGBv303C0n/5j4czWPqUGZSrvyQgGQS5JpVmWWiTUkIkAyRlxNqx0jZRxKR2gPF1vv\n/HhXJUyVspdDUTfiqWRgY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T15:39:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/19352df388d340b951d442cb279a788c5d8d977b","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDE5MzUyZGYzODhkMzQwYjk1MWQ0NDJjYjI3OWE3ODhjNWQ4ZDk3N2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/eb6b1825098fce238eac07006a30d67a8de1adeb","sha":"eb6b1825098fce238eac07006a30d67a8de1adeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/eb6b1825098fce238eac07006a30d67a8de1adeb"}],"sha":"19352df388d340b951d442cb279a788c5d8d977b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/19352df388d340b951d442cb279a788c5d8d977b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/eb6b1825098fce238eac07006a30d67a8de1adeb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:38:58Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-29T14:38:58Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Archive holdout v6 as terminated, and stop exact CLI pins from expiring\n\nProtocol v6 preregistered `Claude Code 2.1.239`. That build has been pruned\n(retained: 2.1.247, 2.1.248, 2.1.250, 2.1.251), the runner enforces identity by\nequality, and six of v6''s nine cells need the Claude host, so the matrix can\nnever complete. This is the second protocol lost the same way: v5 pinned\n2.1.220.\n\nArchive what survived instead of deleting a partial run. Five of nine reports\nremain, two execution-complete. The README states the termination reason, marks\nthe `full` arm as having no usable measurement on any host (full-fable lost 22\nof 60 runs, which suppresses majority-stable labels and depresses its unique\nrecall as an artifact, not a result), and names the single defensible contrast:\nno-skill-opus against catalog-only-opus, same host and model, zero\ninfrastructure errors. A `FAIL` on a control arm is the expected outcome, since\none threshold set applies to every arm.\n\nAdd an `execution_identity.version_policy` of `exact` (default) or `minimum`.\nUnder `minimum` the runner accepts the pinned build or later and records both\nthe resolved identity and an `execution_identity_match`, so drift is written\ndown rather than silent. Exact pinning never bought reproducibility once a build\nis pruned; it only guaranteed expiry. The property an arm comparison needs — one\nidentity across every cell of one matrix — is already enforced by the comparator\nvia arm_runner_identity_mismatch and arm_runner_binding_mismatch plus the\n12-hour window, and never depended on the cut-time constant.\n\nv5 and v6 stay `exact`; their frozen JSON and pinned digests are untouched.\n\nConstraint: v5/v6 are frozen with pinned SHA-256 digests, so the new key is\nemitted into the expected manifest only for protocols that declare a non-default\npolicy. Claude Code and codex both auto-update and prune, which is what makes an\nexact pin expire.\nRejected: relaxing v5/v6 retroactively (breaks their freeze and digests);\nremoving the cut-time check entirely (loses the version floor); pinning at\nmatrix start (needs cross-invocation state the runner has no place for).\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: compare-reviewer-holdouts.py now forwards a policy argument; reports\ngain two optional keys, added to REPORT_OPTIONAL_KEYS so the five archived\nreports still load.\nNot-tested: no live matrix was run under `minimum` — no protocol declares it\nyet. The archived logs were force-added past a global `*.log` ignore.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4c68bf33010867f142889ee8e35f4beffe5a9218","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/4c68bf33010867f142889ee8e35f4beffe5a9218"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/eb6b1825098fce238eac07006a30d67a8de1adeb","verification":{"payload":"tree 4c68bf33010867f142889ee8e35f4beffe5a9218\nparent 4e713f0a63e6c23dab495280561615ef1ffbd3eb\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1788014338 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1788014338 +0900\n\nArchive holdout v6 as terminated, and stop exact CLI pins from expiring\n\nProtocol v6 preregistered `Claude Code 2.1.239`. That build has been pruned\n(retained: 2.1.247, 2.1.248, 2.1.250, 2.1.251), the runner enforces identity by\nequality, and six of v6''s nine cells need the Claude host, so the matrix can\nnever complete. This is the second protocol lost the same way: v5 pinned\n2.1.220.\n\nArchive what survived instead of deleting a partial run. Five of nine reports\nremain, two execution-complete. The README states the termination reason, marks\nthe `full` arm as having no usable measurement on any host (full-fable lost 22\nof 60 runs, which suppresses majority-stable labels and depresses its unique\nrecall as an artifact, not a result), and names the single defensible contrast:\nno-skill-opus against catalog-only-opus, same host and model, zero\ninfrastructure errors. A `FAIL` on a control arm is the expected outcome, since\none threshold set applies to every arm.\n\nAdd an `execution_identity.version_policy` of `exact` (default) or `minimum`.\nUnder `minimum` the runner accepts the pinned build or later and records both\nthe resolved identity and an `execution_identity_match`, so drift is written\ndown rather than silent. Exact pinning never bought reproducibility once a build\nis pruned; it only guaranteed expiry. The property an arm comparison needs — one\nidentity across every cell of one matrix — is already enforced by the comparator\nvia arm_runner_identity_mismatch and arm_runner_binding_mismatch plus the\n12-hour window, and never depended on the cut-time constant.\n\nv5 and v6 stay `exact`; their frozen JSON and pinned digests are untouched.\n\nConstraint: v5/v6 are frozen with pinned SHA-256 digests, so the new key is\nemitted into the expected manifest only for protocols that declare a non-default\npolicy. Claude Code and codex both auto-update and prune, which is what makes an\nexact pin expire.\nRejected: relaxing v5/v6 retroactively (breaks their freeze and digests);\nremoving the cut-time check entirely (loses the version floor); pinning at\nmatrix start (needs cross-invocation state the runner has no place for).\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: compare-reviewer-holdouts.py now forwards a policy argument; reports\ngain two optional keys, added to REPORT_OPTIONAL_KEYS so the five archived\nreports still load.\nNot-tested: no live matrix was run under `minimum` — no protocol declares it\nyet. The archived logs were force-added past a global `*.log` ignore.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIfvukfWZhJXXzGvpb2ftjzT3HGZfjkh90bNoAfIhJg2Idzd88WkXQFakvGK4GfOWU\nZutoV0P4/XB4A6uFYtSAQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-29T15:39:38Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/eb6b1825098fce238eac07006a30d67a8de1adeb","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGViNmIxODI1MDk4ZmNlMjM4ZWFjMDcwMDZhMzBkNjdhOGRlMWFkZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/4e713f0a63e6c23dab495280561615ef1ffbd3eb","sha":"4e713f0a63e6c23dab495280561615ef1ffbd3eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/4e713f0a63e6c23dab495280561615ef1ffbd3eb"}],"sha":"eb6b1825098fce238eac07006a30d67a8de1adeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/eb6b1825098fce238eac07006a30d67a8de1adeb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/4e713f0a63e6c23dab495280561615ef1ffbd3eb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T23:58:30Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T23:58:30Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Cut reviewer holdout protocol v6 and stop stale bytecode masking pins\n\nv5 preregistered `Claude Code 2.1.220`. That build is no longer retained, and\nv5 requires a complete three-host matrix, so v5 can never finish. v6 reuses the\nv5 corpus byte-for-byte — its case and corpus digests are identical — and\nchanges only the frozen CLI identity, which is what v5''s own freeze policy\nprescribes for a later edit. No v5 result had been produced, so nothing is\nrefitted after the fact, and no v6 result is claimed either.\n\nThe runner''s frozen execution identity was a v5-only literal. It is now a\nper-protocol table, so each version stays pinned to the builds it was cut\nagainst. Mutation-checked in both directions: v6 declaring v5''s versions, v5\ndeclaring v6''s, and an invented version are all rejected.\n\nSeparately, `ci-local.sh` now drops inherited `__pycache__` trees before\nverification. Python invalidates a cached `.pyc` by source mtime, which misses\nan edit made in the same second as the cache. The pinned-input check reported a\nprotocol digest that existed nowhere in the repository — a stale cache was\nserving a retired pin to the test whose only job is to catch that.\n\nConstraint: the eval scripts pass a strict environment allowlist, so exporting\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE does not reach them; dropping the caches is the half\nthat works, and the comment says so rather than implying belt-and-braces.\nRejected: relaxing `runner_identity_matches` to accept minor-version drift —\nthat removes the meaning of preregistering an identity at all. Rejected:\ndowngrading the installed Claude Code to 2.1.220 to revive v5, which would\ndegrade the daily-driver install to serve a retired protocol.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none for v5 — its literal identity and digests are unchanged and\nstill validate.\nNot-tested: no v6 matrix has been run. A single-case smoke against v6 completed\nwith codex 0.149.0 at an explicit versioned path (tp=1, fp=0, no infrastructure\nerrors) and is not evidence.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e7ac43f842acb787598c373067b6b7990b9babeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/e7ac43f842acb787598c373067b6b7990b9babeb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/4e713f0a63e6c23dab495280561615ef1ffbd3eb","verification":{"payload":"tree e7ac43f842acb787598c373067b6b7990b9babeb\nparent 1b11cf31d2f56c4df69e62250b75c5930d2843dc\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1787356710 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1787356710 +0900\n\nCut reviewer holdout protocol v6 and stop stale bytecode masking pins\n\nv5 preregistered `Claude Code 2.1.220`. That build is no longer retained, and\nv5 requires a complete three-host matrix, so v5 can never finish. v6 reuses the\nv5 corpus byte-for-byte — its case and corpus digests are identical — and\nchanges only the frozen CLI identity, which is what v5''s own freeze policy\nprescribes for a later edit. No v5 result had been produced, so nothing is\nrefitted after the fact, and no v6 result is claimed either.\n\nThe runner''s frozen execution identity was a v5-only literal. It is now a\nper-protocol table, so each version stays pinned to the builds it was cut\nagainst. Mutation-checked in both directions: v6 declaring v5''s versions, v5\ndeclaring v6''s, and an invented version are all rejected.\n\nSeparately, `ci-local.sh` now drops inherited `__pycache__` trees before\nverification. Python invalidates a cached `.pyc` by source mtime, which misses\nan edit made in the same second as the cache. The pinned-input check reported a\nprotocol digest that existed nowhere in the repository — a stale cache was\nserving a retired pin to the test whose only job is to catch that.\n\nConstraint: the eval scripts pass a strict environment allowlist, so exporting\nPYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE does not reach them; dropping the caches is the half\nthat works, and the comment says so rather than implying belt-and-braces.\nRejected: relaxing `runner_identity_matches` to accept minor-version drift —\nthat removes the meaning of preregistering an identity at all. Rejected:\ndowngrading the installed Claude Code to 2.1.220 to revive v5, which would\ndegrade the daily-driver install to serve a retired protocol.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none for v5 — its literal identity and digests are unchanged and\nstill validate.\nNot-tested: no v6 matrix has been run. A single-case smoke against v6 completed\nwith codex 0.149.0 at an explicit versioned path (tp=1, fp=0, no infrastructure\nerrors) and is not evidence.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQBU4JcxDEV3ajY6AgACftxi1oTzjbmSzHmc/q93nUG30Hgct0iaZKhFSxV515Tj8oY\nPbRGepV5ZMSXc9NKRMvQg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-22T01:22:36Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/4e713f0a63e6c23dab495280561615ef1ffbd3eb","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDRlNzEzZjBhNjNlNmMyM2RhYjQ5NTI4MDU2MTYxNWVmMWZmYmQzZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/1b11cf31d2f56c4df69e62250b75c5930d2843dc","sha":"1b11cf31d2f56c4df69e62250b75c5930d2843dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/1b11cf31d2f56c4df69e62250b75c5930d2843dc"}],"sha":"4e713f0a63e6c23dab495280561615ef1ffbd3eb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/4e713f0a63e6c23dab495280561615ef1ffbd3eb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/1b11cf31d2f56c4df69e62250b75c5930d2843dc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T02:53:32Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T02:53:32Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Stop pipefail from reporting a successful match as a failed check\n\n`printf ... | grep -q` returns 141 under `set -o pipefail` whenever grep finds\nits match early enough to close the pipe before printf finishes writing. That\nonly happens once the output exceeds the pipe buffer, so the same call site\nbehaves correctly on small inputs and inverts its answer on large ones.\n\nThe scanner''s ESLint tier was the worst case: eslint exits 0 when it reports\nonly warnings, so a long warning run returned 141, took the \"no findings\"\nbranch, and dropped every Tier 1 hit. That is the silent-always-pass class the\nscanner exists to catch. `test-parity.sh` absence assertions passed without\nchecking, `pr-preflight.sh` flagged an unchanged test title as renamed, and\n`codex-smoke.sh` reported a correct model answer as a failed check — the last\nof these is the intermittent cypress-debugger F2 failure, now explained.\n\nAll four now match with a native `[[ ]]` test and no pipe.\n\nAlso isolate `codex-smoke.sh` from the operator''s MCP servers and make a nonzero\nexit state whether the expected token was present anyway. A failing MCP server\nemitted a fatal transport error into the run, and the previous message dumped\noutput that contradicted its own failure line.\n\nConstraint: `scan.sh` ships standalone, so the fix has to be a bash builtin\nrather than a shared helper. The eslint test needed alternation, expressed as\ntwo `[[ ]]` comparisons rather than a regex.\nRejected: keeping grep and appending `|| [ $? -eq 141 ]` — 141 is also what a\ngenuinely killed grep returns, so it would mask real failures. Rejected:\ndropping `pipefail`, which these scripts rely on elsewhere.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: `scan.sh` Tier 1 now prints findings in warning-only eslint runs\nthat previously printed \"no findings\"; those runs were under-reporting.\nNot-tested: the eslint warning-only path has no fixture, so the scanner fix is\nverified by mechanism and by the reproduced 141 rather than end to end.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7178beac7bd855c6fde6452ff5f69424a11efc23","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/7178beac7bd855c6fde6452ff5f69424a11efc23"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/1b11cf31d2f56c4df69e62250b75c5930d2843dc","verification":{"payload":"tree 7178beac7bd855c6fde6452ff5f69424a11efc23\nparent 9447092b5862b9749d1667f8db69aac5f78854e1\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1787194412 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1787194412 +0900\n\nStop pipefail from reporting a successful match as a failed check\n\n`printf ... | grep -q` returns 141 under `set -o pipefail` whenever grep finds\nits match early enough to close the pipe before printf finishes writing. That\nonly happens once the output exceeds the pipe buffer, so the same call site\nbehaves correctly on small inputs and inverts its answer on large ones.\n\nThe scanner''s ESLint tier was the worst case: eslint exits 0 when it reports\nonly warnings, so a long warning run returned 141, took the \"no findings\"\nbranch, and dropped every Tier 1 hit. That is the silent-always-pass class the\nscanner exists to catch. `test-parity.sh` absence assertions passed without\nchecking, `pr-preflight.sh` flagged an unchanged test title as renamed, and\n`codex-smoke.sh` reported a correct model answer as a failed check — the last\nof these is the intermittent cypress-debugger F2 failure, now explained.\n\nAll four now match with a native `[[ ]]` test and no pipe.\n\nAlso isolate `codex-smoke.sh` from the operator''s MCP servers and make a nonzero\nexit state whether the expected token was present anyway. A failing MCP server\nemitted a fatal transport error into the run, and the previous message dumped\noutput that contradicted its own failure line.\n\nConstraint: `scan.sh` ships standalone, so the fix has to be a bash builtin\nrather than a shared helper. The eslint test needed alternation, expressed as\ntwo `[[ ]]` comparisons rather than a regex.\nRejected: keeping grep and appending `|| [ $? -eq 141 ]` — 141 is also what a\ngenuinely killed grep returns, so it would mask real failures. Rejected:\ndropping `pipefail`, which these scripts rely on elsewhere.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: `scan.sh` Tier 1 now prints findings in warning-only eslint runs\nthat previously printed \"no findings\"; those runs were under-reporting.\nNot-tested: the eslint warning-only path has no fixture, so the scanner fix is\nverified by mechanism and by the reproduced 141 rather than end to end.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQFl2GtAENdd841B45xWZah1FAnMGaPC2lan+/cQB11SNK7u2kLRLkx348ur0OdroR1\nM9teT8i+nyNbo4qyp8hAs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T10:50:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/1b11cf31d2f56c4df69e62250b75c5930d2843dc","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDFiMTFjZjMxZDJmNTZjNGRmNjllNjIyNTBiNzVjNTkzMGQyODQzZGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/9447092b5862b9749d1667f8db69aac5f78854e1","sha":"9447092b5862b9749d1667f8db69aac5f78854e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/9447092b5862b9749d1667f8db69aac5f78854e1"}],"sha":"1b11cf31d2f56c4df69e62250b75c5930d2843dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/1b11cf31d2f56c4df69e62250b75c5930d2843dc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/9447092b5862b9749d1667f8db69aac5f78854e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-20T01:02:57Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-20T01:02:57Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Release 1.13.0: scanner scope fix, frozen review phases, agent installers\n\nScope the scanner''s `evals/files/` and `scripts/ci/fixtures/` exclusion to\nscans whose target is itself an e2e-skills checkout. The exclusion was\nunconditional, so any project using those directory names had its real tests\nsilently skipped. The fingerprint reads the scanned project, not the scanner''s\nown location, so a symlinked and a copied install answer identically.\n\nResolve the scanner''s own `$0` through symlinks for sibling-file lookup. Bash''s\nlogical `cd` made `pwd -P` unable to recover the real directory, which silently\ndeleted the ast-grep tier along with its own \"not run\" notice.\n\nFreeze the independent-review v5 and v6 contract tests against the source\nsnapshot each phase actually reviewed. Both phases are closed, so rebuilding\nthe packet from the working tree gated today''s product on a retired budget and\nfailed permanently once a later change legitimately grew the same surfaces.\n\nAdd `install-claude-agents.sh` so the two subagents reach Claude Code without a\nplugin install, which would load a second copy of all four skill descriptions\ninto every session. Fix the Codex installer''s ownership marker, which stopped\nrecognising its own earlier output after the header was renamed.\n\nConstraint: Agent Skills frontmatter fixes the top-level key set; version and\nframework metadata must stay under `metadata` as comma-joined strings. Claude\nCode discovers user-level subagents only by frontmatter `name:`.\nRejected: deriving the self-repo decision from the scanner''s install location —\nmeasured 0 hits vs 256 hits / 12 P0 between a symlinked and a copied install of\nidentical input. Rejected: a v11 protocol to fix the v5/v6 budget failure — v5\nand v6 are separately hash-pinned and each would still measure the live tree.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: projects that vendored this repository''s fixture directory names\nnow receive findings there that were previously suppressed.\nNot-tested: the codex-smoke cypress-debugger F2 check reports FAIL while its\nown printed output contains the expected token; smoke is not part of ci-local.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"27d1902117e2f6a935a39f7425bde844a270add7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/27d1902117e2f6a935a39f7425bde844a270add7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/9447092b5862b9749d1667f8db69aac5f78854e1","verification":{"payload":"tree 27d1902117e2f6a935a39f7425bde844a270add7\nparent 24dbfda62339839624e233f377c790c594e653c4\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1787187777 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1787187777 +0900\n\nRelease 1.13.0: scanner scope fix, frozen review phases, agent installers\n\nScope the scanner''s `evals/files/` and `scripts/ci/fixtures/` exclusion to\nscans whose target is itself an e2e-skills checkout. The exclusion was\nunconditional, so any project using those directory names had its real tests\nsilently skipped. The fingerprint reads the scanned project, not the scanner''s\nown location, so a symlinked and a copied install answer identically.\n\nResolve the scanner''s own `$0` through symlinks for sibling-file lookup. Bash''s\nlogical `cd` made `pwd -P` unable to recover the real directory, which silently\ndeleted the ast-grep tier along with its own \"not run\" notice.\n\nFreeze the independent-review v5 and v6 contract tests against the source\nsnapshot each phase actually reviewed. Both phases are closed, so rebuilding\nthe packet from the working tree gated today''s product on a retired budget and\nfailed permanently once a later change legitimately grew the same surfaces.\n\nAdd `install-claude-agents.sh` so the two subagents reach Claude Code without a\nplugin install, which would load a second copy of all four skill descriptions\ninto every session. Fix the Codex installer''s ownership marker, which stopped\nrecognising its own earlier output after the header was renamed.\n\nConstraint: Agent Skills frontmatter fixes the top-level key set; version and\nframework metadata must stay under `metadata` as comma-joined strings. Claude\nCode discovers user-level subagents only by frontmatter `name:`.\nRejected: deriving the self-repo decision from the scanner''s install location —\nmeasured 0 hits vs 256 hits / 12 P0 between a symlinked and a copied install of\nidentical input. Rejected: a v11 protocol to fix the v5/v6 budget failure — v5\nand v6 are separately hash-pinned and each would still measure the live tree.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: projects that vendored this repository''s fixture directory names\nnow receive findings there that were previously suppressed.\nNot-tested: the codex-smoke cypress-debugger F2 check reports FAIL while its\nown printed output contains the expected token; smoke is not part of ci-local.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQLBZv5DUc3gcyX7pkYZtyowurknKdVg3DJoJ2dW4h5RkXFnRiPkg0eqdSy/PuriO5c\nCtk5AJ/VqxdZMdDilIDg4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T10:50:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/9447092b5862b9749d1667f8db69aac5f78854e1","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDk0NDcwOTJiNTg2MmI5NzQ5ZDE2NjdmOGRiNjlhYWM1Zjc4ODU0ZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/24dbfda62339839624e233f377c790c594e653c4","sha":"24dbfda62339839624e233f377c790c594e653c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/24dbfda62339839624e233f377c790c594e653c4"}],"sha":"9447092b5862b9749d1667f8db69aac5f78854e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/9447092b5862b9749d1667f8db69aac5f78854e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/24dbfda62339839624e233f377c790c594e653c4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-17T05:24:05Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-17T05:47:41Z","email":"16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Add PR/diff-scoped review mode to e2e-reviewer\n\nThe reviewer now classifies a request as full mode (a suite, directory, or\nrepository) or diff mode (a PR, patch, range, or changed-file list). In diff\nmode changed Playwright/Cypress artifacts are the review scope, unchanged\nfiles are context, and every finding carries an introduced / worsened /\npre-existing attribution. Only introduced and causally worsened findings\nreach blockers, totals, and top priorities; pre-existing findings stay\nadvisory. A mandatory Review Scope and Evidence header records what was and\nwas not verified, keeping static scanner coverage distinct from\ntarget-controlled runtime evidence.\n\nscan.sh now rejects multiple scan roots instead of silently ignoring extras,\nwhich is what lets diff mode invoke it once per changed artifact.\n\nFixture exclusion no longer applies to every scan. A target project that\nhappens to contain evals/files/ or scripts/ci/fixtures/ had its real tests\nsilently skipped, which is the exact failure class this scanner exists to\ncatch. Exclusion is now decided by fingerprinting the SCANNED PROJECT as an\ne2e-skills checkout. It deliberately does not use the scanner''s own location:\nreinstall-skills.sh installs real copies and the documented manual path\nsymlinks the skill, so a location-derived answer makes identical input\nproduce different findings depending on how the tool was installed.\n\nSeparately, `$0` is now resolved through symlinks before deriving the\nscanner''s sibling paths. Bash''s `cd` is logical, so ASTGREP_RULES_DIR\npreviously pointed at a nonexistent directory under symlinked invocation;\nbecause the Tier 2 branch and its \"not run\" notice both gate on `-d` that\npath, Tier 2 vanished without printing anything. Both scanner-relative paths\nnow derive from one resolved SCANNER_DIR_REAL, which locates files only.\n\nConstraint: independent-review protocols v5 and v6 cap the review packet at\n850,000 transformed bytes, every entry in their allowlists is required, and\nboth are hash-pinned preregistrations that keep measuring the live product.\nHEAD held only 5,125B of margin. The bytes were therefore freed from\nprovenance rather than from the feature contract or manifest parity strings:\nupstream-rule-sources.md was compressed with every source link, pattern-ID\nmapping and qualification preserved, and the 2026-08-16 source-pass decision\nlog moved here, where this repository''s commit protocol says decision records\nbelong. Final margin is 236B, so the next growth needs a real answer rather\nthan another squeeze.\n\nDecisions from that source pass, recorded here rather than shipped in the\nskill''s reference set:\n- Keep diff attribution, the static-versus-runtime evidence boundary, and the\n  smallest V3 behavior fault supported by repository source, a trace, or\n  observed network evidence that should fail one unchanged load-bearing\n  assertion.\n- No new smell ID: these sources strengthen workflow and verification\n  provenance; none establishes a new deterministic anti-pattern.\n- No new tool or service dependencies. StrykerJS, Cypress Cloud, and vendor\n  agent workflows are precedents only.\n- No scoring by AI provenance. Model, co-author, or prompt provenance is\n  reproducibility metadata, not evidence a finding is valid or severe.\n- A proposed fault is not runtime evidence until an exact target-controlled\n  command runs and the expected assertion fails for the declared reason.\n- General model-evaluation platforms stay secondary. OpenAI Evals can inform\n  evaluation design but is not a browser-E2E contract.\n\nRejected: deciding self-repo from the scanner''s own location. An earlier\nrevision of this change did exactly that. Measured against c0b6ed1 with the\nskill tree copied out and run over this repository, the installed copy went\nfrom 0 hits to 256 hits / 12 P0 including 5 focused-test P0s, breaking the\ndocumented verify-reviewer flow while an in-repo run of the same scanner\nreported nothing.\nRejected: minting a protocol v11 with a raised budget. Measurement showed it\nwould not fix the byte failure, because v5 and v6 are separately pinned and\nkeep enforcing their own caps against the current product.\nRejected: moving verify_result_digest_provenance() into the COMPLETE branch.\nThat would delete the check in the INCOMPLETE state it actually runs in; its\ninputs are now named explicitly so a missing artifact fails closed with a\nclear message instead of a raw FileNotFoundError.\nRejected: dropping \"with concrete fixes\" from the README reviewer row. The\nthree translations kept it, so the canonical English was the outlier.\n\nConfidence: high for the scanner fixes, which are reproduced against the\nprevious revision, fixed, and mutation-tested; medium for the diff-mode\ncontract, which is specified and eval-covered but has no accuracy measurement.\nScope-risk: fixture exclusion now depends on the scanned project''s marker\nfiles, so an e2e-skills checkout missing AGENTS.md or the two other\nfingerprint paths would report its own fixtures. Downstream projects that\npreviously benefited from the unconditional exclusion will start seeing hits\nunder evals/files/ and scripts/ci/fixtures/, which is the intended correction.\nNot-tested: no live model run of diff mode; the v3 holdout reports remain\nstale against the current skill digest and no accuracy claim is made.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ad87761e4ae4adb76b0bf6f88af1d956e56c7f92","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/ad87761e4ae4adb76b0bf6f88af1d956e56c7f92"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/24dbfda62339839624e233f377c790c594e653c4","verification":{"payload":"tree ad87761e4ae4adb76b0bf6f88af1d956e56c7f92\nparent c0b6ed1e0f7c099b273e4e008da3d1b3ead5cbce\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1786944245 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <16266103+voidmatcha@users.noreply.github.com> 1786945661 +0900\n\nAdd PR/diff-scoped review mode to e2e-reviewer\n\nThe reviewer now classifies a request as full mode (a suite, directory, or\nrepository) or diff mode (a PR, patch, range, or changed-file list). In diff\nmode changed Playwright/Cypress artifacts are the review scope, unchanged\nfiles are context, and every finding carries an introduced / worsened /\npre-existing attribution. Only introduced and causally worsened findings\nreach blockers, totals, and top priorities; pre-existing findings stay\nadvisory. A mandatory Review Scope and Evidence header records what was and\nwas not verified, keeping static scanner coverage distinct from\ntarget-controlled runtime evidence.\n\nscan.sh now rejects multiple scan roots instead of silently ignoring extras,\nwhich is what lets diff mode invoke it once per changed artifact.\n\nFixture exclusion no longer applies to every scan. A target project that\nhappens to contain evals/files/ or scripts/ci/fixtures/ had its real tests\nsilently skipped, which is the exact failure class this scanner exists to\ncatch. Exclusion is now decided by fingerprinting the SCANNED PROJECT as an\ne2e-skills checkout. It deliberately does not use the scanner''s own location:\nreinstall-skills.sh installs real copies and the documented manual path\nsymlinks the skill, so a location-derived answer makes identical input\nproduce different findings depending on how the tool was installed.\n\nSeparately, `$0` is now resolved through symlinks before deriving the\nscanner''s sibling paths. Bash''s `cd` is logical, so ASTGREP_RULES_DIR\npreviously pointed at a nonexistent directory under symlinked invocation;\nbecause the Tier 2 branch and its \"not run\" notice both gate on `-d` that\npath, Tier 2 vanished without printing anything. Both scanner-relative paths\nnow derive from one resolved SCANNER_DIR_REAL, which locates files only.\n\nConstraint: independent-review protocols v5 and v6 cap the review packet at\n850,000 transformed bytes, every entry in their allowlists is required, and\nboth are hash-pinned preregistrations that keep measuring the live product.\nHEAD held only 5,125B of margin. The bytes were therefore freed from\nprovenance rather than from the feature contract or manifest parity strings:\nupstream-rule-sources.md was compressed with every source link, pattern-ID\nmapping and qualification preserved, and the 2026-08-16 source-pass decision\nlog moved here, where this repository''s commit protocol says decision records\nbelong. Final margin is 236B, so the next growth needs a real answer rather\nthan another squeeze.\n\nDecisions from that source pass, recorded here rather than shipped in the\nskill''s reference set:\n- Keep diff attribution, the static-versus-runtime evidence boundary, and the\n  smallest V3 behavior fault supported by repository source, a trace, or\n  observed network evidence that should fail one unchanged load-bearing\n  assertion.\n- No new smell ID: these sources strengthen workflow and verification\n  provenance; none establishes a new deterministic anti-pattern.\n- No new tool or service dependencies. StrykerJS, Cypress Cloud, and vendor\n  agent workflows are precedents only.\n- No scoring by AI provenance. Model, co-author, or prompt provenance is\n  reproducibility metadata, not evidence a finding is valid or severe.\n- A proposed fault is not runtime evidence until an exact target-controlled\n  command runs and the expected assertion fails for the declared reason.\n- General model-evaluation platforms stay secondary. OpenAI Evals can inform\n  evaluation design but is not a browser-E2E contract.\n\nRejected: deciding self-repo from the scanner''s own location. An earlier\nrevision of this change did exactly that. Measured against c0b6ed1 with the\nskill tree copied out and run over this repository, the installed copy went\nfrom 0 hits to 256 hits / 12 P0 including 5 focused-test P0s, breaking the\ndocumented verify-reviewer flow while an in-repo run of the same scanner\nreported nothing.\nRejected: minting a protocol v11 with a raised budget. Measurement showed it\nwould not fix the byte failure, because v5 and v6 are separately pinned and\nkeep enforcing their own caps against the current product.\nRejected: moving verify_result_digest_provenance() into the COMPLETE branch.\nThat would delete the check in the INCOMPLETE state it actually runs in; its\ninputs are now named explicitly so a missing artifact fails closed with a\nclear message instead of a raw FileNotFoundError.\nRejected: dropping \"with concrete fixes\" from the README reviewer row. The\nthree translations kept it, so the canonical English was the outlier.\n\nConfidence: high for the scanner fixes, which are reproduced against the\nprevious revision, fixed, and mutation-tested; medium for the diff-mode\ncontract, which is specified and eval-covered but has no accuracy measurement.\nScope-risk: fixture exclusion now depends on the scanned project''s marker\nfiles, so an e2e-skills checkout missing AGENTS.md or the two other\nfingerprint paths would report its own fixtures. Downstream projects that\npreviously benefited from the unconditional exclusion will start seeing hits\nunder evals/files/ and scripts/ci/fixtures/, which is the intended correction.\nNot-tested: no live model run of diff mode; the v3 holdout reports remain\nstale against the current skill digest and no accuracy claim is made.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMDrKTd6jIL08vOEXeHZrfqS4klkhdWg0UZEEB27nCcovgkWlI1m9XXHnCs9etl50m\nMrxNGGNQgwvBwxReP30gg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-21T10:50:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/24dbfda62339839624e233f377c790c594e653c4","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDI0ZGJmZGE2MjMzOTgzOTYyNGUyMzNmMzc3Yzc5MGM1OTRlNjUzYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/c0b6ed1e0f7c099b273e4e008da3d1b3ead5cbce","sha":"c0b6ed1e0f7c099b273e4e008da3d1b3ead5cbce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c0b6ed1e0f7c099b273e4e008da3d1b3ead5cbce"}],"sha":"24dbfda62339839624e233f377c790c594e653c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/24dbfda62339839624e233f377c790c594e653c4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c0b6ed1e0f7c099b273e4e008da3d1b3ead5cbce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-16T05:40:27Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-16T05:40:27Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Make the 1.12.1 patch boundary portable and fail closed\n\nPublish the verified patch release with aligned plugin metadata and localized documentation, a public privacy contract, clearer positional-locator review guidance, and bounded Playwright/Cypress process-group cleanup across all four debugger command boundaries.\n\nConstraint: Preserve the published v1.12.0 provenance and keep incomplete public holdout evidence explicitly non-release-eligible.\n\nRejected: Amend or retag v1.12.0 | Published tag and release provenance must remain immutable.\n\nConfidence: high\n\nScope-risk: broad\n\nDirective: Keep all seven version surfaces, four README languages, and four debugger process boundaries in lockstep; never treat unproven process cleanup or incomplete benchmark evidence as success.\n\nTested: /bin/bash -p scripts/ci/ci-local.sh; /bin/bash -p scripts/ci/pre-push-security.sh; four targeted debugger safety suites; Claude Fable final review APPROVE; git diff --check.\n\nNot-tested: Hosted main workflows for this new SHA; wait for them after push before creating the release tag.","tree":{"sha":"8de2a2cba2ed887f2a7da058c8728874733b07d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/8de2a2cba2ed887f2a7da058c8728874733b07d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/c0b6ed1e0f7c099b273e4e008da3d1b3ead5cbce","verification":{"payload":"tree 8de2a2cba2ed887f2a7da058c8728874733b07d0\nparent 2c591b6307b31db7f1efbfee6ca6279ed9325c92\nauthor YONGJAE LEE <dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com> 1786858827 +0900\ncommitter YONGJAE LEE <dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com> 1786858827 +0900\n\nMake the 1.12.1 patch boundary portable and fail closed\n\nPublish the verified patch release with aligned plugin metadata and localized documentation, a public privacy contract, clearer positional-locator review guidance, and bounded Playwright/Cypress process-group cleanup across all four debugger command boundaries.\n\nConstraint: Preserve the published v1.12.0 provenance and keep incomplete public holdout evidence explicitly non-release-eligible.\n\nRejected: Amend or retag v1.12.0 | Published tag and release provenance must remain immutable.\n\nConfidence: high\n\nScope-risk: broad\n\nDirective: Keep all seven version surfaces, four README languages, and four debugger process boundaries in lockstep; never treat unproven process cleanup or incomplete benchmark evidence as success.\n\nTested: /bin/bash -p scripts/ci/ci-local.sh; /bin/bash -p scripts/ci/pre-push-security.sh; four targeted debugger safety suites; Claude Fable final review APPROVE; git diff --check.\n\nNot-tested: Hosted main workflows for this new SHA; wait for them after push before creating the release tag.\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgnIl72o4wKEtDd2pGWzPrS4+Aq1\nc8FhqMeVyeHxawsKEAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQAhh/Vl9EJMjsqz/Ij81x1GSxSpTaDG7plcLQoei4k2ErpjmB12UwlNcrIaYYxgPw+\nupEzZWpr+zhXuw/GRmlgs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-16T05:41:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"htt