hhNGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/5e7feb08ec0637314335ca39db29d184cd8e4ffc","sha":"5e7feb08ec0637314335ca39db29d184cd8e4ffc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/5e7feb08ec0637314335ca39db29d184cd8e4ffc"}],"sha":"0c18520261343ee93bf0034319047102c1818a4b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/0c18520261343ee93bf0034319047102c1818a4b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/5e7feb08ec0637314335ca39db29d184cd8e4ffc/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T15:24:27Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T11:40:28Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Write down the rule that decides P0, and widen #19 to match its own hazard\n\nTwo severity questions the audit raised could not be settled by running\nanything — they are definitional, and the definition was never written\ndown.\n\nP0 reads \"test silently passes when the feature is broken — no real\nverification happening.\" The second clause is the discriminator and\nnothing said so. `#22` passes with the write deleted, which looks like\nP0, but the optimistic UI assertion does verify real client behaviour;\nwhat goes unverified is the write. That is P1, and the contract now says\nwhy, so the next person does not re-litigate it from the first clause\nalone.\n\n`#23` is the opposite shape. Its usual case is a guard leaving the\ncontainer empty and the test failing with a confusing \"element not\nfound\" — P2 diagnostics. But the variant its own text calls worse, where\na negative assertion passes because the guard suppressed the seeded\nitems, meets the P0 definition outright. Severity now follows the\ninstance there, the way `#12` already conditions P0 on the wrong surface\nactually satisfying the assertions. `#4i`''s empty-state SKIP was\ndismissing exactly that case, so it no longer applies when the fixture\ncannot satisfy the component''s guards.\n\n`#19` was left with no home at all after its sweep row was pulled for\ncontradicting the contract. The contract was the wrong half. A `var` at\ncolumn 0 and a `const` holding a mutated container survive a worker\nexactly as an initialised `let` does — the binding keyword was never the\nhazard. The contract covers all three now, the scanner still emits only\nthe `let` because it cannot grow, and the difference between what the\nscanner sees and what the pattern means is stated rather than implied.\n\nConstraint: no pattern ID, title, severity or F-code moved, so the manifest phrase contract is untouched; the change is to what the contracts say, in lock-step across pattern-reference, grep-patterns, the smells doc, four READMEs and SKILL.md.\nRejected: promoting #22 to P0 | it verifies something real, and a definition that catches it also catches every partial verification in the catalog. Rejected promoting #23 wholesale | its common case is a confusing failure, not a silent pass, and pricing the family at P0 would misreport the majority.\nConfidence: medium\nScope-risk: #19 now produces findings the scanner cannot corroborate, so they arrive with only sweep evidence behind them; and instance-conditioned severity on #23 asks reviewers to make a call the table alone does not make for them.\nNot-tested: no eval covers the #23 P0 variant or the widened #19 forms — the holdout corpus has neither shape.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ecab99667a0c6097b609bd32e8f16851f8d08c24","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/ecab99667a0c6097b609bd32e8f16851f8d08c24"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/5e7feb08ec0637314335ca39db29d184cd8e4ffc","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/5e7feb08ec0637314335ca39db29d184cd8e4ffc","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDVlN2ZlYjA4ZWMwNjM3MzE0MzM1Y2EzOWRiMjlkMTg0Y2Q4ZTRmZmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/864ef4fac0d353b0b61dfb37ad1d77ad43312d46","sha":"864ef4fac0d353b0b61dfb37ad1d77ad43312d46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/864ef4fac0d353b0b61dfb37ad1d77ad43312d46"}],"sha":"5e7feb08ec0637314335ca39db29d184cd8e4ffc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/5e7feb08ec0637314335ca39db29d184cd8e4ffc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/864ef4fac0d353b0b61dfb37ad1d77ad43312d46/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T13:10:56Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T11:40:28Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Release 1.12.0\n\nVersion across both plugin manifests, the marketplace entry, and the four\nskills'' metadata.\n\nMinor, not patch: no pattern ID, severity or F-code moved, but scan.sh\nexit codes flip 0 to 1 on repositories that were relying on a\n`// JUSTIFIED:` marker above a describe block to quiet the tests inside\nit. The CHANGELOG leads with that, because a user who reads only the\nrelease notes should not meet those findings as a surprise.\n\nThree numbers in the release notes were wrong and are corrected here: the\nsweep grew from 7 rows to 21, not 8 to 23; shell enumeration was 15.3s to\n1.0s, matching its own commit; and the \"roughly three times faster\" claim\nfor the CI mirror is gone, because no end-to-end measurement supports it —\nthe suite gained stages this release and wall-clock on a loaded machine\nmoves further than any of these changes do. The per-stage figures that\nwere actually measured stay.\n\n`docs/rule-self-audit.md` said the review packet has nineteen tokens of\nheadroom; re-measuring at release state gives eighteen, because the\nversion bump itself shifted a BPE merge in two packet surfaces. It now\nsays what it measured and tells the reader to re-measure.\n\nAGENTS.md still told contributors a JUSTIFIED marker \"above the enclosing\nblock\" suppresses findings — the exact placement this release turns into\na failing scan. It now describes the three positions that work.\n\nThe F1–F15 table is no longer collapsed in any of the four READMEs; a\nreader deciding whether the debugger fits their failure should not have to\nclick first. The 24-pattern table stays collapsed — it is long and the\ntaxonomy doc is linked beside it.\n\nConstraint: the translations bind a digest of exact README.md bytes, so the English edits and all three translations land in one commit or the parity check fails on the next one.\nRejected: major | nothing in the frozen taxonomy moved, and the JUSTIFIED narrowing conforms the implementation to a contract that already shipped.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: consumers gating CI on scan.sh will see new failures on first upgrade; that is the intended correction, but it arrives as a red build.\nNot-tested: the plugin marketplace install path was not exercised against the bumped manifests.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7733d138ca9026a153649a6ccf06ac4f443b2276","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/7733d138ca9026a153649a6ccf06ac4f443b2276"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/864ef4fac0d353b0b61dfb37ad1d77ad43312d46","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/864ef4fac0d353b0b61dfb37ad1d77ad43312d46","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDg2NGVmNGZhYzBkMzUzYjBiNjFkZmIzN2FkMWQ3N2FkNDMzMTJkNDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f99ad47363cc7b88b9d6004d0d6941b2eb5001f8","sha":"f99ad47363cc7b88b9d6004d0d6941b2eb5001f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f99ad47363cc7b88b9d6004d0d6941b2eb5001f8"}],"sha":"864ef4fac0d353b0b61dfb37ad1d77ad43312d46","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/864ef4fac0d353b0b61dfb37ad1d77ad43312d46"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f99ad47363cc7b88b9d6004d0d6941b2eb5001f8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-11T13:10:30Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T11:40:28Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Ship the optimistic-write example the README already links to\n\nThe README points at examples/react-optimistic-write, and the directory\nwas untracked — the link would have 404''d for every reader the moment\nthis was pushed.\n\nThe example makes one false-green pattern executable rather than\ndescribed. React updates a like button optimistically, so a UI-only\nassertion passes with the POST removed, and the same suite run against a\nrequest-proof test goes red at the awaited request. `verify:demo` exits\nzero only after observing all four outcomes, including the deliberately\nred one: green strong suite, green weak mutant under the missing write,\nred strong proof under the same fault, and a green strong suite repeated\nthree times to show the reset seam is deterministic.\n\nRun here before committing: four outcomes observed, exit 0, 16 seconds.\n\nThis matters for #22 specifically. That pattern needs the application in\nscope — whether a click issues a mutation cannot be decided from a spec —\nso a repository holding tests alone gets nothing from it, by design. The\nexample is where the contract can actually be demonstrated, and the\nREADME now says so in all four languages instead of leaving a reader to\ndiscover the precondition by finding nothing.\n\nConstraint: dist/, test-results/ and playwright-report/ are excluded by the example''s own .gitignore and node_modules by the root one; 16 files staged, verified against the security gate at 0 blockers.\nRejected: dropping the README line instead of shipping the directory | the pattern''s honest limitation is easier to state with a working demonstration than without one.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: the example carries its own package-lock and a Playwright dependency; it is disposable and outside the CI mirror, but it is now a surface that can rot.\nNot-tested: whether verify:demo passes on Linux or a cold browser cache — it was run once here with Chromium already installed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"263d5e20bc3bf533cc9f70cc209e1e7c2ffb51db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/263d5e20bc3bf533cc9f70cc209e1e7c2ffb51db"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/f99ad47363cc7b88b9d6004d0d6941b2eb5001f8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f99ad47363cc7b88b9d6004d0d6941b2eb5001f8","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGY5OWFkNDczNjNjYzdiODhiOWQ2MDA0ZDBkNjk0MWIyZWI1MDAxZjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f453a9afe66a8e513afe996cb3dfa9bce87725f5","sha":"f453a9afe66a8e513afe996cb3dfa9bce87725f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f453a9afe66a8e513afe996cb3dfa9bce87725f5"}],"sha":"f99ad47363cc7b88b9d6004d0d6941b2eb5001f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f99ad47363cc7b88b9d6004d0d6941b2eb5001f8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f453a9afe66a8e513afe996cb3dfa9bce87725f5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T15:48:00Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T11:40:28Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Record what the audit got wrong alongside what it found\n\nThe audit document shipped four claims that did not survive checking.\nCorrecting them is the point of keeping it.\n\nF13 was written up as the taxonomy''s worst defect — the readers discard\npassing tests and F13''s criterion is a test that passes, so the debugger\nholdout''s only P0 label looked unproducible. Both halves are true and the\nconclusion does not follow: the debugger enters on a failing suite, the\nreader drop removes passing tests from the Phase 1 records rather than\nfrom the review, and both eval suites pin exactly the intended behaviour —\n\"Flags the PASSING test ... as P0 F13\". The holdout never touches a reader\nat all; its runner is prompt-complete and zero-tool.\n\nwas the error. The fixture put the variable form one line above the inline\nform, and the filter windows twelve lines forward from a hit — the\nvariable line matched the next line''s literal. Isolated, the variable form\nscores zero and the inline form scores one. The finding stands and the\nsweep row withheld on its strength is in.\n\nThe headline claimed seven rules were shown defective by cross-family\ndisagreement. Two were documented; reproducing the other five kept all\nfive.\n\nFour repairs to the fixes themselves, from a later review:\n\nusage along with its declaration and sends `submit` back to UNUSED. It is\nline-level now, and INTERNAL-ONLY is reachable again.\n\nThe #19 row was removed as contradicting the pattern contract while the\ndocument went on claiming it existed. `var` and mutated `const` module\nstate now has no home on any path; that is recorded as an open gap, since\nclosing it means widening the contract rather than adding a sweep row.\n\nEval 32''s assertions were uniformly one line off its own fixture.\n\nThree elapsed-time assertions were left outside the hang guard the same\nwork introduced, so the suite stayed load-flaky through a door the fix had\nnot covered.\n\nThe evidence status is re-derived for the moved skill digest. Nothing is\npromoted: status stays INCOMPLETE, release_eligible false, and all three\nholdout reports stay stale against the current skill.\n\nConstraint: every finding here is meant to be reproducible from the document, so a claim that cannot be reproduced has to move to Refuted rather than be quietly dropped.\nRejected: deleting the wrong findings | the method that produced them is the same one that produced the real ones, and the record of how it failed is the part worth keeping. Rejected keeping the #10b refutation with a caveat | it was not a weaker claim, it was the opposite of what the scanner does.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: the sweep reached 23 rows; #10b''s asks the reviewer to resolve a variable the scanner cannot.\nNot-tested: the #14 false-positive rate and the flake timings quoted in the document were measured once and not re-run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"92e19e9bb4eb237d326ce13464acb0bb7eed1bdb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/92e19e9bb4eb237d326ce13464acb0bb7eed1bdb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/f453a9afe66a8e513afe996cb3dfa9bce87725f5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f453a9afe66a8e513afe996cb3dfa9bce87725f5","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGY0NTNhOWFmZTY2YThlNTEzYWZlOTk2Y2IzZGZhOWJjZTg3NzI1ZjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/e369c7c5f568093aa5cce987cd8888509267a777","sha":"e369c7c5f568093aa5cce987cd8888509267a777","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/e369c7c5f568093aa5cce987cd8888509267a777"}],"sha":"f453a9afe66a8e513afe996cb3dfa9bce87725f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f453a9afe66a8e513afe996cb3dfa9bce87725f5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/e369c7c5f568093aa5cce987cd8888509267a777/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T15:47:37Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T11:40:28Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Make the delegated classifier able to say it cannot know\n\nF1 versus F7 is decided by an isolation probe, and the debugger skills say\nso plainly: classifying from the error text alone is wrong about half the\ntime. The delegated classifier is read-only — `tools: Read, Grep, Glob` —\nso it can never run that probe, and neither it nor its Codex port carried\nthe skills'' own rule for that case. Both would guess F1 from a\nTimeoutError while the inline path returned CANNOT_VERIFY, against a\ncontract requiring an identical verdict on all three paths.\n\nBoth copies now carry it: apply the probe table when the caller''s payload\nincludes the probe outcomes, and return CANNOT_VERIFY between F1 and F7\nwhen it does not. Same code given evidence, same failure token without it.\n\nSP3b pins the term across every copy. Its first draft was weaker than it\nlooked — both debugger skills use CANNOT_VERIFY elsewhere for proof\nlabelling, so a token check stayed green with the F1/F7 rule deleted. It\nnow requires the rule by the pair it names, and test-parity.sh mutates\nthat rule to prove it fails.\n\nTwo CI regressions from earlier in this branch, both self-inflicted:\n\nThe scanner worker default floored at 2, so a two-core runner got the\nwhole box — the oversubscription the change was meant to remove. It is now\nhalf the cores capped below the core count: one worker at two cores, five\nat ten, unchanged where it was measured.\n\nThe debugger contract suite failed repeatedly on a loaded machine. The\nextractor it timed out on processes the same fixtures in 0.4 to 0.8\nseconds against a 20-second cap and holds no lock — it was starved, not\nslow. Those fourteen timeouts never asserted a runtime; they bound a hang.\nAn arbitrary guard should be generous, so they now go through one helper\nat six times the value, raisable with E2E_CONTRACT_TIMEOUT_SCALE.\n\nConstraint: the debugger skills that define the CANNOT_VERIFY rule are inside the v10 packet, so the rule had to be propagated outward to the classifier copies rather than restated there.\nRejected: raising the parity worker default''s sibling deadlines instead of the hang guards | the ReDoS growth check and the reporter-timeout assertion do claim a runtime, so those need the assertion rewritten, not a longer clock.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: a slower default hang guard means a genuine hang in the debugger readers takes two minutes to surface instead of twenty seconds.\nNot-tested: the classifier change is contract text; no delegated run was executed against a real failing suite.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"44d55bd57680c8ca32e63277784d036c3c3ae808","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/44d55bd57680c8ca32e63277784d036c3c3ae808"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/e369c7c5f568093aa5cce987cd8888509267a777","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/e369c7c5f568093aa5cce987cd8888509267a777","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGUzNjljN2M1ZjU2ODA5M2FhNWNjZTk4N2NkODg4ODUwOTI2N2E3Nzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/d8ace10150ee75476a61d6c401cd7b8625734a2c","sha":"d8ace10150ee75476a61d6c401cd7b8625734a2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/d8ace10150ee75476a61d6c401cd7b8625734a2c"}],"sha":"e369c7c5f568093aa5cce987cd8888509267a777","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/e369c7c5f568093aa5cce987cd8888509267a777"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/d8ace10150ee75476a61d6c401cd7b8625734a2c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T15:47:14Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T11:40:28Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Let the reviewer find what the scanner cannot\n\nFifteen rules were confirmed unable to detect the defect they name — the\nregexes assume a statement fits on one physical line, and Prettier wraps at\n80 columns. The obvious repair is wider regexes, and scan.sh has nineteen\ntokens of headroom against a frozen v10 packet cap, so it cannot grow.\n\nThe reviewer''s own procedure can. The audit''s other finding was that the\nrecovery path is closed: contracts hand Phase 2 a candidate list, and the\nsweep that would let it look independently was frozen without the families\nthat need it most. Those families now have sweep rows, each naming the\nscanner''s specific blind spot — #4a''s single literal, #4f''s name-suffix\ngate, #18''s inability to match an awaited soft assertion, #10c treating\n`exact: false` as exact, #3b missing `Cypress[''on'']`, #9b a member\nexpression, #9c a constant, #10d a wrapped async callback, and the rest.\n\nEvery row was written after reproducing the miss against the shipped\nscanner. That mattered: a reported #10b gap turned out not to exist — the\nfilter resolves `test.describe.configure(suitePolicy)` through the\nvariable and correctly ignores `mode: ''parallel''` — so no row was added\nfor it.\n\n#11 was not a coverage gap but a live-code hazard. Its documented grep\nsays \"specs, POMs, and other utility modules\" while the glob beside it\nmatched specs only, so a member called from another POM returned zero hits\nand was classified UNUSED. The glob now covers the E2E root, and discounts\nthe declaring file — the wide glob matches that too, and counting a\nmember''s own declaration would make everything look used.\n\nEvals 32 and 33 pin the parts most likely to rot. 33 in particular fails\nboth ways: the old spec-only glob calls a live member dead, the naive wide\nglob calls a dead member live.\n\nConstraint: scan.sh, both artifact readers and playwright-debugger/SKILL.md sit inside the v10 packet at 19 tokens of headroom; SKILL.md and pattern-reference.md do not, which is why the fix lives there.\nRejected: widening the candidate regexes | unaffordable against a preregistered cap that is evidence, not a setting. Rejected a #19 row for `var` and mutated `const` | pattern-reference defines #19 as an initialised top-level `let`, so the sweep would have produced findings the verifier must refute. Rejected a #5a row covering `test.skip()` | that is the documented fix for #5a and produces a visible skipped result, not a silent pass.\nConfidence: medium\nScope-risk: the mandatory sweep went from 8 rows to 22. Reviews get longer, and #4a''s row asks whether a bound is satisfiable rather than matching a token — a judgement that can go wrong in both directions.\nNot-tested: whether the rows change measured accuracy; the holdout has not been re-run and its reports are marked stale.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"945381bb4dad37eb14ff605b5c4c668c1e6e8de5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/945381bb4dad37eb14ff605b5c4c668c1e6e8de5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/d8ace10150ee75476a61d6c401cd7b8625734a2c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/d8ace10150ee75476a61d6c401cd7b8625734a2c","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGQ4YWNlMTAxNTBlZTc1NDc2YTYxZDZjNDAxY2Q3Yjg2MjU3MzRhMmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/ec40b3219a72e940686d35a236384bd04eb6225e","sha":"ec40b3219a72e940686d35a236384bd04eb6225e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/ec40b3219a72e940686d35a236384bd04eb6225e"}],"sha":"d8ace10150ee75476a61d6c401cd7b8625734a2c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/d8ace10150ee75476a61d6c401cd7b8625734a2c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/ec40b3219a72e940686d35a236384bd04eb6225e/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T12:57:34Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T11:40:28Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Give the audited families a way back into the review\n\nThe audit found rules that cannot see their own defect: #4a is one literal\nstring, #18 cannot match `await expect.soft(`, #4f only recognises a POM\nmember whose name ends in a UI suffix, #4i needs `0` to be the sole\nargument on one line, #10c treats `exact: false` as if it were `exact:\ntrue`. The obvious repair is to widen those regexes, and it is not\navailable. scan.sh is one of seven surfaces in the v10 review packet and\nthe packet measures 122,981 of a preregistered 123,000 reference tokens —\nnineteen tokens, about one line. The cap is frozen evidence, not a knob.\n\nThe reviewer''s SKILL.md and pattern-reference.md are outside that packet,\nwhich turns out to be the better place anyway. The audit''s second finding\nwas that the recovery path is closed: several contracts hand Phase 2 a\ncandidate list and the sweep that would let it look independently is\nfrozen at \"exactly this list\" without the families that need it most. So\nthose five now have sweep rows, each naming the blind spot it covers for,\nand #21 sweeps the Cypress session-file shapes its Playwright-only\n`storageState:` key could never reach. The regexes stay as they are —\ncorrect where they fire, no longer the only place a family can be found.\n\nAlso fixes a regression this branch introduced. Parallelising the scanner\nchecks at one worker per core oversubscribes the machine, because each\nworker spawns scan.sh. At ten workers the check that builds 1500 files\nlost the CPU and failed its own deadline; at five it passes in 362s, at\nfour in 286s, and serial is over ten minutes. Default is now half the\ncores, overridable with E2E_SCANNER_WORKERS.\n\nConstraint: editing the skill moves its digest, so the holdout evidence status is re-derived here with the gate''s own functions; nothing is promoted and the three reports stay stale.\nRejected: raising the v10 prompt cap to afford wider regexes | it is preregistered evidence and moving it to fit a later change is how a benchmark stops meaning anything. Rejected blaming the failing stages on machine load alone | that was true and would have buried our own oversubscription.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: the new sweep rows add work to every review, and #4a''s row asks the reviewer to judge whether a bound is satisfiable rather than match a token — more findings, and more judgement calls to get wrong.\nNot-tested: whether the sweep rows change measured accuracy; the holdout has not been re-run since, and its reports are marked stale for that reason.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"7110a3996e1806b533329965419f42a2b1ded88c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/7110a3996e1806b533329965419f42a2b1ded88c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/ec40b3219a72e940686d35a236384bd04eb6225e","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/ec40b3219a72e940686d35a236384bd04eb6225e","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGVjNDBiMzIxOWE3MmU5NDA2ODZkMzVhMjM2Mzg0YmQwNGViNjIyNWU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/5a41bbc3bdae6c4efa8717a84c735f5069057dd9","sha":"5a41bbc3bdae6c4efa8717a84c735f5069057dd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/5a41bbc3bdae6c4efa8717a84c735f5069057dd9"}],"sha":"ec40b3219a72e940686d35a236384bd04eb6225e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/ec40b3219a72e940686d35a236384bd04eb6225e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/5a41bbc3bdae6c4efa8717a84c735f5069057dd9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T07:04:39Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T11:40:28Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Audit our own rules the way we audit other people''s\n\nSix axes — the 24 patterns, F1-F15, and the operational rules — each read\nadversarially by two model families, with every finding reproduced against\nthe shipped scanner before it was written down.\n\nEight rules cannot detect what they name. Three are P0: #7 misses the\nformatter-wrapped spelling of the alias it documents, so a focused test\nsilently excludes its siblings; #4f covers a POM member only when its name\nends in Button/Link/Locator/Element, so two identically typed Locators get\nopposite verdicts; #4a is one literal string, and `toBeGreaterThan(-1)`\npasses. #18 cannot match `await expect.soft(` at all — the only form it\ncatches is the unawaited one, which is already #15. F13''s criterion is a\ntest that passes, and both debuggers'' readers discard passing tests before\nclassification, so the only P0 label in the debugger holdout is\nunreachable. #10c treats `exact: false` as if it were `exact: true`. #14\nfires on any `.fill(` with a literal, at a 75% false-positive rate on our\nown corpus. #21 keys on a Playwright-only token in a two-framework skill.\n\nTwo causes explain most of it. The candidate regexes assume a statement\nfits on one physical line, and Prettier wraps at 80 columns. And the\nrecovery path is closed: several contracts say Phase 1 supplies the\ncandidates, while the sweep that would let Phase 2 look independently is\nfrozen at \"exactly this list — no more, no less\" and omits the rules with\nthe widest Phase 1 gaps.\n\nThe two model families disagreed usefully. Seven rules one family cleared\nas sound were shown defective by the other, two of them P0. A\nsingle-reviewer audit would have passed all seven. One reported finding\ndid not survive reproduction and is recorded as refuted.\n\nConstraint: docs/ files must be linked from README, and README changes invalidate the translations'' canonical-revision digests — both are recorded here along with the doc.\nRejected: filing these as issues instead of a document | the unfixed list is the part that matters, and an issue tracker loses the reproduction steps that make each one checkable.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none; documentation only.\nNot-tested: the disk-exhaustion fail-open is recorded as SUSPECTED — the condition occurred during the audit but reproducing it means filling the disk.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"2508096bad2ca9a0ee3b488a3ac809246ba059d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/2508096bad2ca9a0ee3b488a3ac809246ba059d7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/5a41bbc3bdae6c4efa8717a84c735f5069057dd9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/5a41bbc3bdae6c4efa8717a84c735f5069057dd9","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDVhNDFiYmMzYmRhZTZjNGVmYTg3MTdhODRjNzM1ZjUwNjkwNTdkZDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/1d9e884885d8b91c8e08c803a4a1f2d883efe17c","sha":"1d9e884885d8b91c8e08c803a4a1f2d883efe17c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/1d9e884885d8b91c8e08c803a4a1f2d883efe17c"}],"sha":"5a41bbc3bdae6c4efa8717a84c735f5069057dd9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/5a41bbc3bdae6c4efa8717a84c735f5069057dd9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/1d9e884885d8b91c8e08c803a4a1f2d883efe17c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T07:04:18Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T11:40:28Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Stop one JUSTIFIED marker from covering a whole describe\n\nA `// JUSTIFIED:` comment above a `test.describe` suppressed findings in\ntests that had nothing to do with its rationale, and turned a red scan\ngreen. The callback-scope walk collected every line between the marker and\nthe hit and asked whether `.evaluate(` or `.waitForFunction(` appeared\nanywhere in that span, so an evaluate call in an earlier sibling test\nsatisfied the check. The comment above the loop already stated the\nintended rule — the hit must stay inside the same brace-delimited callback\n— and the code did not implement it.\n\nMeasured before the fix: a marker whose rationale described a canvas read\nin the first test suppressed a #4f P0 and a #9 P1 in the second test, and\nscan.sh exited 0. Delete the marker and the same file reports 1 P0 and\nexits 1. That matters most where there is no reviewer to catch it:\nscan.sh ships as a standalone CI scanner, the default gate is\nFAIL_ON=p0, and suppressed P1/P2 hits are dropped without retaining a\npattern ID, so nothing downstream can recover them.\n\nNow only the construct that opens the scope can carry the rationale. A\nmarker directly above `page.evaluate(() => {` still covers that callback;\na marker above a `describe` covers nothing inside it.\n\nEval 31 pins both halves: the same fixture has one marker that must\nsuppress and one that must not.\n\nConstraint: scan.sh is one of seven surfaces in the v10 review packet, which sits within a couple hundred bytes of its preregistered prompt-size cap — a four-line comment explaining this change broke the cap, so the fix ships at +17 bytes with no new comment.\nRejected: requiring the marker to be the immediately preceding line | that would drop the documented multi-line callback case the position-2 rule exists to serve.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: any existing repository that was relying on a describe-level marker to quiet a whole block will start reporting those findings. That is the intent, but it will look like new findings appearing.\nNot-tested: Tier 1 ESLint interaction; Tier 1 stays off without an explicit opt-in and was not exercised.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a85011c337b1d764836e282c382360d3797fbaac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/a85011c337b1d764836e282c382360d3797fbaac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/1d9e884885d8b91c8e08c803a4a1f2d883efe17c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/1d9e884885d8b91c8e08c803a4a1f2d883efe17c","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDFkOWU4ODQ4ODVkOGI5MWM4ZTA4YzgwM2E0YTFmMmQ4ODNlZmUxN2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/df574ff185b20cd8f66b4f7774a405229b844568","sha":"df574ff185b20cd8f66b4f7774a405229b844568","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/df574ff185b20cd8f66b4f7774a405229b844568"}],"sha":"1d9e884885d8b91c8e08c803a4a1f2d883efe17c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/1d9e884885d8b91c8e08c803a4a1f2d883efe17c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/df574ff185b20cd8f66b4f7774a405229b844568/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-10T02:04:07Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T11:40:28Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Explain the Codex arm''s score without excusing it\n\nThe holdout put claude-opus-5 at 0.986 precision and gpt-5.6-sol at 0.792,\na gap wide enough to read as a skill that works badly on Codex. It is not\nthat. Every miss lands in a file the model did report, with the correct\npattern ID, one line above the labeled line. The scorer keys findings on\n(pattern_id, severity, file, line), so a single line of disagreement is\ncounted twice — once as a false positive and once as a false negative.\nThat is the whole of the fp == fn symmetry.\n\nThe labels are right: source_line matches the file at every audited line.\nThe line the model picks instead is the start of the enclosing expression\nor the declaration of the subject, and the corpus is written compactly\nenough that this is always exactly one line up. For the multi-line call in\n5b and the arrow body in 6, naming the line where the call begins is a\ndefensible reading of \"the causal line\", so some of this gap is the\ncorpus convention being more specific than the contract.\n\nTwo prompt fixes were measured and reverted: an explicit anchor rule for\nunnamed patterns (0.778) and a re-read-the-line verification step (0.784).\nEach changed the failure shape and neither moved the metric. That is\nrecorded here so the next attempt does not spend another 48 live calls\nlearning the same thing.\n\nThe run stays FAIL at 0.784 against a required 0.900. Nothing here\npromotes it.\n\nConstraint: findings are scored on an exact (pattern_id, severity, file, line) key, so anchor disagreement is indistinguishable from a miss at the metric level.\nRejected: loosening the scorer to tolerate one line | it would hide real mislocation and break comparability with the recorded runs. Rejected keeping the two prompt rules | neither improved the metric, and shipping unproven prompt text is how contracts accumulate.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none; documentation plus a README link, no skill or scorer change.\nNot-tested: whether tightening the anchor contract for multi-line constructs across both the skill and the corpus labels would close the gap — that is the open item.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"347d41079bc5e38d891df68134ca618082609132","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/347d41079bc5e38d891df68134ca618082609132"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/df574ff185b20cd8f66b4f7774a405229b844568","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/df574ff185b20cd8f66b4f7774a405229b844568","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGRmNTc0ZmYxODViMjBjZDhmNjZiNGY3Nzc0YTQwNTIyOWI4NDQ1Njg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/89c33eb7553d3964655c1a5e4aa753c71e5e1f65","sha":"89c33eb7553d3964655c1a5e4aa753c71e5e1f65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/89c33eb7553d3964655c1a5e4aa753c71e5e1f65"}],"sha":"df574ff185b20cd8f66b4f7774a405229b844568","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/df574ff185b20cd8f66b4f7774a405229b844568"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/89c33eb7553d3964655c1a5e4aa753c71e5e1f65/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T13:29:51Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-12T11:40:28Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Keep the public holdout fail-closed after an incomplete matrix\n\nRecord the current 72-scheduled-call public development run without promoting it: Codex missed repeated precision, Opus passed, and one Fable response was unscoreable. Derive incomplete-state artifact pins from the current full reports while preserving historical fallbacks.\n\nConstraint: Public development evidence cannot be described as sealed or hidden, and an incomplete Fable report cannot support cross-host claims.\nRejected: Mark the matrix complete or generate a manifest | One Fable response was unscoreable and the comparison is inconclusive.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: moderate\nDirective: Do not create evidence-manifest.json or publish cross-host metrics until a complete current-snapshot matrix is recorded.\nTested: Three AGENTS.md live host commands; compare-reviewer-holdouts.py; python3 scripts/ci/test-reviewer-evidence-v3.py; /bin/bash -p scripts/ci/ci-local.sh; /bin/bash -p scripts/ci/pre-push-security.sh\nNot-tested: Complete cross-host comparison or sealed release isolation.","tree":{"sha":"9529b94425fd926759eea7ccceff97baaf0c8f4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/9529b94425fd926759eea7ccceff97baaf0c8f4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/89c33eb7553d3964655c1a5e4aa753c71e5e1f65","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/89c33eb7553d3964655c1a5e4aa753c71e5e1f65","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDg5YzMzZWI3NTUzZDM5NjQ2NTVjMWE1ZTRhYTc1M2M3MWU1ZTFmNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/e66dae9e1c0c819c7a7af9b3335f9389ad548b50","sha":"e66dae9e1c0c819c7a7af9b3335f9389ad548b50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/e66dae9e1c0c819c7a7af9b3335f9389ad548b50"}],"sha":"89c33eb7553d3964655c1a5e4aa753c71e5e1f65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/89c33eb7553d3964655c1a5e4aa753c71e5e1f65"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/e66dae9e1c0c819c7a7af9b3335f9389ad548b50/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-09T08:29:40Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T10:35:59Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Prevent zero-test Playwright isolation probes\n\nPlaywright applies --grep to its full title path, so an anchored bare test title can select no tests and produce false isolation evidence. Require a one-test --list preflight and reuse that verified fragment.\n\nConstraint: Targeted probes must prove exactly one selected test before classification.\nRejected: Keep the anchored bare-title regex | Playwright prefixes the title path and can select zero tests.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: narrow\nTested: python3 scripts/ci/test-debugger-contracts.py; Playwright fixture list probes; /bin/bash -p scripts/ci/ci-local.sh; /bin/bash -p scripts/ci/pre-push-security.sh\nNot-tested: Live diagnosis against a third-party Playwright repository.","tree":{"sha":"f50a9a336f693075baff7f0177dbe4e22f2f638b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/f50a9a336f693075baff7f0177dbe4e22f2f638b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/e66dae9e1c0c819c7a7af9b3335f9389ad548b50","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/e66dae9e1c0c819c7a7af9b3335f9389ad548b50","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGU2NmRhZTllMWMwYzgxOWM3YTdhZjliMzMzNWY5Mzg5YWQ1NDhiNTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/b2f9d04e0af854a9ec0c83fa339896c8c519bd11","sha":"b2f9d04e0af854a9ec0c83fa339896c8c519bd11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/b2f9d04e0af854a9ec0c83fa339896c8c519bd11"}],"sha":"e66dae9e1c0c819c7a7af9b3335f9389ad548b50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/e66dae9e1c0c819c7a7af9b3335f9389ad548b50"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/b2f9d04e0af854a9ec0c83fa339896c8c519bd11/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T14:49:29Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T10:35:59Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Point the v3 evidence status at the skill that exists now\n\nevidence-status.json records which skill snapshot the reviewer-holdout-v3\nartifacts describe, and the gate recomputes that digest from\nskills/e2e-reviewer on every run. The skill has moved since the status was\nlast written, so the record named a snapshot that no longer exists and the\ncheck has been red since before this branch.\n\nRefreshing the digest is what the check asks for, not a way around it.\nNothing is promoted: the status stays INCOMPLETE, release_eligible stays\nfalse, cross_host_comparison_available stays false, the same four\nartifacts stay missing and reports/full-codex.json stays stale. The record\nnow says the evidence was produced against an older skill, which is true,\ninstead of naming a snapshot that matches nothing.\n\nThe derived fields were not hand-edited. missing_required_artifacts,\nstale_required_artifacts and every current_snapshot_match flag were\nrecomputed with the gate''s own functions against the new digest and came\nout identical to what was already written, so only the digest changed.\nBlanking stale_required_artifacts still fails, so the record cannot quietly\nclaim more than it has.\n\nConstraint: unlike the pinned v8 evidence validator, this field is specified to track the live skill — the gate derives it rather than asserting a frozen constant, so updating it restores the contract instead of suppressing it.\nRejected: re-running the holdout to make the artifacts current — that is a live model run against a public corpus, a release decision, not a gate repair.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none; no measurement, report, or eligibility flag is touched.\nNot-tested: none.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1ea60ac10888d16e423fbfa5f06ff004887dcd50","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/1ea60ac10888d16e423fbfa5f06ff004887dcd50"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/b2f9d04e0af854a9ec0c83fa339896c8c519bd11","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/b2f9d04e0af854a9ec0c83fa339896c8c519bd11","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGIyZjlkMDRlMGFmODU0YTllYzBjODNmYTMzOTg5NmM4YzUxOWJkMTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/28cedd70a5da33c408016d87fc29414626f9438c","sha":"28cedd70a5da33c408016d87fc29414626f9438c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/28cedd70a5da33c408016d87fc29414626f9438c"}],"sha":"b2f9d04e0af854a9ec0c83fa339896c8c519bd11","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/b2f9d04e0af854a9ec0c83fa339896c8c519bd11"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/28cedd70a5da33c408016d87fc29414626f9438c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T14:47:40Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T10:35:59Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Put back the scanner boundary the README rewrite dropped\n\nThe README rewrite in c9e1598 deleted three documented facts about the\nscanner: which file extensions it reads, that Python maintains NUL-safe\ncandidate identity records so drift or malformed records fail closed, and\nthat this bookkeeping is mandatory rather than part of the optional Tier 2\nAST tier. The extension list went from all four READMEs; the Korean copy\nkept the sentence but lost the list inside it.\n\ntest-reviewer-doc-contracts.py existed to prevent exactly this, and it did\nfail — it has been red since that rewrite. It could not be green and\ncorrect at the same time, because the facts it checks were gone.\n\nThe restored text is the pre-rewrite wording, not new prose, so the\ndocumented boundary matches what the scanner has been doing all along.\nThe extension list is checked against CODE_EXTENSIONS in scan.sh, so the\ntwo cannot drift apart again without the gate saying so; dropping a single\nextension from the README makes it fail.\n\nThe check itself was part of the problem. It bracketed the extension list\nwith two sentences from the README body, so an editor rewording the\nsurrounding paragraph silently removed the contract along with its\nanchors. It now anchors on a marker comment, the same device the README\nalready uses for its i18n-protected regions, and the three translations\nshare that one marker instead of three more sentences to rot.\n\nConstraint: the SCANNER-READ-SCOPE and CORE-SAFETY regions are content-hash-pinned in review.sh, so the restored text sits outside them and leaves those digests untouched.\nRejected: relaxing the assertions to token presence — the contract is that the README states these facts, and weakening it to keywords would have let the same deletion through.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: the three translations carry a digest of the README.md bytes they were reviewed against; that digest is refreshed here, which asserts the new sentences were translated, not that the whole translation was re-reviewed.\nNot-tested: none.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c64ce3e1f8170b0ba95e6ff5c6c27c1ecac112a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/c64ce3e1f8170b0ba95e6ff5c6c27c1ecac112a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/28cedd70a5da33c408016d87fc29414626f9438c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/28cedd70a5da33c408016d87fc29414626f9438c","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDI4Y2VkZDcwYTVkYTMzYzQwODAxNmQ4N2ZjMjk0MTQ2MjZmOTQzOGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/3704b3da790c694d2a8e2e6eb3cf998c2e90bce4","sha":"3704b3da790c694d2a8e2e6eb3cf998c2e90bce4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/3704b3da790c694d2a8e2e6eb3cf998c2e90bce4"}],"sha":"28cedd70a5da33c408016d87fc29414626f9438c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/28cedd70a5da33c408016d87fc29414626f9438c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/3704b3da790c694d2a8e2e6eb3cf998c2e90bce4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T13:42:15Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-11T10:35:59Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Version the README exclusions v7 applies\n\nThe independent-review packet blanks the README sections that argue the\nproject''s own case, and the heading names had been hardcoded. After the\nREADME was rewritten they matched nothing, so the exclusion silently\nstopped happening while the manifest kept claiming it.\n\nv7 sees two different READMEs — the working tree now, and the archived\nsnapshot taken before the rewrite — so one hardcoded set cannot serve both.\nUpdating it to the current names fixes live derivation and breaks archive\nreproduction; leaving it fixes the archive and strips nothing today. Both\ndirections were measured and both fail. The names are versioned instead,\nand the applicable generation is chosen from the README in hand.\n\nVerified in both directions: the working tree goes 26,867 to 22,933 bytes\nremoving the three current sections, and the v7 archived snapshot goes\n56,507 to 40,306 removing the three original ones — the same numbers the\narchived manifest already records.\n\nConstraint: the runner and its evidence reimplementation are compared packet-for-packet, so the selector had to land in both in the same shape.\nRejected: applying the same fix to v8 | v9 and v10 pin scripts/ci/test-independent-review-v8-evidence.py by SHA-256 and assert it still hashes to f453718a. The edit was caught by that pin at test-independent-review-v10.py:189, and re-pinning to the new digest would have silenced the control that caught it. v8 keeps the stale set and its live-tree exclusion stays a no-op — a real remaining gap, recorded rather than papered over.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: v8, v9 and v10 remain no-ops on the live README; only v6, v7 and the base runner enforce the exclusion.\nNot-tested: whether any v7 packet published between the README rewrite and this commit carries the sections it claims to omit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8d54be2de427c6f1254f675a67d441723cf94a44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/8d54be2de427c6f1254f675a67d441723cf94a44"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/3704b3da790c694d2a8e2e6eb3cf998c2e90bce4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/3704b3da790c694d2a8e2e6eb3cf998c2e90bce4","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDM3MDRiM2RhNzkwYzY5NGQyYThlMmU2ZWIzY2Y5OThjMmU5MGJjZTQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/c835b944a0cd8012adea81ede8c35d2bb97b7388","sha":"c835b944a0cd8012adea81ede8c35d2bb97b7388","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c835b944a0cd8012adea81ede8c35d2bb97b7388"}],"sha":"3704b3da790c694d2a8e2e6eb3cf998c2e90bce4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/3704b3da790c694d2a8e2e6eb3cf998c2e90bce4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c835b944a0cd8012adea81ede8c35d2bb97b7388/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T13:24:39Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T13:24:39Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Restore the v6 packet''s README bias exclusions\n\nThe independent-review packet blanks three README sections so an outside\nreviewer never reads the project''s own case for itself. The heading names\nwere a hardcoded set, and the README was later rewritten: \"Methodology\"\nand \"Open-source adoption and case evidence\" no longer exist, and the\nCodeRabbit FAQ entry is gone. Nothing matched, so nothing was stripped.\n\nThe exclusion did not fail — it evaporated. strip_markdown_sections\nreturned the README unchanged and reported an empty excluded list, while\nthe manifest''s omissions block kept naming all three sections, because it\nrecords the configured set rather than the applied one. A fresh v6 packet\ntherefore documented an exclusion that had not happened, and shipped the\nsections it claimed to withhold.\n\nMeasured on the current README: 26,867 bytes in, 26,867 bytes out, zero\nsections removed. After this change, 26,867 to 22,933 with all three\nsections removed. The archives are not retroactively affected — the v5\nsnapshot records README 55,658 to 40,306, so the exclusion was live when\nthose reviews ran.\n\nThe guard is the part that matters: a configured heading that no longer\nresolves now raises instead of silently stripping nothing, so the next\nREADME rewrite fails loudly and names the heading. That mirrors the guard\nalready in run-independent-review.py.\n\nThe suite''s own line-number check depended on a literal \"## At a glance\"\nthat the rewrite had already removed. Rather than swap in another literal\nthat will rot the same way, it now asserts the invariant directly: every\nsurviving top-level heading keeps its original line number, and no\nexcluded heading survives. Injecting a line-shift into the blanking loop\nmakes it fail; without the injection it passes.\n\nConstraint: run-independent-review-v7..v10 and their evidence reimplementations share one constant across both the live tree and archived snapshots, whose READMEs are different generations. Updating the constant there fixes live derivation and breaks archive reproduction (verified both directions), so those need a generation-aware list, not this edit.\nRejected: updating all eleven copies of the heading list — six are evidence reimplementations that reproduce archived packets from archived READMEs, where the old names are correct and load-bearing.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: v7-v10 remain no-ops on the live README; only v6 and the base runner enforce the exclusion today.\nNot-tested: whether any already-published v6 packet was generated after the README rewrite and therefore carries the sections it claims to omit.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bda954435bb191e124a955ae4ca4bb4a5ac1a918","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/bda954435bb191e124a955ae4ca4bb4a5ac1a918"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/c835b944a0cd8012adea81ede8c35d2bb97b7388","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/c835b944a0cd8012adea81ede8c35d2bb97b7388","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGM4MzViOTQ0YTBjZDgwMTJhZGVhODFlZGU4YzM1ZDJiYjk3YjczODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/fe9973c0712cba14cb806a404b26845e3c639092","sha":"fe9973c0712cba14cb806a404b26845e3c639092","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/fe9973c0712cba14cb806a404b26845e3c639092"}],"sha":"c835b944a0cd8012adea81ede8c35d2bb97b7388","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/c835b944a0cd8012adea81ede8c35d2bb97b7388"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/fe9973c0712cba14cb806a404b26845e3c639092/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T12:23:36Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T12:23:36Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Shard the parity suite across disposable copies\n\ntest-parity.sh was the largest stage in the gate at 629s. The cost is\nstructural: ~68 mutate-assert-restore cases, and 59 of them run\nreview.sh end to end because review.sh accumulates errors rather than\nshort-circuiting, so every case pays the full walk.\n\nThe isolation needed to parallelize was already there — the runner copies\nthe repo, mutates only inside the copy, and digest-checks the source\nbefore and after. The cases were serial only because they shared one\ncopy. Now the runner can create N copies concurrently and hand each an\n(index, count) shard; the inner script walks every case and asserts only\nthe indices congruent to its shard. 629s to 217s with six workers.\n\nCoverage is preserved by construction and checked, not assumed: the set\nof case names that pass is byte-identical between a one-worker and a\nsix-worker run, and both report zero failures. The pass *count* differs\nbecause the scan-fixture assertions are not shard-gated and therefore\nrun on every worker — redundant, not missing.\n\nAnd the suite still does its job: removing the docs-orphan check from\nreview.sh makes the sharded run exit 1 and name\n\"Check 7 — docs orphan detection\" as the failure.\n\nThe source digest is still proven once around the whole fan-out, so a\nworker that wrote outside its own copy trips the same 74.\n\nConstraint: mutation isolation depends entirely on each worker owning a copy; sharding without per-worker copies would corrupt the suite.\nRejected: gating the scan-fixture assertions too — they read SCAN_OUT set by a preceding run_scan, so gating them individually would assert against another shard''s output. Duplicating eight cheap scan runs is the safe trade.\nConfidence: medium\nScope-risk: six concurrent copytrees of the repo plus six review.sh walks; on a small runner this is heavier in peak memory and disk than before. E2E_PARITY_WORKERS=1 restores the old behavior exactly, and 0 derives the count from the core count.\nNot-tested: Linux and single-core runners; the wall-clock gain and the peak resource cost were both measured only on a 10-core macOS machine.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"41faf82b483b5b1826d5c314ff194f34fab7a5d8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/41faf82b483b5b1826d5c314ff194f34fab7a5d8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/fe9973c0712cba14cb806a404b26845e3c639092","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/fe9973c0712cba14cb806a404b26845e3c639092","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGZlOTk3M2MwNzEyY2JhMTRjYjgwNmE0MDRiMjY4NDVlM2M2MzkwOTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f4c0d5c52f4dd7a8f65afff787c0ac8429d687ac","sha":"f4c0d5c52f4dd7a8f65afff787c0ac8429d687ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f4c0d5c52f4dd7a8f65afff787c0ac8429d687ac"}],"sha":"fe9973c0712cba14cb806a404b26845e3c639092","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/fe9973c0712cba14cb806a404b26845e3c639092"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f4c0d5c52f4dd7a8f65afff787c0ac8429d687ac/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T11:12:24Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T11:12:24Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Memoize oracle text normalization\n\nvalidate_skill_dir re-normalized the same file content once per label,\nso normalize_oracle_text — a pure str->str function — accounted for\nroughly 5s of the 7.9s each holdout invocation spent in CPU, through\n29,000 regex substitutions over content that had not changed.\n\ntest-reviewer-holdout.sh invokes the runner 29 times: 213s to 99s\nmeasured. test-reviewer-holdout-v3.py calls validate_skill_dir directly\nand gets the same benefit, and so does every real live holdout run.\n\nThe output is a deterministic function of the input, so caching cannot\nchange a leak verdict. Checked rather than assumed: 4,000 random strings\ndrawn from an alphabet including whitespace, path separators, hashes and\nnon-ASCII compared against the uncached function through __wrapped__ —\nzero mismatches.\n\nConstraint: only safe because the function is pure; nothing else in the leak path was cached.\nRejected: hoisting the per-label recomputation out of the loop instead — a larger edit to the leak-detection control flow for a similar gain, where the cache leaves that logic untouched.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: maxsize 4096 bounds memory; a corpus larger than that degrades to the old cost rather than misbehaving.\nNot-tested: the remaining per-label disclosure_text recomputation, which the profile says is the next ~0.8s per call; left alone as a separate change.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8f04313ade1cbe25c7bdd3e67fb7b999f3183233","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/8f04313ade1cbe25c7bdd3e67fb7b999f3183233"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/f4c0d5c52f4dd7a8f65afff787c0ac8429d687ac","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f4c0d5c52f4dd7a8f65afff787c0ac8429d687ac","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGY0YzBkNWM1MmY0ZGQ3YThmNjVhZmZmNzg3YzBhYzg0MjlkNjg3YWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/717464510fff3d6b71b5b5e221c5312021ac14f7","sha":"717464510fff3d6b71b5b5e221c5312021ac14f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/717464510fff3d6b71b5b5e221c5312021ac14f7"}],"sha":"f4c0d5c52f4dd7a8f65afff787c0ac8429d687ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f4c0d5c52f4dd7a8f65afff787c0ac8429d687ac"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/717464510fff3d6b71b5b5e221c5312021ac14f7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T11:05:29Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T11:05:29Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Stop forking a grep per discovered file\n\nenumerate-shell-files.sh checked each candidate path for control\ncharacters with `printf | grep`. That is two forks per file, and the walk\nis deliberately unfiltered, so with the opt-in evals fixtures installed\nit covers ~4600 paths — 4151 of them inside\nscripts/evals/fixtures/node_modules. Measured 15.3s per call.\n\nA bash-native `[[ =~ [[:cntrl:]] ]]` gives the identical verdict in\n0.99s. Verified on bash 3.2 against tab, bell, and clean names, and the\nenumerated set is byte-identical: same 38 files. Control-character\nrejection still fires — checked with a real bell-containing filename.\n\nThe enumerator runs twice per gate (the shell-syntax stage, and again\ninside pre-push-security.sh via review.sh), so this is ~30s off\nci-local.sh and ~15s off the standalone pre-push gate.\n\nConstraint: the walk stays unfiltered. Pruning node_modules would have been faster still, but it changes which files are examined, and the point of the stage is that nothing escapes it.\nRejected: excluding scripts/evals/fixtures — a coverage change dressed up as a speedup.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none — same discovered set, same rejection behavior, verified by diff and by test-shell-enumeration.py.\nNot-tested: bash 5.x and Linux runners; the construct is POSIX-class matching inside [[ ]], supported since bash 3.0.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0ec4f9acc721db4b1bf94ec3d9734c2b8b96a885","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/0ec4f9acc721db4b1bf94ec3d9734c2b8b96a885"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/717464510fff3d6b71b5b5e221c5312021ac14f7","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/717464510fff3d6b71b5b5e221c5312021ac14f7","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDcxNzQ2NDUxMGZmZjNkNmI3MWI1YjVlMjIxYzUzMTIwMjFhYzE0Zjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/1e3ebdb0d2c0a017edb2a0316f8aff7258f86a0b","sha":"1e3ebdb0d2c0a017edb2a0316f8aff7258f86a0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/1e3ebdb0d2c0a017edb2a0316f8aff7258f86a0b"}],"sha":"717464510fff3d6b71b5b5e221c5312021ac14f7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/717464510fff3d6b71b5b5e221c5312021ac14f7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/1e3ebdb0d2c0a017edb2a0316f8aff7258f86a0b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T10:07:25Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T10:07:25Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Run the scanner checks concurrently, and report every failure\n\nTiming each ci-local stage showed this one suite was 630s of the 1027s\nthe Python stages take — the next slowest was 71s. The wall clock is\nsubprocess wait: 93 independent checks each build a temporary project\nand shell out to scan.sh.\n\nThey now run in a thread pool. Threads rather than processes because the\nwork releases the GIL inside subprocess.run and the checks stay ordinary\nfunctions needing no pickling. 630s to 239s here.\n\nThe pool also collects failures instead of stopping at the first assert.\nThat is the more valuable half: the sequential version hid four real\nfailures behind an earlier one this week, including an npx guard this\nrepository''s own contract requires. Verified by injecting faults into\ntwo pooled checks and confirming both are named in the output.\n\nassert_representative_suite_completes_within_budget stays sequential and\nlast, because a saturated pool would distort the budget it measures.\n\nConstraint: every pooled check must own its temporary directory and touch no shared path; the 93 here already did, which is why the pool is safe without further isolation.\nRejected: ProcessPoolExecutor — the checks are subprocess-bound, not CPU-bound, and processes would force these closures to become picklable for no gain.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: a future check that writes outside its temp dir would race. The docstring says so.\nNot-tested: behavior on a single-core runner, where max_workers collapses to 1 and the suite runs effectively sequentially.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4461dd98f22527e86b49bc6c0103eb0444e80781","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/4461dd98f22527e86b49bc6c0103eb0444e80781"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/1e3ebdb0d2c0a017edb2a0316f8aff7258f86a0b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/1e3ebdb0d2c0a017edb2a0316f8aff7258f86a0b","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDFlM2ViZGIwZDJjMGEwMTdlZGIyYTAzMTZmOGFmZjcyNThmODZhMGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/e102a26b58177d1f529bc2d75ecd3a74426f1d7f","sha":"e102a26b58177d1f529bc2d75ecd3a74426f1d7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/e102a26b58177d1f529bc2d75ecd3a74426f1d7f"}],"sha":"1e3ebdb0d2c0a017edb2a0316f8aff7258f86a0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/1e3ebdb0d2c0a017edb2a0316f8aff7258f86a0b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/e102a26b58177d1f529bc2d75ecd3a74426f1d7f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T08:37:44Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T08:37:44Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Note that a hallucinated locator lands in #4i too\n\nA generated spec can arrive with an invented data-testid that never\nmatched anything. That is indistinguishable from a selector that rotted,\nand an absence assertion keeps both green forever — so the resolution is\nalready #4i''s.\n\nRecorded as a scope note rather than a new ID. The candidate pattern was\nassessed and rejected: \"hallucinated locator\" adds a causal story, not a\ndetection signal, and #4i deliberately ignores cause, which is why it\nalso catches framework migrations, class renames, and design-system\nswaps. Narrowing it to authorship would make it strictly weaker. The\nloud half — an invented selector in a positive assertion — turns the\ntest red and reaches the debuggers as F2/F12, never the reviewer.\n\nThe note ends by saying so, so the next reader does not re-open the\nquestion.\n\nConstraint: adding a 25th base ID would hard-fail the frozen expected_families assertion in scripts/ci/test-reviewer-holdout-v3.py and require ~21 lock-step files, a new labeled corpus case with a matching false-positive guard, and a three-host live benchmark re-run.\nRejected: a new pattern ID, and a \"closed AI loop\" ID alongside it — the latter has no anchor in the artifacts under review at all, and its only objective detector is a mutation-tool install this skill forbids. Its symptoms are already partitioned across #1, #2, #4a/#4f, #8, #20 and #22, and V2/V3/V6 in the generator prevent it structurally.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none — prose inside an existing sub-block, no ID, severity, count, or manifest surface moves.\nNot-tested: none.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bcaf1293277d1053f6898284112205f9b410f5a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/bcaf1293277d1053f6898284112205f9b410f5a6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/e102a26b58177d1f529bc2d75ecd3a74426f1d7f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/e102a26b58177d1f529bc2d75ecd3a74426f1d7f","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGUxMDJhMjZiNTgxNzdkMWY1MjliYzJkNzVlY2QzYTc0NDI2ZjFkN2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/34bf552400a4a142e184a930fa2999f4c1097c01","sha":"34bf552400a4a142e184a930fa2999f4c1097c01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/34bf552400a4a142e184a930fa2999f4c1097c01"}],"sha":"e102a26b58177d1f529bc2d75ecd3a74426f1d7f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/e102a26b58177d1f529bc2d75ecd3a74426f1d7f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/34bf552400a4a142e184a930fa2999f4c1097c01/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T08:25:34Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T08:25:34Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Define false-green, and separate it from flaky\n\nThe README used the term six times and never said what it meant. A term\nnobody can quote is not a term anyone adopts, and another project is\nalready building a benchmark around the same phrase.\n\nThe definition leads with the distinction that makes it useful: a flaky\ntest fails sometimes, so retry dashboards and flake analytics eventually\nsee it. A false-green test never fails, including when the product is\nbroken, so nothing that watches for tests flipping can surface it. That\nis why post-run analytics are complementary rather than competing, and\nit is the sentence a reader can repeat.\n\nConstraint: the three translations mirror README.md section-for-section and carry its exact byte digest; all four are updated together.\nRejected: a glossary entry in docs/ — the term needs to be defined where it is first used, not one link away.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none; README i18n parity and the independent-review packet both still pass.\nNot-tested: translation quality in ja and zh-cn is not attested, per the existing disclaimer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"083761c4305d0accf8abc01f072babc21415062c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/083761c4305d0accf8abc01f072babc21415062c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/34bf552400a4a142e184a930fa2999f4c1097c01","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/34bf552400a4a142e184a930fa2999f4c1097c01","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKDM0YmY1NTI0MDBhNGExNDJlMTg0YTkzMGZhMjk5OWY0YzEwOTdjMDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/fe63f9ced3054cb8e26c6ea1e668547a8dccc9b8","sha":"fe63f9ced3054cb8e26c6ea1e668547a8dccc9b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/fe63f9ced3054cb8e26c6ea1e668547a8dccc9b8"}],"sha":"34bf552400a4a142e184a930fa2999f4c1097c01","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/34bf552400a4a142e184a930fa2999f4c1097c01"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/fe63f9ced3054cb8e26c6ea1e668547a8dccc9b8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T08:23:36Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T08:23:36Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Give the skills machine-readable classification metadata\n\nEvery skill declared only author and version, so nothing but a\nhand-written listing could tell a registry that e2e-reviewer covers\nPlaywright and Cypress while cypress-debugger covers one of them. That\nis a distribution problem: a directory that cannot categorise a skill\nwill not surface it.\n\nframeworks, testing-types and languages now sit under metadata. The\nAgent Skills specification fixes the set of top-level frontmatter keys —\nanything else is a validation error — and defines metadata as a\nstring-to-string map, so the values are comma-joined rather than YAML\nlists.\n\nframeworks mirrors the scope contract in docs/framework-scope.md rather\nthan advertising reach the skills do not have.\n\nConstraint: spec-fixed top-level keys and string-only metadata values; both rule out the obvious `frameworks: [playwright, cypress]` shape.\nRejected: a separate manifest file — a registry reading SKILL.md would not find it, which defeats the purpose.\nConfidence: medium\nScope-risk: none in this repo — CI validates only that the frontmatter name matches the directory. Whether any registry actually reads these keys is unverified; they are inert if not.\nNot-tested: no registry has been shown to consume these fields; this makes classification possible, it does not prove anyone consumes it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0cef91c6a0e9491fc24cb732b571d146f3675fea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/0cef91c6a0e9491fc24cb732b571d146f3675fea"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/fe63f9ced3054cb8e26c6ea1e668547a8dccc9b8","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/fe63f9ced3054cb8e26c6ea1e668547a8dccc9b8","node_id":"C_kwDORZiZUtoAKGZlNjNmOWNlZDMwNTRjYjhlMjZjNmVhMWU2Njg1NDdhOGRjY2M5Yjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commit/f70a76e54ba7be7fcbd57e651bccd8f57755ad45","sha":"f70a76e54ba7be7fcbd57e651bccd8f57755ad45","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f70a76e54ba7be7fcbd57e651bccd8f57755ad45"}],"sha":"fe63f9ced3054cb8e26c6ea1e668547a8dccc9b8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/fe63f9ced3054cb8e26c6ea1e668547a8dccc9b8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/voidmatcha","id":16266103,"login":"voidmatcha","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MjY2MTAz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/f70a76e54ba7be7fcbd57e651bccd8f57755ad45/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T08:21:20Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T08:21:20Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Make the signal-rollback test independent of how CI was launched\n\ntest_commit_signals_roll_back_and_are_re_raised asserts the installer\ndies from the signal it re-raises. A shell sets SIGINT and SIGQUIT to\nignore for background jobs, and nohup does the same for SIGHUP; children\ninherit that. Run ci-local.sh in the background and the re-raise cannot\nkill anything, so the installer exits 143 and the assertion fails for a\nreason unrelated to the installer.\n\nThe child now resets those dispositions to default before exec. Verified\nboth ways: foreground and background both pass, where before only\nforeground could.\n\nThis was masking a real problem — ci-local.sh takes longer than a\nforeground tool invocation allows here, so every background run of the\nfull gate reported a failure that no code change could fix.\n\nConstraint: preexec_fn runs between fork and exec and is not thread-safe; this script is single-threaded and does nothing else in the child.\nRejected: skipping the case when signals are ignored — that turns a real regression surface into a silent pass, which is the failure mode this repository exists to catch.\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: run_installer is used by every case in this file; resetting to default only restores standard behavior.\nNot-tested: Linux CI runners — verified on macOS bash 3.2 only.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6184682fb030866a42b0612cb0d7807eae8bf4f5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/6184682fb030866a42b0612cb0d7807eae8bf4f5"},"u