n":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/commits/4207c27e3d48630c8647292969c27531031e0e43/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-08T08:19:08Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-08T08:19:08Z","email":"dev.yongjaelee@gmail.com","name":"YONGJAE LEE"},"message":"Name the credential leak in #21\n\n#21 described a committed storageState file only as unreproducible —\nabsent on fresh clones, silently expiring. It is also a credential leak:\nthe file holds live session cookies, and any bearer token the app keeps\nin origin storage, for whatever account captured it. #14 does not reach\nthis; its scope is string literals in test code.\n\nSeverity is unchanged. This is a hygiene finding, not a silent pass.\n\nConfidence: high\nScope-risk: none — prose only, no ID, severity, or title change, so no parity surface moves.\nNot-tested: none.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"61da6c63d9ecdde94e3b97df813f98a7f96ee00d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/trees/61da6c63d9ecdde94e3b97df813f98a7f96ee00d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/voidmatcha/e2e-skills/git/commits/4207c27e3d48630c8647292969c27531031e0e43","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16266103?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voidmatcha/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/voi