url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oriolcanades","id":83498869,"login":"oriolcanades","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDk4ODY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commits/93cfa1d6707847aa41982460ca3d658fc5aeb816/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T09:39:44Z","email":"oriol.canades@altia.es","name":"Oriol Canadés"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T09:39:44Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: publish the ZAP report in the job summary and block on High/Critical (#73)\n\nThe zap-report artifact is a ZIP with 90-day retention, so reading a DAST\nresult meant downloading it first. Dump ZAP''s markdown report into the job\nsummary instead: it renders on the run page, which is what a PR needs. The\nartifact stays as the backup carrying the full HTML.\n\nSplit the severity policy while at it. Low and Informational stay\nnon-failing (fail_action: false) — on a passive baseline they are noise.\nAnything at riskcode >= 3 now exits non-zero, which reddens the run and\nlets GitHub''s failure notification fire. ZAP''s risk scale tops out at 3\n(High), so the comparison also covers a future Critical level.\n\nSame change is going into every EUDIStack repo that runs a DAST baseline.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f7f89937765191e13341838dea9f8efac1ed738b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/git/trees/f7f89937765191e13341838dea9f8efac1ed738b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/git/commits/93cfa1d6707847aa41982460ca3d658fc5aeb816","verification":{"payload":"tree f7f89937765191e13341838dea9f8efac1ed738b\nparent a04fb939bd3fdc461aa726847a8c2771407772be\nauthor Oriol Canadés <oriol.canades@altia.es> 1787823584 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787823584 +0200\n\nci: publish the ZAP report in the job summary and block on High/Critical (#73)\n\nThe zap-report artifact is a ZIP with 90-day retention, so reading a DAST\nresult meant downloading it first. Dump ZAP''s markdown report into the job\nsummary instead: it renders on the run page, which is what a PR needs. The\nartifact stays as the backup carrying the full HTML.\n\nSplit the severity policy while at it. Low and Informational stay\nnon-failing (fail_action: false) — on a passive baseline they are noise.\nAnything at riskcode >= 3 now exits non-zero, which reddens the run and\nlets GitHub''s failure notification fire. ZAP''s risk scale tops out at 3\n(High), so the comparison also covers a future Critical level.\n\nSame change is going into every EUDIStack repo that runs a DAST baseline.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqkAXgCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAB90QAFLkcxCXhoglQUa51s08REbY\nhwlCMNETgL7UMxbjSEaKvlj9p8vO1alMeSzt1bfgYsavc/DRgZ3HcL00/ncpi/sB\nM4W/WdXFTGEt/kGAvXOkfntXS/JjWS+x1r3MZzo8ZBBucYVQiIARBh6mUNOOel7K\nmdWqaIbS7FkDlW12H9SflF5a2UjTNpRF3bo7TOIIzn8BBscShstztkp1cXmep68w\n4UnQm16pOJPAKZ/dgoFG/YHtyRjXQDaVqvHZY6BLwDBngBlR6QxQ4om8L1281jWa\nOQZqCBO1Ams4HsqzqI5EmZb9F+GKWYdtIyHuOSFB7ogcmY1vFGMpDjxcCD1bfvm2\nxkl6vgCvLx+pq6kNl6BpxVtP13foKSzyrnoRyodqCCuuJzfnuIsAY9SbIlWJc/wL\nZejgF8LLk66r/aDKqaecKPzN9seG7kP5DfFm1kfj7JgSAExB+SL/G96oypZjAUcE\nmwEDMxxrDx2w+yOjQljrpns0ATDn5vl47TjTNeTYFJJ2SCL7n3p+pZZOa426olA5\nNUsHe5pljLDhlYz56QaBSqa6s+BbvYA92GgImwMfv74xx9nI7UyvoJwULlCOg3cc\nfnBCkAadsLOAmODurHVgoCf2/sVxH9A0JL7lKMb41dRVXYlvNMXAx82/SMJcgfgX\nH/EfTMNqGQHqqT0fSotW\n=Nw7n\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-27T09:39:45Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commit/93cfa1d6707847aa41982460ca3d658fc5aeb816","node_id":"C_kwDORZ98G9oAKDkzY2ZhMWQ2NzA3ODQ3YWE0MTk4MjQ2MGNhM2Q2NThmYzVhZWI4MTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commit/a04fb939bd3fdc461aa726847a8c2771407772be","sha":"a04fb939bd3fdc461aa726847a8c2771407772be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commits/a04fb939bd3fdc461aa726847a8c2771407772be"}],"sha":"93cfa1d6707847aa41982460ca3d658fc5aeb816","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commits/93cfa1d6707847aa41982460ca3d658fc5aeb816"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83498869?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oriolcanades","id":83498869,"login":"oriolcanades","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDk4ODY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commits/a04fb939bd3fdc461aa726847a8c2771407772be/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T15:46:04Z","email":"oriol.canades@altia.es","name":"Oriol Canadés"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T15:46:04Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: add ZAP DAST baseline scan to PR pipeline (#71)\n\n* ci: add ZAP DAST baseline scan to PR pipeline\n\nAngular SPA — scans the built static bundle served locally in the runner,\nwith Ajax Spider enabled (ZAP''s default spider only sees index.html on\nclient-side-routed apps). Rules vendored from eudistack-platform-dev''s\ndev-tools/testing/baseline/zap/zap-baseline.conf (single source of truth\nper conv-infrastructure-testing.md §5.3/§6.3 Gate G2). Non-blocking —\nfindings surface only via the uploaded HTML artifact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: use action-baseline''s artifact_name, fix rules-file comment path\n\n- Use action-baseline''s artifact_name input instead of a separate manual\n  upload-artifact step (avoids producing two report artifacts for the\n  same scan — same class of issue Copilot flagged on eudistack-core-issuer).\n- Fix a stale path in the rules-file comment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Oriol Canadés <83498869+oriolcanadesin2@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"000e1a6a2bc990ad84e40741a3bf0c764ed04291","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/git/trees/000e1a6a2bc990ad84e40741a3bf0c764ed04291"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/git/commits/a04fb939bd3fdc461aa726847a8c2771407772be","verification":{"payload":"tree 000e1a6a2bc990ad84e40741a3bf0c764ed04291\nparent 7d254f3e3e3cc847c3a76d52bd0ed61b2a203b74\nauthor Oriol Canadés <oriol.canades@altia.es> 1787327164 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787327164 +0200\n\nci: add ZAP DAST baseline scan to PR pipeline (#71)\n\n* ci: add ZAP DAST baseline scan to PR pipeline\n\nAngular SPA — scans the built static bundle served locally in the runner,\nwith Ajax Spider enabled (ZAP''s default spider only sees index.html on\nclient-side-routed apps). Rules vendored from eudistack-platform-dev''s\ndev-tools/testing/baseline/zap/zap-baseline.conf (single source of truth\nper conv-infrastructure-testing.md §5.3/§6.3 Gate G2). Non-blocking —\nfindings surface only via the uploaded HTML artifact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: use action-baseline''s artifact_name, fix rules-file comment path\n\n- Use action-baseline''s artifact_name input instead of a separate manual\n  upload-artifact step (avoids producing two report artifacts for the\n  same scan — same class of issue Copilot flagged on eudistack-core-issuer).\n- Fix a stale path in the rules-file comment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Oriol Canadés <83498869+oriolcanadesin2@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet