:"C_kwDORZ98G9oAKGEwNGZiOTM5YmQzZmRjNDYxYWE3MjY4NDdhOGMyNzcxNDA3NzcyYmU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commit/7d254f3e3e3cc847c3a76d52bd0ed61b2a203b74","sha":"7d254f3e3e3cc847c3a76d52bd0ed61b2a203b74","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commits/7d254f3e3e3cc847c3a76d52bd0ed61b2a203b74"}],"sha":"a04fb939bd3fdc461aa726847a8c2771407772be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commits/a04fb939bd3fdc461aa726847a8c2771407772be"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/83498869?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/oriolcanades","id":83498869,"login":"oriolcanades","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgzNDk4ODY5","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/oriolcanades","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commits/7d254f3e3e3cc847c3a76d52bd0ed61b2a203b74/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-21T12:46:50Z","email":"oriol.canades@altia.es","name":"Oriol Canadés"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-21T12:46:50Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"ci: add software composition analysis (Trivy + CycloneDX SBOM) (#69)\n\nCloses the SCA gap for the release gate required by Annex 2.1 of the PRH\nLPID tender. The Java backends already ran Trivy; this brings the npm side\nup to the same convention.\n\n- pr.yml: Trivy fs scan of the repo root (reads package-lock.json),\n  HIGH,CRITICAL severity, vulnerability DB cache, JSON report artefact and\n  config/trivy/.trivyignore for documented accepted risks. Trivy''s npm\n  parser omits dev dependencies by default, so the scan reflects what\n  actually ships to the browser rather than the build tooling.\n- exit-code is 0 ON PURPOSE: this lands as a baseline, not yet a gate. The\n  production dependency tree carries HIGH advisories on Angular <= 19.2.25\n  (XSS in core/compiler, DoS via OOM and HttpTransferCache cross-request\n  data leakage in common) and 19.2.25 is the last 19.x release, so no fix\n  exists inside the 19.x line. Flip exit-code to 1 once the Angular major\n  upgrade lands or the accepted risks are listed in .trivyignore.\n- ci-cd.yml: CycloneDX SBOM (@cyclonedx/cyclonedx-npm 6.0.1, spec 1.6,\n  production dependencies only), uploaded as a 90-day artefact and attached\n  to the GitHub Release as sbom.cdx.json.\n\n- config/trivy/** added to the ci-cd.yml paths-ignore: changing the Trivy\n  allow-list is a policy change, never a deployment.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a5be8e8a7cfc289f71bdd45249ccc5d7fcf31a12","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/git/trees/a5be8e8a7cfc289f71bdd45249ccc5d7fcf31a12"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/git/commits/7d254f3e3e3cc847c3a76d52bd0ed61b2a203b74","verification":{"payload":"tree a5be8e8a7cfc289f71bdd45249ccc5d7fcf31a12\nparent 8cf2bf5c669882232cdafc96a81c8d900f4340c6\nauthor Oriol Canadés <oriol.canades@altia.es> 1787316410 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1787316410 +0200\n\nci: add software composition analysis (Trivy + CycloneDX SBOM) (#69)\n\nCloses the SCA gap for the release gate required by Annex 2.1 of the PRH\nLPID tender. The Java backends already ran Trivy; this brings the npm side\nup to the same convention.\n\n- pr.yml: Trivy fs scan of the repo root (reads package-lock.json),\n  HIGH,CRITICAL severity, vulnerability DB cache, JSON report artefact and\n  config/trivy/.trivyignore for documented accepted risks. Trivy''s npm\n  parser omits dev dependencies by default, so the scan reflects what\n  actually ships to the browser rather than the build tooling.\n- exit-code is 0 ON PURPOSE: this lands as a baseline, not yet a gate. The\n  production dependency tree carries HIGH advisories on Angular <= 19.2.25\n  (XSS in core/compiler, DoS via OOM and HttpTransferCache cross-request\n  data leakage in common) and 19.2.25 is the last 19.x release, so no fix\n  exists inside the 19.x line. Flip exit-code to 1 once the Angular major\n  upgrade lands or the accepted risks are listed in .trivyignore.\n- ci-cd.yml: CycloneDX SBOM (@cyclonedx/cyclonedx-npm 6.0.1, spec 1.6,\n  production dependencies only), uploaded as a 90-day artefact and attached\n  to the GitHub Release as sbom.cdx.json.\n\n- config/trivy/** added to the ci-cd.yml paths-ignore: changing the Trivy\n  allow-list is a policy change, never a deployment.\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqiEi6CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuE0QAKQz2yC9299fwpKmQjPbPk6r\nRoktAqfjrlJdPVDfTVO2+0LlIzleDikcfi9Bo3DPdpfV7oufrt+k94fWURLBmtP+\nqHCByECOD3rZppTqVFpSKjY60ofH5LNlPLK0p8NmiDGfJB+/fCqBORh0DE9nPNUH\nU4WFZrsorWGkJLQ/aRRaOthFzQ1BMb8qFOH+DXy1Z8QWAllljL44uwwS9jmgyJtg\nZhiDL/a1bodIIFONk2+HRSIuEeN3NIH+FqgfwuAnnU6d3gjLpf3WPJrziXU6vS3u\n1nJnKk7sUc68HX920tUhJbiGjJGhJcxGSuMxU1+d4Vplp6H/vIZpeY6h9lENztse\n/swSnhwCfZVPY9PWOHlecCDzIu8GSc+uN6JrIq2kjOYQTEA3WgNoBtc9N8kiVKCY\nikAn6aHm+Wa2z1yYZagBQAtqwS6otkuzOQz+zNIKScSH6cJSR/2be3X/3AiidwXM\nWho+u9uU3VJBNZwOfxrR4JZfP5lKrPSLmo1eEwVWsh3wNTSXjXW1sKCWstLlDtUj\nTwWyW3xqVqXgWIZEIpW4LKs