ml_url":"https://github.com/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commit/91395898471f7474e71aa8e8d794910cca315b55","node_id":"C_kwDORZ98G9oAKDkxMzk1ODk4NDcxZjc0NzRlNzFhYThlOGQ3OTQ5MTBjY2EzMTViNTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commit/42dd632b079f394de8d7ce335dd21705290fb2d4","sha":"42dd632b079f394de8d7ce335dd21705290fb2d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commits/42dd632b079f394de8d7ce335dd21705290fb2d4"}],"sha":"91395898471f7474e71aa8e8d794910cca315b55","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commits/91395898471f7474e71aa8e8d794910cca315b55"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commits/42dd632b079f394de8d7ce335dd21705290fb2d4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-15T07:48:47Z","email":"alba.lopez@in2.es","name":"AlbaLopez552"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-15T07:48:47Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(login): embedded header for tenant-provided nav (EUDISTACK-605 US-002) (#56)\n\n* feat(login): add DOMPurify allow-list constants and install dompurify\n\nCreate embed-sanitizer.constants.ts materialising 1:1 the allow-list\nfrom architecture.md §6 (EMBED_ALLOWED_TAGS, EMBED_ALLOWED_ATTR,\nEMBED_ALLOWED_URI_REGEXP). Shared source of truth for header (US-002)\nand footer (US-003) embed sanitization.\n\nInstall dompurify + @types/dompurify as runtime/dev dependencies.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-605\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(login): add sanitizeEmbedHtml to ThemeService (EUDISTACK-605)\n\nInject DomSanitizer and add sanitizeEmbedHtml(raw) method applying\nDOMPurify with the canonical allow-list (EMBED_ALLOWED_TAGS/ATTR/URI),\nnull-guarding falsy inputs and empty-after-sanitize results (AD-1, AD-2).\nbypassSecurityTrustHtml is called only on the DOMPurify-cleaned string.\n\nFix pre-existing Theme fixture gaps in login and error component specs\n(knowledgeBaseUrl/tenantDomain fields missing after US-001 model update).\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-605\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(login): render tenant embedded header conditionally (EUDISTACK-605)\n\nAdd headerHtml: SafeHtml | null to LoginComponent, derived from\nThemeService.sanitizeEmbedHtml on each theme emission. Template renders\n<div *ngIf=\"headerHtml\" class=\"embedded-header\" [innerHTML]=\"headerHtml\">\nabove the branding header — *ngIf removes the node entirely when null\nso no space is reserved when the header is absent (FR-04 / AC-02 / AD-2).\n\nSCSS .embedded-header: width 100%, overflow hidden, no fixed height.\n\nAdd sanitizeEmbedHtml stub to LoginComponent spec ThemeService mock.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-605\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(theme): unit tests for sanitizeEmbedHtml — allow-list + XSS vectors (EUDISTACK-605)\n\nAdd sanitizeEmbedHtml describe block (13 tests) to ThemeService spec:\nEC-04 null/undefined/empty → null, AC-01/AC-03 valid HTML preserved,\nEC-01/EC-02/EC-03 mixed-content and deep-nesting cases,\nES-01 <script>, ES-02 javascript: href, ES-03 on* handler, ES-04 <style>.\nAll 40 ThemeService tests pass.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-605\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(login): unit tests for embedded header conditional render (EUDISTACK-605)\n\nAdd ''embedded header conditional render'' describe block to LoginComponent spec:\nAC-01 verifies .embedded-header is present in DOM when sanitizeEmbedHtml returns\na SafeHtml value; AC-02/EC-04 verifies the DOM node is fully absent when null.\nUses real DomSanitizer via TestBed.inject to produce a valid SafeHtml fixture.\nAlso adds DomSanitizer/SafeHtml to spec imports. All 123 tests pass.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-605\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(login): update CHANGELOG.md for EUDISTACK-605 (US-002 embedded header)\n\nAdd [Unreleased] entries: tenant embedded header, DOMPurify sanitization\nwith allow-list, empty-after-sanitize guard, and shared allow-list constants.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-605\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(login): sanitize-then-interpolate, double-logo guard and allow-list refinements (EUDISTACK-605)\n\n- EMBED_ALLOWED_URI_REGEXP extended to allow {placeholder} URIs so DOMPurify\n  does not strip src=\"{logoUrl}\" before interpolation\n- style attr added to EMBED_ALLOWED_ATTR (needed for inline-styled embed HTML)\n- sanitizeEmbedHtml: DOMPurify runs first, {logoUrl}/{logoDarkUrl} resolved after\n- ThemeModel: logoDarkUrl optional field added to branding interface\n- rewriteAssetPaths: rewrites logoDarkUrl alongside logoUrl and faviconUrl\n- login template: branding header hidden when embedded header is present\n- unit tests: conditional render (AC-02) + SVG sanitization (SVG-01/02)\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-605\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"89ba57b7c795f34db1709219c766693e5d9b4e2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/git/trees/89ba57b7c795f34db1709219c766693e5d9b4e2d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/git/commits/42dd632b079f394de8d7ce335dd21705290fb2d4","verification":{"payload":"tree 89ba57b7c795f34db1709219c766693e5d9b4e2d\nparent 1f1fe4b44e4c41e39df9526d2037b07003e0644b\nauthor AlbaLopez552 <alba.lopez@in2.es> 1781509727 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781509727 +0200\n\nfeat(login): embedded header for tenant-provided nav (EUDISTACK-605 US-002) (#56)\n\n* feat(login): add DOMPurify allow-list constants and install dompurify\n\nCreate embed-sanitizer.constants.ts materialising 1:1 the allow-list\nfrom architecture.md §6 (EMBED_ALLOWED_TAGS, EMBED_ALLOWED_ATTR,\nEMBED_ALLOWED_URI_REGEXP). Shared source of truth for header (US-002)\nand footer (US-003) embed sanitization.\n\nInstall dompurify + @types/dompurify as runtime/dev dependencies.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-605\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(login): add sanitizeEmbedHtml to ThemeService (EUDISTACK-605)\n\nInject DomSanitizer and add sanitizeEmbedHtml(raw) method applying\nDOMPurify with the canonical allow-list (EMBED_ALLOWED_TAGS/ATTR/URI),\nnull-guarding falsy inputs and empty-after-sanitize results (AD-1, AD-2).\nbypassSecurityTrustHtml is called only on the DOMPurify-cleaned string.\n\nFix pre-existing Theme fixture gaps in login and error component specs\n(knowledgeBaseUrl/tenantDomain fields missing after US-001 model update).\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-605\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(login): render tenant embedded header conditionally (EUDISTACK-605)\n\nAdd headerHtml: SafeHtml | null to LoginComponent, derived from\nThemeService.sanitizeEmbedHtml on each theme emission. Template renders\n<div *ngIf=\"headerHtml\" class=\"embedded-header\" [innerHTML]=\"headerHtml\">\nabove the branding header — *ngIf removes the node entirely when null\nso no space is reserved when the header is absent (FR-04 / AC-02 / AD-2).\n\nSCSS .embedded-header: width 100%, overflow hidden, no fixed height.\n\nAdd sanitizeEmbedHtml stub to LoginComponent spec ThemeService mock.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-605\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(theme): unit tests for sanitizeEmbedHtml — allow-list + XSS vectors (EUDISTACK-605)\n\nAdd sanitizeEmbedHtml describe block (13 tests) to ThemeService spec:\nEC-04 null/undefined/empty → null, AC-01/AC-03 valid HTML preserved,\nEC-01/EC-02/EC-03 mixed-content and deep-nesting cases,\nES-01 <script>, ES-02 javascript: href, ES-03 on* handler, ES-04 <style>.\nAll 40 ThemeService tests pass.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-605\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(login): unit tests for embedded header conditional render (EUDISTACK-605)\n\nAdd ''embedded header conditional render'' describe block to LoginComponent spec:\nAC-01 verifies .embedded-header is present in DOM when sanitizeEmbedHtml returns\na SafeHtml value; AC-02/EC-04 verifies the DOM node is fully absent when null.\nUses real DomSanitizer via TestBed.inject to produce a valid SafeHtml fixture.\nAlso adds DomSanitizer/SafeHtml to spec imports. All 123 tests pass.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-605\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(login): update CHANGELOG.md for EUDISTACK-605 (US-002 embedded header)\n\nAdd [Unreleased] entries: tenant embedded header, DOMPurify sanitization\nwith allow-list, empty-after-sanitize guard, and shared allow-list constants.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-605\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(login): sanitize-then-interpolate, double-logo guard and allow-list refinements (EUDISTACK-605)\n\n- EMBED_ALLOWED_URI_REGEXP extended to allow {placeholder} URIs so DOMPurify\n  does not strip src=\"{logoUrl}\" before interpolation\n- style attr added to EMBED_ALLOWED_ATTR (needed for inline-styled embed HTML)\n- sanitizeEmbedHtml: DOMPurify runs first, {logoUrl}/{logoDarkUrl} resolved after\n- ThemeModel: logoDarkUrl optional field added to branding interface\n- rewriteAssetPaths: rewrites logoDarkUrl alongside logoUrl and faviconUrl\n- login template: branding header hidden when embedded header is present\n- unit tests: conditional render (AC-02) + SVG sanitization (SVG-01/02)\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-605\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqL65fCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOkIQAGM6urV4WTttohyey9euURls\nD3MOz7mwS2CyGokeO22KD6U+Ng+TpQiWQzwVzSWjEGPEkY5JFJsMw9VIiqCGYfVc\nXSH4Ssnx55gVHjvUqJzQlADoJCqYHnPVf2DaO0QrFVCiauoc8D0MOFWAwVwSG738\ncBQ41/vQN/0ETfr2D9XdzFr2jmpCnBlEH/MIOPis+6B8yC0/EX6XLjGTEtXJUQtJ\n4GbvB