644b"}],"sha":"42dd632b079f394de8d7ce335dd21705290fb2d4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commits/42dd632b079f394de8d7ce335dd21705290fb2d4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/commits/1f1fe4b44e4c41e39df9526d2037b07003e0644b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-06-12T08:08:30Z","email":"alba.lopez@in2.es","name":"AlbaLopez552"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-06-12T08:08:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(EUDISTACK-604): per-tenant theme.json load with asset path rewriting (#54)\n\n* feat(tenant): add resolveTenant constants ported from Wallet PWA\n\nPort KNOWN_TENANTS, FALLBACK_TENANT, stripEnvSuffix, resolveTenant from\neudistack-core-wallet-pwa. FALLBACK_TENANT=''eudistack'' (sandbox->eudistack\nalias handled at nginx/CloudFront level). Add ^[a-z0-9-]+ validation guard\nbefore asset URL composition to prevent path traversal (ES-05).\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(tenant): unit tests for resolveTenant — happy path, EC-01, EC-03, ES-05\n\n13 tests passing. localhost→''localhost'' per source behavior (ThemeService\nprovides EC-03 end-to-end via HTTP fallback). ES-05 path-traversal guard\ntested with ../etc and null-byte inputs.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(theme): extend Theme contract with headerEmbedCode and footerEmbedCode\n\nAdd optional string|null fields to ThemeContent for US-002/003 embed slots.\nMark onboardingUrl @deprecated — kept for backward-compat (ADR-arch-005).\nNo runtime change; deserialization is already defensive via optional chaining.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(theme): resolve tenant from hostname and load per-tenant theme.json\n\nThemeService.load() now resolves tenant via resolveTenant(window.location.hostname),\nfetches /assets/tenants/{tenant}/theme.json with 800ms timeout. Any error\n(404, 5xx, timeout, parse failure) falls through to applyDefault() — load()\nalways resolves (no throw). APP_INITIALIZER contract preserved.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(theme): implement applyDefault() with built-in EUDIStack fallback theme\n\napplyDefault() synchronously applies the EUDIStack default branding via the\nsame applyTheme() codepath as the happy path. Satisfies AC-02 (fallback <=1s,\nno visible error) and AC-04 (backward-compat: fields without embed codes load OK).\nFix test expectation: load() now resolves on HTTP failure (no throw).\nAlso fix URL mismatch in all spec expectations introduced by Task 4\n(assets/theme.json -> /assets/tenants/localhost/theme.json) and add missing\nknowledgeBaseUrl to mockTheme fixture.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(assets): align theme.json fallback fixture with extended Theme schema\n\nAdd headerEmbedCode: null and footerEmbedCode: null to content block.\nKeeps DEFAULT_THEME constant in sync with the JSON fixture (ADR-arch-005).\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(theme): extend ThemeService spec — AC-01, AC-02, EC-04, ES-01..05\n\nAdd per-tenant load, 404/5xx/timeout/bad-response fallback tests (AC-01, AC-02,\nES-01..04), backward-compat without embed codes (AC-04/EC-04), and invalid-tenant\npath-traversal guard (ES-05). Fix pre-existing tsc error on onLangChange mock.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(bootstrap): APP_INITIALIZER resolves on theme.json 404/500 and per-tenant URL\n\nIntegration test: ThemeService.load() always settles (no bootstrap freeze) even\nwhen theme.json is unavailable. Covers the same codepath as APP_INITIALIZER.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(changelog): add EUDISTACK-604 entries under [Unreleased]\n\nPer-tenant theme resolution, deterministic fallback, extended Theme\ncontract (headerEmbedCode/footerEmbedCode), path-traversal guard.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: bump version to 3.3.0\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(theme): move applyDefault() to private methods block\n\nResolves W1 member-ordering ESLint warning. Method was placed between\npublic methods; moved to the private section before applyTheme(), which\nit calls, grouping all private methods together.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(theme): manage onLangChange subscription + add ES-02b test\n\nW1: store onLangChange subscription in a private field and unsubscribe\nbefore re-subscribing. Prevents accumulation if load() is called more\nthan once (HMR / test isolation). Avoids takeUntilDestroyed which\nrequires rxjs-interop and breaks mock-based tests.\n\nW2: add AC-02/ES-02b test covering 200 OK + malformed JSON body — the\nAC literal for ES-02. HTTP 400 test (existing) covers the same catch\npath; this test exercises the SyntaxError/HttpResponseParseError route.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(theme): rewrite /assets/tenant/ paths to /assets/tenants/{tenant}/ after load\n\nPorts rewriteAssetPaths() from the Wallet PWA ThemeService to the Login MFE.\nTenant theme.json files reference logos as /assets/tenant/logo.png (nginx\nresolves $tenant server-side), but the Login MFE was using the URL directly\nwithout normalisation — causing broken logos on non-sandbox tenants in STG.\n\nAfter a successful theme fetch the method rewrites:\n  /assets/tenant/logo.png → /assets/tenants/{tenant}/logo.png\nPaths already in /assets/tenants/* format are left untouched.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* revert(version): restore 3.2.5 — version bump deferred to squash-merge\n\nCHANGELOG stays [Unreleased] until PR is merged; version bump happens\nat merge time, not on the feature branch.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"8dc2459574271b52da341e47e8a7d2f4a73d81d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/git/trees/8dc2459574271b52da341e47e8a7d2f4a73d81d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/in2workspace/eudistack-mfe-login/git/commits/1f1fe4b44e4c41e39df9526d2037b07003e0644b","verification":{"payload":"tree 8dc2459574271b52da341e47e8a7d2f4a73d81d9\nparent 57ac7dbeb516a3ccb65f73d35ee3e608217148bc\nauthor AlbaLopez552 <alba.lopez@in2.es> 1781251710 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1781251710 +0200\n\nfeat(EUDISTACK-604): per-tenant theme.json load with asset path rewriting (#54)\n\n* feat(tenant): add resolveTenant constants ported from Wallet PWA\n\nPort KNOWN_TENANTS, FALLBACK_TENANT, stripEnvSuffix, resolveTenant from\neudistack-core-wallet-pwa. FALLBACK_TENANT=''eudistack'' (sandbox->eudistack\nalias handled at nginx/CloudFront level). Add ^[a-z0-9-]+ validation guard\nbefore asset URL composition to prevent path traversal (ES-05).\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(tenant): unit tests for resolveTenant — happy path, EC-01, EC-03, ES-05\n\n13 tests passing. localhost→''localhost'' per source behavior (ThemeService\nprovides EC-03 end-to-end via HTTP fallback). ES-05 path-traversal guard\ntested with ../etc and null-byte inputs.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(theme): extend Theme contract with headerEmbedCode and footerEmbedCode\n\nAdd optional string|null fields to ThemeContent for US-002/003 embed slots.\nMark onboardingUrl @deprecated — kept for backward-compat (ADR-arch-005).\nNo runtime change; deserialization is already defensive via optional chaining.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(theme): resolve tenant from hostname and load per-tenant theme.json\n\nThemeService.load() now resolves tenant via resolveTenant(window.location.hostname),\nfetches /assets/tenants/{tenant}/theme.json with 800ms timeout. Any error\n(404, 5xx, timeout, parse failure) falls through to applyDefault() — load()\nalways resolves (no throw). APP_INITIALIZER contract preserved.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat(theme): implement applyDefault() with built-in EUDIStack fallback theme\n\napplyDefault() synchronously applies the EUDIStack default branding via the\nsame applyTheme() codepath as the happy path. Satisfies AC-02 (fallback <=1s,\nno visible error) and AC-04 (backward-compat: fields without embed codes load OK).\nFix test expectation: load() now resolves on HTTP failure (no throw).\nAlso fix URL mismatch in all spec expectations introduced by Task 4\n(assets/theme.json -> /assets/tenants/localhost/theme.json) and add missing\nknowledgeBaseUrl to mockTheme fixture.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(assets): align theme.json fallback fixture with extended Theme schema\n\nAdd headerEmbedCode: null and footerEmbedCode: null to content block.\nKeeps DEFAULT_THEME constant in sync with the JSON fixture (ADR-arch-005).\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(theme): extend ThemeService spec — AC-01, AC-02, EC-04, ES-01..05\n\nAdd per-tenant load, 404/5xx/timeout/bad-response fallback tests (AC-01, AC-02,\nES-01..04), backward-compat without embed codes (AC-04/EC-04), and invalid-tenant\npath-traversal guard (ES-05). Fix pre-existing tsc error on onLangChange mock.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test(bootstrap): APP_INITIALIZER resolves on theme.json 404/500 and per-tenant URL\n\nIntegration test: ThemeService.load() always settles (no bootstrap freeze) even\nwhen theme.json is unavailable. Covers the same codepath as APP_INITIALIZER.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs(changelog): add EUDISTACK-604 entries under [Unreleased]\n\nPer-tenant theme resolution, deterministic fallback, extended Theme\ncontract (headerEmbedCode/footerEmbedCode), path-traversal guard.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* chore: bump version to 3.3.0\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(theme): move applyDefault() to private methods block\n\nResolves W1 member-ordering ESLint warning. Method was placed between\npublic methods; moved to the private section before applyTheme(), which\nit calls, grouping all private methods together.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(theme): manage onLangChange subscription + add ES-02b test\n\nW1: store onLangChange subscription in a private field and unsubscribe\nbefore re-subscribing. Prevents accumulation if load() is called more\nthan once (HMR / test isolation). Avoids takeUntilDestroyed which\nrequires rxjs-interop and breaks mock-based tests.\n\nW2: add AC-02/ES-02b test covering 200 OK + malformed JSON body — the\nAC literal for ES-02. HTTP 400 test (existing) covers the same catch\npath; this test exercises the SyntaxError/HttpResponseParseError route.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(theme): rewrite /assets/tenant/ paths to /assets/tenants/{tenant}/ after load\n\nPorts rewriteAssetPaths() from the Wallet PWA ThemeService to the Login MFE.\nTenant theme.json files reference logos as /assets/tenant/logo.png (nginx\nresolves $tenant server-side), but the Login MFE was using the URL directly\nwithout normalisation — causing broken logos on non-sandbox tenants in STG.\n\nAfter a successful theme fetch the method rewrites:\n  /assets/tenant/logo.png → /assets/tenants/{tenant}/logo.png\nPaths already in /assets/tenants/* format are left untouched.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* revert(version): restore 3.2.5 — version bump deferred to squash-merge\n\nCHANGELOG stays [Unreleased] until PR is merged; version bump happens\nat merge time, not on the feature branch.\n\nStory: EUDISTACK-604\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqK75/CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACdYQAKmmZKlWyWYHLwtA7t8pH2rJ\nDOt5brNr00kgKgIVpGflI9ZqPBn3TSoNQBZklbgz9AfwU1bZc/Xwin0Xlu7cSGrj\nIl+Y6yJkB4QvJ8Trg+yoV2w4/w8reMV8etf+bsmGTmxSMrmE0AH48/FEoUlnLaO9\nf23oqv0VsvFDGbJ0sOk6QMRSNLVlEbBcB2vljuBHypWMMwlgleqO8XYwiy91kW5Z\nUud/LlxiQWzCJN9BylQi8Q8UQH9GfI4ZcFiOXfwy1wAraPwUxZMkcP7ifthB/sq8\nPx+ZUBYlG3gHLqG/f/VTHso/mcNsWCqtuQEc/t95FjgJ6x3L4v1cpyc8Gmj5pWIf\nHrxirwroHLZFE2diSYHJyB/ZD7lZMC+UUIbdBp3I4rvLOdUkfikfr8T6VZn2tW33\nryq/8Nc6rgx3dD3YRJPOKzE7RGgPGjcc6EqyJb2iWbi7TukDTw67OoQ4AYu+mwQ3\nb4Rp+0NgOOoA8t04egjBiiGvGx5eyDFfVYui6inaRFTfYo1ZeC9lICxk/EGxcr5K\nMvNRBlHuzo0sl7uUHKQTK1V8Cl90syJwB9+Zgl3VwDf2wif1+KRf5Fb7jnQDm+dG\nDGV7+YOjV8n+DFxGew6eafnuuIRikQdR2HmExTNSNr4VYF1aA2qwytyyb3diZjTn\nmbIcSmjl5+0mRYCwrsxl\n=xfN8\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-06-12T08:08:31Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url"