api.github.com/users/jk1224-23/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jk1224-23","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jk1224-23/js-reference-architecture/commits/02d184074a9d3a3a1f46f5df3773a0cb94aff083/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-03-02T19:26:46Z","email":"jk1224-23@users.noreply.github.com","name":"jk"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-03-02T19:26:46Z","email":"jk1224-23@users.noreply.github.com","name":"jk"},"message":"Add FedCM and third-party cookie removal doc\n\nNew doc 51-fedcm-and-cookie-removal:\n- Explains third-party cookie removal impact on hidden iframe\n  silent refresh and prompt=none OIDC flows\n- Covers three injection types: direct, indirect (from retrieved\n  web/document content), stored (in database records)\n- Shows which auth flows are affected vs safe:\n  SPA-only silent refresh breaks, SPA+BFF is protected\n- FedCM API implementation with redirect fallback pattern\n- Migration paths: SPA+BFF (recommended), in-memory refresh\n  tokens (degraded), FedCM with fallback, Storage Access API\n- How to verify app safety by testing with 3P cookies blocked\n- Why SPA+BFF HttpOnly session cookie is first-party and safe\n\nNavigation:\n- 03-security: link to doc 51\n- _index.md: doc 51 in security and identity section\n- 35-reference-map: entries for silent refresh failures and\n  third-party cookie removal impact","tree":{"sha":"b983feda27b31e126339d11f6bb59c6e2342d47d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jk1224-23/js-reference-architecture/git/trees/b983feda27b31e126339d11f6bb59c6e2342d47d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/jk1224-23/js-reference-architecture/git/commits/02d184074a9d3a3a1f46f5df3773a0cb94aff083","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260568759?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jk1224-23/events{/privac