"email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"fix(api): preserve lazy export identity and codec compatibility\n\nDiscard stale child-publication cache entries without eager circular imports.\nKeep historical workspace codec definitions and pickle paths while delegating\nto the shared typed codec; resolve shift planning from its genuine leaf.\nInstall the hashed Studio provider and combine subprocess coverage in CI.\nBind the parity tests to the actual temp directory and exact data-file paths.\n\nValidation: 284 original public tests; 654 serialized connected tests;\n56 CI policy tests; initializer 869 statements/152 branches at 100 percent;\ncodec and changed executable statements at 100 percent; strict Python,\nNumPy docs, Ruff, format, actionlint, TS strict and Rust clippy all passed.\nParity: five genuine Python/TypeScript/Rust/WASM corpus consumers passed;\ncanonical bytes and numerical algorithms unchanged.\nBenchmarks: real 10-sample/3-warmup local functional affinity run repeated;\nnon-isolated evidence only, with no performance promotion or rewritten data.\nFrozen public fixture, import budgets and product thresholds unchanged.\n\nSeat: 01a0f27d\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"a17eea3ba339c2b29714d84f4ad7fb2de9f99f58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-quantum-control/git/trees/a17eea3ba339c2b29714d84f4ad7fb2de9f99f58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-quantum-control/git/commits/a74b05ef23cd93a25aa73affd127ab0e8786ee49","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/scpn-quantum-control/commit/a74b05ef23cd93a25aa73affd127ab0e8786ee49","node_id":"C_kwDORazOJtoAKGE3NGIwNWVmMjNjZDkzYTI1YWE3M2FmZmQxMjdhYjBlODc4NmVlNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/anulum/scpn-quantum-control/commit/52e5ea0567c1099a73f0a16c64537fdaf6c82fe5","sha":"52e5ea0567c1099a73f0a16c64537fdaf6c82fe5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-quantum-control/commits/52e5ea0567c1099a73f0a16c64537fdaf6c82fe5"}],"sha":"a74b05ef23cd93a25aa73affd127ab0e8786ee49","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-quantum-control/commits/a74b05ef23cd93a25aa73affd127ab0e8786ee49"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/35185786?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/anulum","id":35185786,"login":"anulum","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM1MTg1Nzg2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-quantum-control/commits/52e5ea0567c1099a73f0a16c64537fdaf6c82fe5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-04T19:20:58Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-04T19:20:58Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"feat(quality): hold shell scripts to the pinned formatter\n\nThe shell gate linted scripts and left their layout unchecked, so the\nsource surface inventory kept the four shell rows open.\n\nPin shfmt-py 4.2.0 beside the linter in the same hash-locked file and let\nthe gate fail on any script the formatter would change. The formatter''s\ndistribution version differs from the version of the binary it carries,\nso the gate checks that the distribution installed beside the running\ninterpreter is the pinned one and uses that binary. Its exit status is\nnon-zero both for an error and for a script that needs formatting; the\ngate tells them apart by the error stream.\n\nThree scripts are reformatted to the repository''s editor configuration:\nthe runner provisioning script, the WSL bootstrap and the notebook push\nscript, which also gains the licence header it lacked. For each, the\nformatter''s minified form of the old and the new text is identical, so\nonly layout changed; the linter still reports nothing. The four shell\nrows of the inventory are closed.\n\nThe gate''s 26 tests run real Git, the real linter and the real formatter\nin temporary repositories and, with the script entry point, cover every\nstatement and branch. Tooling and script layout only; no behaviour change.\n\nSeat: 90ad\n\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"f4bd71c2906d19a71bc46f660c5a71a67ea1f834","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scp