g2","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/anulum","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/anulum/scpn-quantum-control/commits/feff2e7246297c8f4ea0b633e3bbfda27f650fe0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-02T20:21:53Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-02T20:21:53Z","email":"protoscience@anulum.li","name":"Miroslav Šotek"},"message":"test(exports): exercise lazy packages and constrain pickle identity\n\nThe hosted DLA and KYMA gates found unexercised lazy export and inspection\npaths, while serialization rejected two unrestricted pickle calls in the\npublic compatibility test. Use the real package API and a restricted\nunpickler that resolves only exact known public bindings.\n\nKeep the original export snapshot unchanged. Lock the twenty scientific and\ncircuit-compiler additions from completed work explicitly, including their\npositions and original objects; arbitrary additions still fail. Require the\nexplicit export declarations observed in all 48 original packages.\n\nThe 225 DLA, 68 KYMA and 126 public identity cases pass without skips.\nTheir measured owners have 100% line and branch coverage. Strict types,\nNumPy docstrings, lint, format and the actual serialization audit pass.\nUse a hash-locked isolated CPU JAX overlay without altering the shared venv.\nNo full local preflight or suite runs; no timing comparison is claimed.\n\nSeat: 01a0f279\nAuthored by Anulum Fortis & Arcane Sapience (protoscience@anulum.li)","tree":{"sha":"1bd3d4b038eead021c3ba48be3ae4a43df673764","url":"https:/