mail.com","name":"Ifet Great"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-04-14T19:46:46Z","email":"greatifet12@gmail.com","name":"Ifet Great"},"message":"feat(core): implement robust resilience architecture and UI lazy-loading\n\n- **System Stability:** Injected `SQLAlchemyError` try-except wrappers into the Orchestrator''s database commit cycles. The system now safely traps idle SSL connection drops caused by long LLM api waits, autonomously executing `db.rollback()` to fetch fresh connections and prevent server crashes.\n- **AI Fallback Tier Expansion:** Expanded the `UNIFIED_MODEL_POOL` from 18 to a massive 25-model rotation tier. Recalibrated agent offset arrays and raised the global `max_tries` constraint to 25, allowing complete utilization of OpenRouter fallbacks during severe rate-limiting events.\n- **Scraper Anti-Bot Bypass:** Integrated a hard fallback inside the `NewsScraperAgent` to catch `403 Forbidden` errors. The scraper dynamically triggers `curl_cffi` TLS fingerprinting (impersonating `chrome110`) to effortlessly bypass advanced Cloudflare/Imperva firewalls on NCDC and The Guardian portals.\n- **UI Performance & Lazy Loading:** Re-engineered the Command Centre routing to implement True Lazy Loading. Wrapped the heavy Folium map inside a UX toggle switch and heavily utilized Streamlit''s `@st.fragment`. Tab 1 now renders the StAMP intelligence instantaneously without UI thread-locking.\n- **UI Bug Fixes:** Replaced all deprecated `streamlit.components.v1.html` calls with `st.html()` to permanently eliminate component warnings. Silenced `Duplicate Widget ID` Streamlit crashes by injecting strict keys into the Health Map filters.\n- **Documentation:** Updated `presentation_script.md` to reflect the 25-model expansion and added deep technical explanations of Dempster-Shafer, Neonserverless DB pooling, and TLS scraping tactics for the final academic defense.","tree":{"sha":"f32cdfc0050e277e61d2638b680528a4c92fb5a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/